  <Placemark>
    <name>Khorog - Pamir Highway and Wakhan (Tajikistan) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Remote high-altitude mountain-bike expeditions through the Pamirs</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Khorog is the main riding and logistics base for the Pamir Highway, Wakhan Valley and Gorno-Badakhshan. This is expedition terrain rather than a trail centre: long gravel stages cross passes above 4,000 m, with rough descents including Koi-Tezek, Nayzatash and Ak-Baital. Side valleys add unmaintained tracks, river crossings and very isolated mountain riding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Most trips combine pedalling with a 4x4 support vehicle, luggage transport and local guiding. Independent riding is possible for experienced expedition cyclists, but distances, altitude and limited supplies make supported travel strongly advisable.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 July; closed from 01 October (average high-pass riding window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>A GBAO permit is required. Some border areas and Zorkul require additional permission; rules, crossings and road conditions can change at short notice.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Khorog</td><td>Bike / 4x4</td><td>Direct</td></tr><tr><td>Dushanbe</td><td>Flight / long 4x4 transfer</td><td>Variable</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://traveltajikistan.tj/en/sports-tourism/">Travel to Tajikistan sports tourism</a>, the <a href="https://tour.tj/en/catalog/pamir-bike-tour/">Pamir Guides bike-tour itinerary</a> and <a href="https://www.traveltajikistan.net/tours/bike_tours/pamir_highway/itinerary.php">Travel Tajikistan Pamir Highway itinerary</a>. Confirm permits, security advice and current road access before departure.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>71.548922,37.490917,2084</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">khorog-pamir-highway-wakhan</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">expert natural no-lift enduro</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">07-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">10-01</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Menton · Sainte-Agnès · Peille · Sospel [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sainte-Agnes 800 m - pedal-access trail hub above Menton</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A big natural enduro area in the hills behind Menton, spread between Sainte-Agnes, Castillon, the Col de la Madone, Peille, Gorbio and Sospel. Historic mule paths and technical limestone singletrack link into long rides, and the best of them run from the frontier ridge all the way down to the sea, up to about 1100 m of descent in one go. Around 50 traces are drawn here, mostly red and black: rocky, narrow and steep rather than machine-built, with a handful of easier flowing lines lower down.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no trail fee. Climb by road from Menton, Sainte-Agnes, Gorbio, Peille or Sospel; shuttling by car is possible for some lines.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Natural, largely unsigned trails on public land. Several lines are exposed and rocky: scout before committing.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round in a typical year; check weather, wildfire restrictions and local trail access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Menton</td><td>Bike</td><td>~1 h climb</td></tr><tr><td>Nice</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://vttour.fr/sentiers/83">VTTour Ravin du Rank</a>, <a href="https://vttour.fr/sentiers/137">VTTour Sainte-Agnes - Monti</a>, and the linked OpenStreetMap trail geometries. Routes and access can change; verify locally.</i>]]></description>
