  <Placemark>
    <name>St-Cergue: St-Cergue station (NStCM)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Givrine (top of the NStCM train)</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The closest real singletrack riding to Lausanne. Three marked descents drop off the Jura crest back towards Arzier and St-Cergue: Mont Chaubert, Mont Bailly (plus an eastern variant) and La Plagne. Rooty, rocky, north-facing forest trails, short (1-2 km each) but you can chain them and pedal back up in 20-30 min, or reload with the train. Dry quickly, ridable from April to November - the best shoulder-season option on this map.<br/><br/><b>Rain sensitivity</b><br/>Rain-resilient: rocky Jura ground drains quickly despite the shaded forest; heavy same-day rain can still make roots slick.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift needed: the train is the climb (Nyon 400 m > La Givrine 1228 m). Normal CFF/NStCM fare, plus a bike ticket - the national day bike pass is about 14 CHF (bikes are carried on the NStCM, space is limited at peak times).<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h05</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.nstcm.ch/">NStCM railway</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
