  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Pléiades (above Vevey) [train fare only]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Les Pleiades 1350 m - top station of the MVR rack railway, where the descents start</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>No bike park, no shuttle circus - just a 750 m vertical drop of forest tracks and singletrack back down to Blonay, Les Chevalleyres or Lally. Mellow, green, family-friendly gradients with a couple of steeper trail options in the woods above Blonay. Good first outing of the season, and you can extend north towards Les Paccots.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No dedicated bike pass: it is a normal public-transport ticket (Vevey > Les Pleiades is a short-distance fare, roughly 12-14 CHF one way full price) plus a bike ticket, ~14 CHF for the day pass. Cheap day out.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mob.ch/">MOB transport</a>. Pin placed on the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/3161728535">Les Pleiades station</a> (node 3161728535), verified at 1350 m; the valley pin is the MVR <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2827690369">Blonay station</a> at 621 m.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
