  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Chaumont (Neuchâtel) [city fare, ~5 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Coudre 520 m - valley station of the La Coudre funicular</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Chaumont bike park: a proper DH line with 110+ doubles and around 20 drops, clearly aimed at experienced riders - but a chicken line runs alongside the whole way so you can pick your level. Back down to La Coudre it alternates forest doubletrack and singletrack. Open all year, which makes it the winter fallback when the Alps are shut.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The funicular is part of the Neuchatel city network (transN / Onde Verte): a few francs per ride, so this is by far the cheapest lift-served riding in the region. Runs year-round, every 15-30 min.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure (normally open year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + funicular</td><td>~1h10</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.transn.ch/">TransN</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
