  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Leysin: Berneuse gondola top (2048 m)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Berneuse 2048 m - top of the Leysin gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Leysin Bike Park, still young and still growing. Two machine-built runs off the Berneuse: Nerine (1 km, red/black) and Les 3 Tours (0.4 km, red/black), plus a short liaison between them - steep, rocky and aimed at confident riders. A blue intermediate line is due in August 2026 and a green one in 2027. Off-park, the Endless Ride enduro descent towards Prafandaz and Roc de Veyges is the reason to come, and stage 1 of the Alpes du Leman Bike route runs from here to Les Diablerets.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Gondola + downhill day pass around 28 CHF. Free with the Magic Pass. Bike park opens 25 April 2026, daily 20 June - 23 August, weekends either side; the Tete d'Ai chairlift runs 11:30-16:00 in high summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 24 August (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 11:30-16:00<br/><small>Published high-summer Tete d'Ai chairlift hours; other lifts vary.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h10</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.leysin.ch/en/">Leysin tourism</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i><br/><br/>
    <b>Rain sensitivity</b><br/><i>Rain-sensitive: steep, rooty and rocky north-facing terrain turns greasy quickly and stays wet a while after rain.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.002932,46.359507,2032</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
