  <Placemark>
    <name>Crans-Montana - Cry d'Er [35 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Crans 1510 m - valley station of the Cry d'Er gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Three downhill runs covering every level plus a new flowtrail. Flowtrail Arnouva is the beginner line - wide, rolling, a good place to learn to let go of the brakes. Cry d'Er Downhill is the intermediate/technical one: berms, rock features and a proper rhythm section. Beyond the park, Freeride Grand Montana and the Montana-Village > Loc flowtrail give you long natural descents through the larch forest all the way to the valley. The natural side is the bigger half of this spot: a large set of signed enduro lines is drawn here, from the black Col du Schwarzhorn, 5.7 km and 770 m off the 3050 m ridge above the Plaine Morte, and the black Ancienne Bisse du Ro along the gorge, down through reds like Le Tsan (670 m), Super Bella and Creux de la Tieche to short blues around Aminona and the Cry d'Er plateau.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer day pass around 35 CHF; Crans - Cry d'Er return alone is 25 CHF. Bike park runs 13 June - 25 October 2026. The Funitel from Les Violettes up to the Plaine Morte - the one that puts you on the glacier for the Sion epic - carries bikes but runs to a departure interval rather than continuously, reportedly about every 30 minutes, so time your arrival.<br/><small>The 30-minute interval is a rider report, not a published figure; check it with the lift company if the start of your day depends on it.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 26 October (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + funicular</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.crans-montana.ch/en/bike/">Crans-Montana bike</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i><br/><br/>
    <b>Rain sensitivity</b><br/><i>Rain-resilient: sunny, high-altitude larch-forest and open terrain that drains well - only heavy rain on the day itself makes it properly wet.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.467313,46.308583,1509</coordinates></Point>
