  <Placemark>
    <name>Crans-Montana: Plaine Morte Bike</name>
    <description><![CDATA[37.6 km black, 2880 m on the glacier down to 540 m in the Rhone valley, with only about 520 m of climbing - almost all of it a single 440 m pull back to 2390 m in the middle of the route. This demanding alpine route, from the Plaine Morte to the forests of the Pfyn-Finges Nature Park is punctuated by glaciers, high-altitude lakes, waterfalls, and alpine meadows. <i>Source: <a href="https://www.crans-montana.ch/en/mod_oa#ipd=807854622">Crans-Montana - Plaine Morte Bike</a>. Official Outdooractive geometry supplied by Crans-Montana, simplified to 8 m; elevation profile re-measured along the trace.</i>]]></description>
