  <Placemark>
    <name>Anzère - Pas de Maimbré [bikes ride free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Anzere 1550 m - valley station of the Pas-de-Maimbre gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The gravity riding is the red Phoenix Ride, about 380 m of descent from La Dent off the gondola mid-station, and the red Pas de Maimbre, a 3.7 km line straight off the top station for 680 m. Above them Les Andins is the black, 6.9 km and 880 m from the Wildhorn side. Blues Turin and Fun Comes Last, and the long, near-flat Bisse d'Ayent traverses, fill in the rest, alongside five official enduro routes from the easy lift-assisted Gentiane Bike Light to the longer Arnica and Tulipe loops. High, open and dry: a good choice in a wet spell lower down.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Carrying a mountain bike on the gondola is free in summer, which makes this unusually good value; you only pay your own passenger ticket. Anzere is a Magic Pass resort.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.anzere.ch/fr">Anzere tourism</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.394922,46.295157,1548</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">anzere</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="tags">beginner intermediate expert magic-pass natural dh enduro rain-resilient gondola</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="open_from">06-15</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="closed_from">10-19</mwm:value>
      </mwm:properties>
