  <Placemark>
    <name>Verbier - 4 Vallées [47 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Verbier: La Chaux lower station</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Verbier Bike Park by Commencal has long, steep, properly rough World-Cup-adjacent lines off Les Ruinettes and La Chaux, plus a huge natural enduro network reaching down 1500 m to Le Chable. Savoleyres is the quieter side with more natural, flowy trails, and Bruson (across the valley on its own gondola from Le Chable) is quieter still: no built lines at all, just pasture, larch and ridge traverses carrying the long Enduro 14 and 19 routes. Bring a real bike and pads.<br/><br/><p class="warn">The enduro routes are not signposted on the ground. Download the GPS traces before riding.</p>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Verbier bike day pass 47 CHF; the full 4 Vallees bike day pass 57 CHF. Season: Verbier 229 CHF, 4 Vallees 329 CHF. Le Chable > Verbier return is 12.80 CHF and Verbier > Les Ruinettes return 25 CHF if you only want one lap. 10% off online 10+ days ahead. Main summer season 4 July - 21 September 2026.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 4 July; closed from 22 September (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://verbier4vallees.ch/en">Verbier 4 Vallees</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i><br/><br/>
    <b>Rain sensitivity</b><br/><i>Rain-resilient: high-altitude, sunny and largely rocky/well-draining terrain - only heavy rain on the day itself makes it properly wet.</i>]]></description>
