  <Placemark>
    <name>Le Chable-Mayens de Bruson: Mayens de Bruson upper station (1646 m)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mayens de Bruson 1646 m - top of the Le Chable - Bruson gondola</b><br/><br/>
    Bruson is the quiet side of the Val de Bagnes, facing Verbier: natural enduro ground rather than built bike park, and the start of the signed Enduro 14 La Pasay (28.8 km, 1919 m of descent) and the easier Enduro 19 down through the Mayens to Le Chable. The 8-seat gondola from Le Chable carries bikes and runs a much shorter summer than the Verbier lifts opposite - roughly 4 July to 30 August, 08:30-17:00. It also tops out well below Moay, where the long Bruson-side loops and both Tour du Val de Bagnes routes begin; from May to October a bus with a bike trailer runs Le Chable to Moay at 09:50 and 16:30. Covered by the same 47 CHF Verbier bike pass.<br/><br/>
    Verified at 1646 m on <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/255543777">OSM way 255543777</a>. See the main Verbier pin for prices and access.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.196398,46.060392,1646</coordinates></Point>
