  <Placemark>
    <name>Jeizinen / Gampel (Valais) [small cable car]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gampel 635 m - valley station of the Jeizinen cable car</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two marked routes rather than a park, and they see almost no traffic: Jeizibaerg Bike (SchweizMobil 117) and Jeizi Enduro (118), both dropping through the dry south-facing slopes above the Rhone. The Jeizibaerg descent loses roughly 900 m from the Feselalp back to the valley, easy and open at first, then progressively steeper into a mix of flowing and technical singletrack with rock steps. Both are for confident riders - there is no easy alternative line. The pedal-up variant climbs about 800 m past the Traechu Hittu alp restaurant to the Heruhubel before turning down. The Pfyn-Finges nature park right below is worth a detour on the way back.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The small cable car from Gampel at 640 m up to Jeizinen takes 7 to 10 minutes and runs on request, all year. Fares are set by the operator; check before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Runs all year; the trail itself is rideable roughly May to October depending on snow.<br/>Daily opening hours: on request<br/><small>Ring the operator - the cable car does not run to a fixed timetable.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gampel-Steg station</td><td>Walk</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Visp</td><td>Train</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.schweizmobil.ch/de/mountainbikeland/routen/route-0117.html">SchweizMobil route 117 Jeizibaerg Bike</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.739287,46.315529,634</coordinates></Point>
