  <Placemark>
    <name>Arosa (Graubunden) [from 53 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Arosa: village lift hub</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The high, open, quieter half of the Bike Kingdom. The Hoernli Trail is the classic - over 6 km of flowing alpine singletrack from the Hoernligrat back to the village - with the Aelplisee and Schwellisee trails threading past the lakes below the Weisshorn. Less built and more mountain than Lenzerheide; the Arosa Lenzerheide Rundtour ties the two resorts into one big day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Same Bike Kingdom ticket as Lenzerheide, from 53 CHF, and the Urdenbahn links the two sides so you can ride both on one pass. Note the Arosa Card discount is only sold at Arosa counters.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~4h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://arosalenzerheide.swiss/en/Arosa/Summer/Biking">Arosa Lenzerheide</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>9.678332,46.782947,1751</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
