  <Placemark>
    <name>Chur - Brambrueesch [from 53 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Chur 595 m - valley station of the Brambrueesch cable car</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Five freeride runs down the city's own mountain, graded across three levels: blue, red and black, with steep berms, jumps, northshore, drops and long root-and-rock sections. The whole 1000 m from Brambrueesch at 1595 m to the station at 595 m goes in one run, which is unusually big for a park you can reach on foot from a main-line platform.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Chur-Brambrueesch cable car starts in the middle of town, ten minutes' walk from Chur railway station, and carries bikes. Day pass from 53 CHF; it is part of Bike Kingdom, so the same pass also covers Lenzerheide and Arosa.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from mid-May; closed from late October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Chur station</td><td>Walk</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Zurich</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.churbergbahnen.ch/en/summer/mountainbiking">Chur Bergbahnen</a> and <a href="https://www.bikekingdom.ch/en/Bikeparks/Alpenbikepark-Chur">Bike Kingdom</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>9.525755,46.847324,593</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">chur</mwm:value>
