  <Placemark>
    <name>Chamrousse (Belledonne) [23.50 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Chamrousse 1675 m - valley station of the Croix de Chamrousse gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The closest lift-served riding to Grenoble and the cheapest on this map by some margin. Six marked trails and around 20 km of descent off the Croix de Chamrousse: one green, three blue, one red and one black, so it works for a mixed group. Tetras and Transhumance are the long flowing ones, the DH de Chamrousse and Mange tes morts are where it gets serious. Granite, roots and alpenrose, with the whole Vercors laid out across the valley.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Day pass 23.50 EUR adult, 19.50 EUR youth; a 4-hour ticket is 10.50 EUR, and in June and September weekends the day pass is sold at the 4-hour price. Two lifts run: the Croix gondola and the Berangere chairlift. Weekends 5-28 June, then daily 4 July to 30 August 2026.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 4 July; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Grenoble</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://en.chamrousse.com/bike-park.html">Chamrousse</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
