  <Placemark>
    <name>Villard-de-Lans / Correncon (Vercors) [see operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Villard-de-Lans 1155 m - valley station of the Cote 2000 gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 15 km of descent off Cote 2000. Everything starts on the green Carambar, then the hill opens into six separate runs: 1 green, 3 blue, 1 red and 1 black, so it is weighted towards riders still building confidence rather than towards steeps. Rolling flow and technical rock both present, and the Vercors limestone gives it a character you do not get in the granite Alps.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Cote 2000 gondola from 1155 m carries three bikes and their riders per cabin. Prices are set by the lift company each season - check the operator.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 5 July; closed from 1 September for daily running, with weekends either side in June and September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Published hours, weather permitting.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Grenoble</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Lyon</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.villarddelans-correnconenvercors.com/activites/sport-au-grand-air-outdoor-besoin-de-se-depasser/velo/bike-park-velo-de-descente/">Villard de Lans / Correncon tourist office</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
