  <Placemark>
    <name>Gurten (Bern) [city fare + 3.50 CHF bike]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bern-Wabern 600 m - valley station of the Gurtenbahn funicular</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>GurtenTrail 2.0, rebuilt from scratch in 2025: 2.5 km and 240 m of descent with around 40 jumps, endless berms and a lot of thought in the shaping. Every feature is rollable, so beginners can ride the whole thing, while the line choices and doubles keep it interesting if you can send. Free bike wash on the third floor of the car park at the bottom.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Bern's local hill, so it is city transport pricing: take the S-Bahn or tram to Wabern, then the Gurtenbahn funicular. A bike ticket is 3.50 CHF per ride on top of your own fare, and the trail itself is free. Runs all year, every 15 minutes, which is what makes this a genuine winter option.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure (normally open year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: 07:00-23:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + funicular</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.gurtenpark.ch/">Gurtenbahn</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
