  <Placemark>
    <name>Grindelwald - First [Firstbahn, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Grindelwald 1060 m - valley station of the Firstbahn gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>No built bike park - Grindelwald is signed routes on alp roads and singletrack, with the scenery doing the heavy lifting, and it splits over two lifts. Off the <b>Firstbahn</b>: <b>green</b> Flat Track and Waldspitz First Section; <b>blue</b> Beni's Trail, Nodhalten, Sumpfenweg, Waldspitz Trail and Waldspitz Second Section; <b>red</b> Aellfluh, Bachalpsee - Waldspitz A and Spitze, the last dropping 739 m in 3.3 km. Off the <b>Eigerexpress and Wengernalpbahn to Kleine Scheidegg</b>, under the Eiger north face: <b>green</b> Alpiglen and the 8.8 km Romantikweg, which loses 1091 m; <b>blue</b> Lauberhorn and Scheideggwang; <b>red</b> Eigertrail (5.3 km, 705 m) with its two intro sections, Gemsenweg (721 m) and Blackrock. Grades are the operator's own signing rather than bike-park colours, so judge the line in front of you rather than the map.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Firstbahn six-seater gondola from Grindelwald at 1060 m to First in about 25 minutes, calling at Bort and Schreckfeld. Bikes cost 12 CHF per trip, and e-bikes are not carried. Bikes also go on the Bussalp, Waldspitz and Grosse Scheidegg postbus routes at half fare if there is room, but you must register by 15:00 the day before.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from late May; closed from late October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Interlaken Ost</td><td>Train</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bern</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h25</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://grindelwald.swiss/en/experiences/summer-activities/bike.html">Grindelwald Tourism</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>8.041783,46.625023,1062</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
