  <Placemark>
    <name>Andermatt - Gemsstock / Gutsch [bike pass, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Andermatt 1440 m - village, a few minutes from the Gutsch-Express valley station</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Signed routes rather than a built bike park, and high, exposed ground: the Gemsstock trail runs from the summit station down to the valley, flowing in places and technical in others; the Schoellenen downhill drops through the gorge above the Devil's Bridge and is for confident riders only; the Naetschen flow trail off the Gutsch-Express is the gentle one, and the valley-floor route suits families. No official per-difficulty count is published for the bike routes, so treat the grading on the ground as the authority.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Gutsch-Express gondola from Andermatt, and the Gemsstock cable car for the high start. Andermatt-Sedrun-Disentis sells dynamic tickets; the half-price card at 69 CHF pays for itself in two days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from late June; closed from mid-October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Goeschenen</td><td>Train</td><td>~12 min</td></tr><tr><td>Zurich</td><td>Train</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.andermatt-sedrun-disentis.ch/en/stories/tickets">Andermatt-Sedrun-Disentis</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>8.593329,46.636840,1438</coordinates></Point>
