  <Placemark>
    <name>La Forclaz - Le Tsaté (Val d'Hérens) [small t-bar]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Forclaz 1695 m - bottom station of the Le Tsaté t-bar, with the access road, parking and the restaurant</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A tiny, old-school bike spot on a south-facing slope above Evolène. Two surface lifts - a platter and a t-bar - drag you and your bike up to just above 2200 m, and you drop back through larch forest and open pasture on natural, unsurfaced singletrack. No bike park features, no crowd, just a quiet local run with views of the Dent Blanche and the Val d'Hérens. Two harder red descents drop off the Col du Tsaté at 2865 m, 3.5 km south of the lift and reached by pedalling or shuttling rather than by the t-bar: the east side runs 2.7 km to 2354 m, the west side 2.2 km to 2359 m. The Les Rocs Bike Tour is the other line here. The restaurant at the bottom does a solid croûte au fromage.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Small t-bar (téléski du Tsaté) and platter lift - bikes tag along on a hook. Day pass around 15-20 CHF; price not verified here. Check with the Evolène tourist office before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.evolene-region.ch/">Evolène Région Tourisme</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
