  <Placemark>
    <name>Thyon / Veysonnaz [~35 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Veysonnaz 1360 m - village gondola station, bus from Sion</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The forgotten corner of the 4 Vallées: Thyon sits on a high balcony above the Rhone and sends riders down through the Forêt de l'Ours (Bear Forest) on the 19 km Sion Descent, an expert enduro line that drops over 1600 m to Sion station - fast forest singletrack giving way to rocky switchbacks before rolling into the vineyards. Shorter named lines like DH sous cabine, Morraine, little red, backside greppon, Mind the gap, Sofleu and the Antenne ridge loop pack plenty into a lift-accessed day. South-facing and dry, the trail surface is fast when the snow clears.<br/><br/><b>Rain sensitivity</b><br/>Rain-resilient: south-facing slopes, rocky switchbacks and dry Rhone-valley exposure shed ordinary rain quickly.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Veysonnaz gondola to Thyon day ticket around 35 CHF - price not verified here; check veysonnaz.ch before travelling. Bike carriage on the gondola is included. The trailhead is right at the Thyon top station.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~2h00</td></tr><tr><td>Sion</td><td>Bus to Veysonnaz</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.veysonnaz.ch/fr/">Veysonnaz Tourisme</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
