  <Placemark>
    <name>Chalet-a-Gobet / Jorat (Lausanne) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Chalet-a-Gobet - Jorat forest trailhead</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The after-work option: a dense web of forest doubletrack and singletrack across the Jorat, ridable in any weather and floodlit by nothing at all, so bring lights in winter. No descents worth travelling for, but 20 minutes from your door and the trails drain well.<br/><br/><b>Rain sensitivity</b><br/>Rain-resilient: the Jorat forest network drains well and is regularly rideable in mixed weather.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and none needed - it is only 400 m above the city. Bus 64 from Lausanne, or the m2 to Croisettes and pedal up.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure in a typical year; check local conditions.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Bus / metro + bus</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.lausanne-tourisme.ch/en/">Lausanne tourism</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.692604,46.565724,869</coordinates></Point>
