    <name>Pila: Aosta-Pila gondola top (1790 m)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Pila 1790 m - Aosta-Pila gondola top station</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A large, natural-feeling gravity area above Aosta with more than 130 km of riding and 2100 m of vertical. The official 2026 park lists one blue flow trail, twelve red descents, three black trails and the black Corrado Herin World Cup line, plus the long freeride descent back to Aosta.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The 2026 adult bike pass is 40 EUR and includes bike transport. The Aosta-Pila gondola and bike park run daily from 13 June to 13 September 2026; Chamole opens from 20 June.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 14 September (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
