  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Houches: Prarion gondola top (1850 m)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Prarion 1850 m - gondola top station</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Lift-served riding at the quieter western end of the Chamonix valley. The Prarion sector has blue, red and black downhill lines, including the 4 km Chamois black run with 640 m of descent. The same valley pass also reaches the larger Balme network, which has six marked trails from blue to black.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The 2026 whole-valley MTB day pass is 40.50 EUR and gives uphill access at Les Houches and Balme. A Les Houches-only pass is 29.40 EUR. Summer riding is restricted to marked MTB routes in July and August.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; In July and August, ride only the marked MTB routes under the local municipal rules.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 21 September (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Chamonix</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.leshouches.com/summer/mountain-bike">Les Houches</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
