  <Placemark>
    <name>Whistler Mountain Bike Park (British Columbia) [season pass 999 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Whistler: bike park base, Whistler Village (675 m)</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The one every other bike park is measured against: over 100 km of trail across four zones, and the operator's own claim to be the number one lift-serviced bike park in the world. <b>Fitzsimmons</b> (max 1019 m) is the original zone and holds the widest spread, from the Fox Den skills zone and EZ Does It through B-Line and Crank It Up to A-Line, Dirt Merchant and Schleyer. <b>Garbanzo</b> (max 1850 m) sits above it and is steeper, longer and rockier - Freight Train, In Deep, Original Sin, No Joke. <b>Creekside</b> (max 1442 m) is the newest and purest singletrack, more than 30 km of it through creek-side forest: Blue Velvet, Midgard, Insomnia, Una Moss. <b>Peak</b> (max 2182 m) is one trail, Top of the World, an alpine descent of roughly 1500 m for advanced riders only.<br/><br/>
    The map carries 112 traces covering 100 named trails, drawn from OpenStreetMap and cross-checked against the official 2026 park map. Whistler hosts Crankworx from 24 July to 2 August 2026 and a UCI Downhill World Cup round from 25 to 27 September 2026.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Fitzsimmons Express chair lifts riders out of Whistler Village; the Garbanzo Express, the Creekside Gondola and the Peak Express open the higher zones as the season progresses. <b>The Peak Zone limits rider numbers per day and needs a separate Top of the World lift ticket on top of your bike park pass.</b> The adult bike-park season pass is 999 CAD. Single-day pricing varies by date and advance purchase.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Zone by zone in 2026: Fitzsimmons 15 May to 12 October, Garbanzo 13 June to 23 September, Creekside 20 June to 23 September, and the Peak Zone opening on conditions and running to 13 September. All zone dates are subject to weather.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-20:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Vancouver</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.whistlerblackcomb.com/explore-the-resort/activities-and-events/whistler-mountain-bike-park/whistler-mountain-bike-park.aspx">Whistler Bike Park</a>, <a href="https://www.whistlerblackcomb.com/plan-your-trip/lift-access/bike-park-passes.aspx">bike-park passes</a>, the <a href="https://cdn.whistler.com/s3/pdf/maps/whistler-mountain-bike-park-trail-map-2026.pdf">official 2026 bike park map</a>, <a href="https://blog.whistlerblackcomb.com/2026/05/whismas-ready-2026-trail-report/">Whistler Blackcomb 2026 trail report</a> and the linked OpenStreetMap trail geometries.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
