  <Placemark>
    <name>Machairas - Lythrodontas (Cyprus) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Machairas Forest mountain-bike hub from Lythrodontas</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Cyprus's strongest documented mountain-bike area combines long rough dirt tracks, pine forest, sudden technical descents and substantial climbing around Kionia, Machairas Monastery and Mantra tou Kampiou. The area hosts major MTB races, but it is a natural route network rather than a gravity park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free and pedal-accessed; no lift. The official 45 km circular route gains about 890 m and is rated very difficult. Guided e-MTB trips are available locally.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 October; closed from 01 June (best cooler-season window; access may be possible year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Summer heat and fire restrictions can affect forest access; check locally.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Nicosia</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Larnaca</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.visitcyprus.com/discover-cyprus/rural/cycling-rural/lythrodontas-circular-cycling-route/">Visit Cyprus circular route</a> and the <a href="https://www.visitcyprus.com/discover-cyprus/nature/cycling/lefkosia-2-lythrodontas-kionia-machairas-monastery-lythrodontas-cycling-route/">Machairas route guide</a>. Follow current forestry rules.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>33.298047,34.951352,412</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">machairas-lythrodontas</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">expert natural no-lift enduro</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">10-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">06-01</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Troodos Mountain Bike Routes (Cyprus) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Highland riding around Troodos Square and Mount Olympus</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Troodos cycling network mixes paved connectors, rough mining and forest roads, and natural mountain descents through pine forest and exposed ophiolite geology. It is best treated as adventure/enduro touring rather than a signed downhill park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No documented summer bike uplift. Ride from Troodos Square or build pedal/shuttle routes with a local guide; winter ski lifts should not be assumed to carry bikes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 April; closed from 01 December (typical snow-free riding window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Check forestry closures, heat, fire risk and route legality before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Limassol</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr><tr><td>Nicosia</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.troodosgeopark.com/en">Troodos UNESCO Global Geopark</a> and the official <a href="https://www.visitcyprus.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Cycling-WEB-ONLY.pdf">Visit Cyprus cycling guide</a>. Confirm current access locally.</i>]]></description>
