  <Placemark>
    <name>Mzaar Mountain Resort MTB (Lebanon) [no bike lift documented]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Summer mountain-bike trails at Mzaar Kfardebian</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Lebanon's largest mountain resort advertises summer MTB trails designed for speed, mountain exploration and full-day riding. Expect open limestone terrain, high ridges and natural resort tracks rather than a fully documented modern downhill park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Book the resort's MTB activity or arrange local support. Summer bicycle carriage on the ski lifts could not be verified, so plan on pedal or vehicle-assisted access rather than assuming uplift.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 May; closed from 01 December (typical snow-free window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical activity hours; booking, access and local conditions must be confirmed directly.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Beirut</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Faraya</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mzaarresort.com/activity/mtb-trail">Mzaar Mountain Resort</a>. Confirm the precise route, booking and access before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>35.847454,33.984282,2027</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">mzaar-mtb</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert natural no-lift enduro</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">05-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">12-01</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Chouf - Barouk Cedar Reserve MTB (Lebanon) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Natural mountain riding around Barouk and the Chouf</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Chouf is one of Lebanon's best-known mountain-bike regions, with long climbs and descents on rough tracks between Barouk, Maasser el Chouf, cedar forest and exposed Mount Lebanon ridges. The attraction is backcountry scenery and endurance-oriented natural riding, not purpose-built gravity trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal the routes or arrange guide and vehicle support. The cedar reserve is protected: bicycles may be restricted to designated roads and routes, so confirm the exact itinerary with reserve staff.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 May; closed from 01 December (typical snow-free window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Reserve hours, security conditions, snow and fire restrictions can change.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Beirut</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Barouk</td><td>Bike</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: official Lebanon tourism cycling guidance and the <a href="https://shoufcedar.org/">Shouf Biosphere Reserve</a>. Confirm bicycle permissions and current local conditions before riding.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>35.702272,33.705273,1326</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">chouf-barouk</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">expert natural no-lift enduro</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">05-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">12-01</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Bjelasnica Bike Park (Bosnia and Herzegovina) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>K1 ski lift - lift-assisted gravity above Babin Do</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Bosnia's clearest operating bike park uses purpose-built downhill and enduro terrain on the Olympic mountain. Expect open ski-slope sections, rocky technical ground and wooded lower trails rather than a large network of machine-built flow.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The K1 surface lift uses a special bicycle hook to tow riders and bikes uphill. Check the Olympic Centre for the current bike ticket and operating days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 June; closed from 01 October (typical summer operating window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00<br/><small>Season and hours are estimates; confirm the K1 bike-lift schedule before travel.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sarajevo</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://ocbjelasnica.com/bike-park/">OC Bjelasnica Bike Park</a>. Prices, lift operation and trail status can change.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>18.282900,43.714791,1274</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">bjelasnica</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">expert bike-park dh enduro t-bar</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">10-01</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Jahorina Bike Park (Bosnia and Herzegovina) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Olympic Centre gravity trail above Poljice</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A resort-operated bike trail on the 1984 Olympic mountain, combining open alpine riding with forest and shaped gravity sections. The developing park is suitable for confident riders but has less documented progression terrain than the large Alpine resorts.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer resort uplift serves the bike trail when scheduled. Check Jahorina for the current lift, bike transport and ticket details.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 15 September (typical summer window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; verify that bike uplift is operating on the selected date.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sarajevo</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.oc-jahorina.com/en/bike-staza/">Olympic Centre Jahorina</a>. Verify current summer operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>18.566872,43.736783,1528</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">jahorina</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">expert bike-park dh enduro gondola</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-15</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-15</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Durmitor - Zabljak (Montenegro) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>High-alpine adventure riding from Zabljak</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Durmitor offers demanding backcountry riding on rough mountain roads, shepherd tracks and permitted routes around the plateau, Tara canyon and Sinjajevina. The appeal is remote scenery and long natural days, not built downhill trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No verified bike uplift: climb under your own power or arrange vehicle support with a local guide. This is a protected national park, so confirm the exact bicycle route and current restrictions before riding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 June; closed from 01 November (typical snow-free window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Weather, snow and national-park access can change quickly.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Podgorica</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr><tr><td>Zabljak</td><td>Bike</td><td>direct</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.montenegro.travel/en/unique-montenegro/national-parks-of-montenegro/durmitor-national-park">Montenegro Tourism</a> and its official biking-route publications. Confirm permitted access locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>19.118866,43.155777,1435</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">durmitor-zabljak</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">expert natural no-lift enduro</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">11-01</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
