  <Placemark>
    <name>Saben Trail Area (Borgo San Dalmazzo) [pedal / shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Meridiane 1205 m - start of the freeride descent</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A volunteer-maintained natural enduro and freeride network on the wooded ridge between Valle Stura and Valle Gesso. The official Valle Stura routes include Meridiane, Monte Croce, Antenne and the long Saben 1500 descent; expect steep loam, roots, tight turns, natural features and shared hiking paths.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Pedal from Piano Quinto or arrange a local shuttle where permitted. The upper access beyond Tetto Pilone is closed to unauthorized motor vehicles; there is no trail fee.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Generally snow-free for much of the year. Conditions and volunteer maintenance vary; hikers always have priority.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Cuneo</td><td>Car / train + bike</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Piano Quinto</td><td>Bike</td><td>Pedal access</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mtbvallestura.com/b11-meridiane-freeride/">MTB Valle Stura - Meridiane Freeride</a>, <a href="https://www.mtbvallestura.com/b12-saben-1500-enduro/">Saben 1500</a> and <a href="https://www.mtbvallestura.com/b13-antenne-enduro/">Antenne Enduro</a>. Pin and geometry use OSM way 842338735, tagged with the Meridiane MTB name; indicative only.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>7.420652,44.319393,1206</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">saben-trail-area</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">expert natural no-lift enduro freeride shuttle rain-sensitive</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Saben Trail Area: Meridiane</name>
    <description><![CDATA[1.0 km mapped core of the red Meridiane freeride descent. The official route is longer; this line only draws the OSM section whose mtb:name is Meridiane. Geometry simplified from OpenStreetMap way 842338735. <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mtbvallestura.com/b11-meridiane-freeride/">MTB Valle Stura</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/842338735">OSM way 842338735</a>.</i>]]></description>
