  <Placemark>
    <name>Lanzo Valley Enduro [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Coassolo ridge 1425 m - top of a representative advanced descent</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A dispersed natural enduro network around Lanzo Torinese, Germagnano, Coassolo and the lower Valli di Lanzo. Community mapping lists green through double-black singletrack, including Funogolo and other long forest descents, with rocks, roots and old paths rather than a single signed park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or trail fee. Pedal or e-bike access is the norm; local guides run organized rides and occasional enduro days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Low trails can be ridden for much of the year; snow and freeze-thaw affect the upper network. This is shared, partly unsanctioned terrain, so verify access and current conditions.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Turin</td><td>Train / car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Lanzo Torinese</td><td>Bike</td><td>Pedal access</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://turismovallidilanzo.it/en/offers/mtb-tour-2026/">Turismo Valli di Lanzo MTB programme</a>, <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/region/lanzo-valley-enduro/map/">community trail inventory</a> and OSM way 522466645. The drawn line is an unnamed OSM S4 way in the mapped area, not an official signed trace.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>7.415881,45.324183,1423</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">lanzo-valley-enduro</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert natural no-lift enduro rain-sensitive</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Lanzo Valley Enduro: Coassolo ridge descent</name>
    <description><![CDATA[2.5 km unnamed S4 path descending from about 1425 m to 1190 m. It is included as a representative OSM trace, not as an official named line. Geometry simplified from OpenStreetMap way 522466645; check local access. <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/region/lanzo-valley-enduro/map/">Lanzo Valley Enduro inventory</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/522466645">OSM way 522466645</a>.</i>]]></description>
