  <Placemark>
    <name>Valle Cervo Freeride (Campiglia Cervo) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Catuin 1185 m - start of a representative freeride descent</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact but technical all-mountain and downhill network around Campiglia Cervo. Community mapping lists roughly 40 lines over rock, roots and steep forest terrain, from easier links to severe descents. The trails are natural, shared and condition-sensitive rather than a patrolled bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or trail fee. Pedal and e-bike access from Campiglia Cervo; use local parking and avoid blocking the narrow valley roads.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best from spring through autumn, with some low trails possible without snow in winter. Check reports after storms; the community currently warns of severe trail conditions.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Biella</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Campiglia Cervo</td><td>Bike</td><td>Pedal access</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/region/valle-cervo-freeride-73622/">Valle Cervo Freeride community inventory</a> and <a href="https://www.montagnabiellese.com/territorio/valle-cervo/">Montagna Biellese</a>. Catuin's trailhead aligns exactly with OSM way 573936538; the OSM way extends beyond the 1.9 km named community segment, so the drawn geometry is labelled representative.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>8.005822,45.642810,1183</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">valle-cervo-freeride</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert natural no-lift dh enduro freeride rain-sensitive</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Valle Cervo Freeride: Catuin corridor</name>
    <description><![CDATA[2.4 km OSM path starting at Catuin's community-mapped red trailhead. The named Catuin trail is 1.9 km; this longer OSM geometry is therefore a representative corridor, not claimed as an exact official trace. <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/trails/catuin/">Catuin community page</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/573936538">OSM way 573936538</a>.</i>]]></description>
