  <Placemark>
    <name>Fort Mountain State Park (Georgia) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>301 trail entrance 845 m - start of the official mountain-bike loop</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Fort Mountain State Park has 27 miles of bike-accessible trails. Its main ride is the 14.6-mile 301 Mountain Bike Trail, also called the East-West Bike Loop: a challenging backcountry circuit from ridge top to valley floor through hardwood forest, rocky ground, old mine country, waterfalls and Hassler's Mill Creek. The shorter Lake Loop is also open to bikes and walkers.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. The 301 is a pedal-powered loop with substantial climbing back to the trailhead. Georgia State Parks charges the current state-park parking fee; check the park page before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round, subject to park hours, weather and temporary trail closures. This is shared, remote terrain; carry water and repair equipment and yield to walkers.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Chatsworth, GA</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Cleveland, TN</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://gastateparks.org/FortMountain/Trails">Georgia State Parks trail description</a> and <a href="https://gastateparks.org/sites/default/files/parks/pdf/trailmaps/FortMountain_TrailMap.pdf">official trail map</a>. Pin on the entrance of the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/315250816">301 trail</a>, measured at 843 m. The full loop is not mapped as a reliable OSM geometry, so no trace is drawn.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-84.704437,34.765368,843</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">fort-mountain-state-park</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">intermediate expert natural no-lift enduro rain-sensitive</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>William Hastie Natural Area (Knoxville) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Third Circuit 330 m - top of a directional downhill trail</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A wooded natural-surface network in Knoxville's Urban Wilderness with about 6.3 miles of singletrack and old roads. The system mixes approachable multi-use trails with short technical sections. Third Circuit is a difficult, directional downhill mountain-bike trail; Sugar and Rum is another difficult hand-built line designed for downhill bike traffic.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no trail fee. Pedal from the official trailhead at 1302 Margaret Road; the natural area connects into the larger Urban Wilderness South Loop network.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open dawn to dusk unless posted otherwise. Natural-surface trails can be rain-sensitive; check local conditions, obey directional signs and yield on shared trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Downtown Knoxville</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Margaret Road trailhead</td><td>Bike</td><td>Pedal access</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.knoxvilletn.gov/cms/one.aspx?pageId=166756&amp;portalId=109562">City of Knoxville park page</a>, <a href="https://www.visitknoxville.com/urban-wilderness/explore/william-hastie-natural-area/">official Urban Wilderness trail information</a> and <a href="https://assets.simpleviewinc.com/simpleview/image/upload/v1/clients/knoxville/UW_hastie_print_7deab77f-c87b-491f-a39a-d786398aed70.pdf">official trail map</a>. Pin on the OSM-mapped top of Third Circuit, measured at 328 m.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-83.873754,35.932091,328</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">william-hastie-natural-area</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert natural no-lift dh enduro rain-sensitive</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>William Hastie Natural Area: Third Circuit</name>
    <description><![CDATA[0.7 km difficult directional downhill mountain-bike trail, descending from about 328 m to 280 m. Geometry simplified from OpenStreetMap way 1252742034; follow the official direction and signs on the ground. <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.visitknoxville.com/urban-wilderness/explore/william-hastie-natural-area/">Knoxville Urban Wilderness</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1252742034">OSM way 1252742034</a>.</i>]]></description>
