  <Placemark>
    <name>Cimone Bike Park (Sestola, Emilia-Romagna) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sestola 1036 m - valley station of the Sestola - Pian del Falco chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A broad Apennine destination mixing lift-served downhill, freeride, enduro and trail riding. Volcanic-looking rock, roots and long forest lines range from smooth flow to technical black descents.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Sestola - Pian del Falco chairlift is the bike-park lift, 1036 m to 1342 m. Selected summer lifts carry bikes; check Cimone for the current bike pass and sector schedule.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 27 September (typical summer window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; verify open lifts and trails.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Modena</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Bologna</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.cimone.it/">Cimone Bike Park</a>. Pin placed on the valley station of the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/79649819">Sestola - Pian del Falco chairlift</a> (way 79649819), measured at 1036 m. Verify current operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>10.765540,44.229370,1036</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">cimone</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-13</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-27</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Ponte di Legno - Tonale Bike Park (Lombardy/Trentino) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>High-alpine lift network from Ponte di Legno toward Tonale</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Long lift-linked descents combine bike-park flow, natural enduro, steep forest and rocky alpine terrain across a large vertical range. Easier family routes coexist with technical lines toward the valley.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer gondolas and chairlifts carry bikes; check Pontedilegno-Tonale for the current bike pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 20 September (typical lift season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; individual lifts have different calendars.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Brescia</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr><tr><td>Edolo</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.pontedilegnotonale.com/en/">Pontedilegno-Tonale</a>. Verify current MTB lift access.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>10.508662,46.258603,1243</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">ponte-tonale</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro chairlift gondola</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-20</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-20</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Monte Amiata Freeride (Tuscany) [uplift days]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Volcanic forest gravity on Monte Amiata</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A distinctive central-Italian network on an extinct volcano, with deep beech forest, loam, roots, rock gardens, enduro stages and purpose-built freeride. The best descents are technical and feel unusually alpine for Tuscany.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Organized uplift operates on selected days; otherwise climb by pedal or arrange a local shuttle. Check Amiata Freeride before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 April; closed from 01 December (typical riding and uplift season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00 on uplift days<br/><small>Opening is event/calendar-dependent.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Siena</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Grosseto</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.amiataturismo.it/">Amiata Turismo</a>. Confirm uplift and trail access.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>11.623274,42.887426,1724</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">monte-amiata</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">expert natural dh enduro freeride shuttle</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">04-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">12-01</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Roccaraso Bike Park (Abruzzo) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served gravity in the central Apennines</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of southern-central Italy's most relevant lift parks, with downhill, freeride and enduro over open mountain terrain and wooded lower slopes. It covers progression flow through technical rock, roots and jump lines.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Selected summer ski lifts carry bikes; check the operator for current tickets and sectors.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 06 September (typical main season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify open days and lift status.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Naples</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr><tr><td>Rome</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://roccaraso.net/">Consorzio Skipass Alto Sangro</a> and <a href="https://www.roccarasoturismo.it/en/">Roccaraso Turismo</a>. Verify current summer bike operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>14.078257,41.850261,1235</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">roccaraso</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride gondola</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-27</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-06</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Orres Bike Park (Hautes-Alpes) [28 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Three chairlifts above Les Orres 1650 and 1800</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of France's original purpose-built bike parks, with a broad progression from family flow to World Cup-level downhill, rough roots, steep natural lines and major freeride features. The long vertical and famously shaped tracks make it a national gravity destination.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Prelongis, Pic Vert and Pousterle chairlifts serve the park. Adult day pass 28 EUR at the published 2026 opening tariff.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 14 September (published 2026 main season plus September weekends).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Published standard hours; lift availability varies by period and weather.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gap</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Embrun</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.lesorres.com/espace-presse/saison-d-ete-2026-c-est-parti">Les Orres 2026 season</a> and <a href="https://www.lesorres.com/activites-et-animations/programme-des-animations/opening-les-orres-bike-park">opening information</a>. Verify live lift and trail status.</i> Pin corrected to the valley station of the Pic Vert chairlift (OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/161021884">way 161021884</a>), measured at 1666 m: the pin sat in the old village of Les Orres at 1457 m, 1.7 km below the ski station; the DH Coupe de France, Black Patrol and Cool Rider ways descend to the Les Orres 1650 front de neige, where the Pic Vert chairlift starts at a measured 1666 m.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.558120,44.493070,1666</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">les-orres</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-13</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-14</mwm:value><mwm:value key="price_day">28 EUR</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Pra Loup Bike Park (Ubaye) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Telemix de la Clappe above Pra Loup 1600</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>An accessible Southern Alps park with maintained downhill lines for progression, families and experienced riders, mixing sunny open slopes with forest singletrack, berms and technical sections.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Telemix de la Clappe carries bikes. Check the resort ticket shop for the current day tariff; rentals and a wash station are available at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Published 2026 lift hours; last descent at 17:00.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Barcelonnette</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Gap</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.praloup.com/en/activities/bike-park-de-pra-loup/">Pra Loup Tourism</a>. Verify ticket and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.602503,44.370151,1634</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">pra-loup</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">07-04</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">08-31</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Vars - Risoul Foret Blanche 360 (Hautes-Alpes) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Connected Vars and Risoul lift-served MTB domain</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The two resorts joined their networks for 2026 as Foret Blanche 360: 360 km of DH, enduro, cross-country and e-MTB routes. Vars alone offers green-to-black park lines, wooded singletrack, open alpine terrain and a huge 1800 m descent toward Embrun.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts on both sides serve the connected domain. Check Vars/Risoul for the current combined pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 31 August (published 2026 daily dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical lift hours; verify the connected-domain schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Briancon</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Embrun</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.vars.com/summer/experiences-to-live/mountain-biking-in-vars/">Vars official tourism</a>. Verify lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.682570,44.569868,1891</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">vars-risoul</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">07-04</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">08-31</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Montgenevre Bike Park (Hautes-Alpes) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served border park at Montgenevre 1860</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A high-altitude park straddling open alpine slopes and larch forest near the Italian border, with green and blue progression, technical red and black downhill, enduro links and a village pump track.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts carry bikes; current tariffs are published by the resort ticket office.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 31 August (typical summer window; verify 2026 lift dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical lift hours; check the official operating calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Briancon</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Turin</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://montgenevre.com/ete/bike-park">Montgenevre Bike Park</a>. Verify prices, lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.721800,44.931171,1859</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">montgenevre</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-27</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">08-31</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Meribel Bike Park (3 Vallees) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served park and enduro hub in the central 3 Vallees</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A large network of shaped downhill, jump lines and natural enduro connects Meribel's villages and high lifts. It offers genuine beginner flow alongside steep roots, rocks and long valley descents, with selected links toward Courchevel.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer gondolas and chairlifts carry bikes seven days a week; check the 3 Vallees summer tariff.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 30 August (typical main lift season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; check the lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Moutiers</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Chambery</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.meribel.net/en/resort/cyling-experience/">Meribel official tourism</a>. Verify current lifts and trails.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.566606,45.399064,1464</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">meribel</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift gondola</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">07-04</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">08-30</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Courchevel Bike Park (3 Vallees) [26.50 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Le Praz 1260 m - valley station of the Praz gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Courchevel valley sector counts 8 graded enduro itineraries - 1 green, 3 blue, 3 red and 1 black - plus 2 red downhill runs, 3 Funny Track learning routes and a pump track. The long one drops unbroken from the Saulire summit at 2740 m to Le Praz at 1350 m, and the network links east into Meribel Bike Park across the 3 Vallees. Big pedal-access terrain sits above the Vallee des Avals, outside the marked park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Five lifts carry bikes: the Saulire cable car and the Verdons, Praz and Chenus gondolas, plus the Foret chairlift (which closes 12:30-13:30). MTB day pass 26.50 EUR; 3 days 63 EUR, 7 days 99 EUR, season 240 EUR.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 30 August (2026 summer lift season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Ticket desks 09:00-12:40 and 13:30-16:10; hours vary by lift.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Moutiers</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Chambery</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.les3vallees.com/en/activities/enduro-and-bikepark">Les 3 Vallees enduro and bikepark</a> and <a href="https://www.skipasscourchevel.com/en/mtb-rates">Courchevel MTB rates</a>. Verify prices, lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.619240,45.431650,1261</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">courchevel</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift gondola cable-car</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">07-04</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">08-30</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Courchevel: Saulire cable car top</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Top of the Saulire cable car at 2690 m, the high entry point into the Courchevel network and the start of the full descent to Le Praz.]]></description>
