  <Placemark>
    <name>Valmeinier Bike Park (Maurienne) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Valmeinier 1800 - 1790 m, base of the Jeux chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eight marked downhill itineraries graded green to black, all of them starting from the base of the Jeux chairlift and dropping through the larch above the resort. The Galibier-Thabor domain is shared with Valloire, so the two link along the Crey du Quart ridge, and Valmeinier hosts a round of the French enduro series.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Jeux chairlift carries bikes and a lift pass is required; the operator does not publish a summer MTB tariff online, so ask at the ticket office.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 30 August (typical summer lift window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00<br/><small>Estimated; the Galibier-Thabor summer calendar is not published in advance.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saint-Michel-de-Maurienne</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Chambery</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h35</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.velo-maurienne.com/equipement/itineraires-descentes-vtt-valmeinier/">Maurienne Tourisme - Valmeinier downhill itineraries</a>. Verify prices, lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.494440,45.174360,1788</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">valmeinier</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">07-04</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">08-30</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Valmeinier: Jeux chairlift top</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Top of the Jeux chairlift at 2400 m, the high point of the Valmeinier descents.]]></description>
