  <Placemark>
    <name>Aussois Bike Park (Haute Maurienne) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Aussois 1540 m - base of the Grand Jeu chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A south-facing enduro spot above the Plan d'Aval and Plan d'Amont dams, better known locally than nationally and long a Transmaurienne Vanoise venue. The Grand Jeu chairlift opens Les Moulins (red, 5.7 km for 630 m of descent) and the black Plan d'Aval and Barrages lines; Evita Carnea is the blue and the longest, 6.5 km for 654 m off the chairlift top; Moulinator 1 is the red below the lake, narrow with hairpins and overbanked turns, and Moulinator 2 the black above it. A bike park sits in the village itself.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Grand Jeu chairlift takes bikes to 2180 m; a lift pass is required and no summer MTB tariff is published online.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 01 October, snow and weather permitting.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00<br/><small>In July and August the chairlift also runs for car-park access; hours are estimated, check locally.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Modane</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Chambery</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.aussois.com/en/les-activites-et-loisirs/l-ete-a-aussois/le-velo/les-parcours-vtt/">Aussois official tourism - mountain bike trails</a>. Verify prices, lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
