  <Placemark>
    <name>Alpe du Grand Serre (La Morte, Isere) [8 EUR per ride]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Alpe du Grand Serre 1380 m - base of the Blache chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A small Matheysine resort south of Grenoble carrying eight graded downhill trails from beginner up, and one line that is out of proportion to the rest of it: the DH de la Morte drops 1000 m over 6.5 km and is one of the most storied descents in the Isere. The mapped network runs to Black Forest 1 to 4, Canyon, DH de Lachaud and the Col du Parche lines. The Blache chairlift feeds the park; Serriou and Portes Sud carry on up toward the 2184 m summit.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Blache chairlift serves the downhill runs. A single ride is 8 EUR; family packages run 46 to 65 EUR. Winter season passes are valid in summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 30 May (weekends only through June and the first weekend of July, then Thursday to Sunday from 09 July to 23 August, weekends again in September); closed from 28 September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:40<br/><small>2026 published bike park calendar - it is a weekend operation for most of the season, so check before travelling.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Grenoble</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Lyon</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h10</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.matheysine-tourisme.com/en/alpe-du-grand-serre/activities/summer/bike/bike-park/">Matheysine Tourisme - Alpe du Grand Serre bike park</a>. Verify prices, lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>5.862100,45.022170,1379</coordinates></Point>
