  <Placemark>
    <name>Saint-Honore 1500 (Matheysine, Isere) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Saint-Honore 1500 - 1510 m, the station the tracks drop from</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A steep, unpatrolled downhill network dug under the little Matheysine station, 6 km south of Alpe du Grand Serre and completely separate from it. Six tracks fall roughly 350 m from around 1550 m to the fields above Villard-Saint-Christophe, and the gradients are the point: Black Forest averages 26%, High Way to VSC 31% and La petite derniere 32% - among the steepest sustained lines on this map. DH de Lachaud, La Jonche and Sunset Trail fill in the rest. Locals report the tracks well maintained, with clear lines and good grip.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. The station's own drag lifts do not run in summer and are not mapped; riders shuttle by car or pedal the forest road up from Villard-Saint-Christophe. Nothing to pay.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 May; closed from 31 October (snow-free season).<br/><small>No lift calendar - the tracks are north-facing forest, so they hold moisture in spring.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Grenoble</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>La Mure</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: trail geometry and grades from OpenStreetMap; the network is not covered by an operator page. Verify access and condition locally - these are steep unpatrolled tracks.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>5.820890,44.970470,1508</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">saint-honore-1500</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">expert natural no-lift dh freeride shuttle</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">05-15</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">10-31</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Savoie Grand Revard - La Feclaz (Bauges) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Feclaz 1330 m - base of the Orionde chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>An FFC-labelled site in the Bauges rather than a big gravity resort. The bike park sits at the top of the Orionde chairlift: five trails over about 200 m of drop - one green for learning, two blue, one red for committed riding and one black for confirmed riders - each mixing berms, jumps, modules and technical sections. Around it the Nordic ski network becomes a large FFC-signed summer layout with four entry points at La Feclaz, Le Revard, Saint-Francois-de-Sales and Arith.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Orionde chairlift is fitted with bike hooks. Helmets are compulsory and full-face plus protection is strongly advised. The operator does not publish a summer MTB tariff online.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 30 August.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-12:55 and 14:05-17:00<br/><small>2026 published chairlift hours - note the midday break.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Chambery</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Annecy</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.chamberymontagnes.com/savoiegrandrevard/que-faire/vtt/">Chambery Montagnes - Savoie Grand Revard mountain biking</a>. Verify prices, lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>5.982020,45.645530,1326</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">savoie-grand-revard</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">07-04</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">08-30</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
