  <Placemark>
    <name>St. Anton am Arlberg (Tirol, AT) [bike ticket]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>St. Anton 1305 m - valley station of the Rendlbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A major Arlberg resort whose summer riding is trail rather than shaped park. Two descents start at mountain stations in the village: the Rendl-Trail from the top of the Rendlbahn at 2020 m, and the technically harder Galzig-Trail from the Galzigbahn at 2080 m. Down in the valley the EldoRADo Bike-Areal Verwall adds a northshore trail, drop-offs, a pump track and an e-trial course, with dirt bikes for hire on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The bike ticket gives unrestricted use of the Rendlbahn and Galzigbahn including bike carriage; the Summer Premium Card includes bike transport free.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 04 October (2026 summer season; individual cable car dates vary).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check which lifts are turning before buying.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>St. Anton (railway station)</td><td>Walk</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Innsbruck</td><td>Train / car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.skiarlberg.at/en/st-anton/summer/mountain-bike">Ski Arlberg - St. Anton mountain biking</a>. Verify prices, lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
