  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Katzenkopf Leutasch (Seefeld, AT) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Leutasch 1130 m - valley station of the Katzenkopf chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A small, deliberately family-and-beginner-oriented park in the Olympiaregion Seefeld, running between 1100 and 1360 m. Three single trails - Kitty Twister, Green Pangea and the Dirty Dancer line - plus a pump track, a gravel-pit practice area and a beginners' zone. The trails are mapped as one-way singletrack at the easy end of the technical scale, so this is a progression spot, not a gravity destination.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A three-seater chairlift carries bikes and hikers, and a conveyor belt serves the pump track. The Seefeld region guest card gives one ascent and descent at half price; the Freizeitticket Tirol is valid with a bike park surcharge. Rental and shop at the valley station.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 09 May (Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays only until 19 June, then daily); closed from 13 September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00<br/><small>2026 published lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Seefeld in Tirol</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Innsbruck</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.seefeld.com/en/bikepark-katzenkopf-leutasch.html">Olympiaregion Seefeld - Bikepark Katzenkopf Leutasch</a>. Verify prices, lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
