  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Hochkonig - Dienten (Salzburg, AT) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Dienten 1075 m - base of the Burglalm chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two flowtrails on opposite sides of the Hochkonig massif, 7.2 km between them. The Flowtrail Hochkonig off the Burglalm six-seater in Dienten is the substantial one: 4.2 km winding through meadow and forest for 550 m of descent. The second, Flow One above Maria Alm, runs 2.2 km for 280 m off the Natrunbahn. Both are flow lines rather than technical downhill.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Burglalmbahn in Dienten and the Natrunbahn in Maria Alm both take bikes; the trails are open during those lifts' operating hours. The HochkonigCard includes one bike carriage per day on one of the summer cable cars.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 20 September (typical summer cable car window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated; ring the Burglalmbahn or Natrunbahn for the current calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bischofshofen</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Salzburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.hochkoenig.at/en/summer/bike/adrenalin-action-on-the-mountain.html">Hochkonig - MTB adventures</a>. Verify prices, lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
