  <Placemark>
    <name>Trailcenter Faaker See - Finkenstein (Karnten, AT) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Finkenstein 1030 m - top of the trail network, above Faak am See</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eight signed, hand-built singletrails on the slopes above the Faaker See, numbered T22 to T29 and maintained by the Finkenstein tourist board: Flowgartner T25 and Lowgartner T26 as the flowing beginner-friendly pair with the turquoise lake below, Latschacher T29 built harder with jumps, Kopein T23, Samonigg T22, Ischnig, Shorty, and the Blairwitch T27 as the black - a natural line of roots, stone and narrow passages near the Baumgartnerhof. Everything sits between about 690 and 1030 m.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. The trails are pedalled or shuttled on the forest roads, and there is no charge to ride them.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 April; closed from 15 November (snow-free season; low altitude means a long one).<br/><small>No lift calendar to check - ride when the ground is dry.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Villach</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Klagenfurt</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.lake.bike/de/trails.html">lake.bike - Faaker See trails</a>. Verify access and trail status locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>13.904590,46.533310,1026</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">faaker-see</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert natural no-lift enduro flow</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">04-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">11-15</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>La Plagne Bike Park (Tarentaise) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Colorado chairlift sector up to 2300 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A high-volume park with green progression, long blue flow, technical reds and blacks, enduro itineraries and descents linking the altitude villages to the valley. The lower maximum altitude helps it open reliably by late June.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts including Colorado serve the park; check La Plagne for the current MTB pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 30 August (typical main season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify the published lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Aime-la-Plagne</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Albertville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h05</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://en.la-plagne.com/explore-the-multitude-of-activities-on-offer/dive-into-the-heart-of-summer/biking/bike-park">La Plagne official tourism</a>. Verify lifts and trails.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.704912,45.504299,2076</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">la-plagne</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-27</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">08-30</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Saisies Bike Park (Beaufortain) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served Beaufortain park facing Mont Blanc</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>17 marked runs: 3 green (Coyote, Pikachu, Shrek), 7 blue (Cornifle, Droit dans lo Boets, El'fly, Fends la Bise, Lovely Woods, Monchu, Tsapa Secreta), 4 red (Bougnette, Dre dans l'Pentu, Saisissante, Tabasco) and 3 black (Borat, Cuberote, Natur Hell). Around that sit enduro routes, FFC cross-country loops, play zones and a pump track. The mix runs from approachable flow to rooty, steep forest, and the whole thing faces Mont Blanc.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Three lifts in summer: Legette, Chard du Beurre and Bisanne. Legette and Chard du Beurre run daily from 20 June to 6 September, Bisanne daily from 4 July to 28 August. One day pass covers the Les Saisies and Crest-Voland/Cohennoz bike areas together.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 7 September (published 2026 lift dates, with a pre-opening weekend on 13-14 June).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00 (Legette); 09:30-16:55 (Chard du Beurre, Bisanne)<br/><small>Published 2026 hours; verify the daily lift schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Albertville</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Annecy</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://en.lessaisies.com/accessible-mountains-in-summer/mountain-biking-for-all/bike-park-2/">Les Saisies official tourism</a>. Verify current operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.539448,45.757330,1637</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">les-saisies</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-15</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-15</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>La Rosiere Bike Park (Espace San Bernardo) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sunny border-facing park above the Tarentaise</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Four downhill tracks and six enduro/e-bike routes deliver up to 1200 m of descent, combining shaped park sections, natural singletrack and panoramic traverses toward the Italian border.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts carry bikes; passes are sold at La Rosiere Centre and Les Eucherts.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 06 September (typical summer window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify the current lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bourg-Saint-Maurice</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.larosiere.net/bike-park/">La Rosiere Tourism</a> and <a href="https://www.larosiere.ski/en/activity/bike-park">Espace San Bernardo</a>. Verify current operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.850258,45.626652,1839</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">la-rosiere</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-27</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-06</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
