  <Placemark>
    <name>The Mother Bikepark Winterberg (Germany) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Three uplifts serving Germany's largest gravity park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eleven lines from beginner to professional on a small hill, packed tightly enough that Winterberg is the reference park for northern Germany. The 1650 m SRAM Flow Country Line is the longest and the one everyone rides first; the Conti Track and the slopestyle area are the serious end; Fly by and Jolly Jumper are the newest, built with small jumps and side hits so riders of any level can work up. Rental and coaching at the base. The park does not publish a green/blue/red/black split - the grades are marked on the ground.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Three lifts serve the park. Day ticket from 46 EUR adult, 34 EUR youth and 25 EUR child; four-hour tickets run 09:30-13:30 or 13:30-17:30. Multi-day tickets shared with Willingen are available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 24 April; closed from 09 November (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:30 April-September; 09:30-16:30 October-November<br/><small>Published 2026 hours; individual lifts and trails may close.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Dortmund</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Winterberg station</td><td>Bike</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bikepark-winterberg.de/?lang=eng">Bikepark Winterberg</a> and its <a href="https://www.bikepark-winterberg.de/tagesticket">day-ticket page</a>. Check live lift, trail and ticket information.</i>]]></description>
