    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Rold Skov Trailcenter (Denmark) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Denmark's largest technical forest MTB network</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around 50 km and roughly 1000 m of cumulative climbing cover blue, red, black and extreme grades. The network mixes flowing singletrack, roots and punchy climbs with a dedicated skills area and Denmark's largest downhill track, a 450 m orange line dropping about 45 m.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free and pedal-accessed; no lift. Routes start near Skorping Hallen and must be ridden in the marked direction.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 January; closed from 01 January (normally year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Respect Nature Agency rules and avoid damaging saturated or frozen trails.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Aalborg</td><td>Train + bike</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Skorping station</td><td>Bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://naturstyrelsen.dk/aktiviteter-i-naturen/cykling-loeb-og-fitness/mountainbike/de-10-spir/rold-skov-himmerland">Danish Nature Agency</a>. Follow current forestry notices.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>9.871925,56.831338,79</coordinates></Point>
