  <Placemark>
    <name>Twin Peaks Bike Park (Niseko, Hokkaido) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Free community trail network above Hirafu</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Japan's largest free-access bike park has more than 17 km across 20 professionally built trails. Five green trails lead into blue flow, rock-and-root black lines and the double-black Taki Tech. Most descents are bike-specific and one-way, while several connectors are shared with other users.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free. No lift and no shuttle: use the purpose-built climbing trails. The nonprofit NAMBA manages the network and publishes live wet-trail status; do not ride closed or saturated trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 May; closed from 1 November (published mid-May to end-October window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 07:00-19:00<br/><small>Check NAMBA for current trail conditions.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://namba.ngo/twin-peaks/">NAMBA Twin Peaks</a>. Access and conditions can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
