  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Kronplatz: Reischach valley station (950 m)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kronplatz summit 2270 m - top of the Kronplatz 2000 gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The biggest bike park in the Dolomites, on a free-standing dome with lifts up three separate sides. The Herrnsteig is the one people come for: 8 km and 1300 m of descent from the summit to Reischach, South Tyrol's first designated freeride trail back in 2010 and still the yardstick. Around it sit graded flow and jump lines, and the Furcia and San Vigilio sectors on the far flanks. The 360-degree summit view over the Dolomites is not a bad way to start a run.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Every summer gondola carries bikes: Kronplatz 2000 and Ried from Reischach at 950 m, Olang from the Valdaora side, Piz de Plaies from San Vigilio. Adult bike day pass 53 EUR, season 325 EUR, bike transport included. The Dolomiti Supersummer pass at 67 EUR a day covers this and the neighbouring valleys.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 16 May; closed from 12 October (published 2026 dates). Sectors open in stages: Reischach from 16 May, San Vigilio from 19 June, Valdaora from 20 June.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bolzano</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Innsbruck</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.kronplatz.com/en">Kronplatz</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
