  <Placemark>
    <name>Peyragudes-Loudenvielle Bike Park (Pyrenees) [33 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Loudenvielle 963 m - valley station of the Skyvall gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Twenty marked green-to-black downhill and enduro trails sit inside the Louron valley's much larger 420 km riding network. The full mountain combines maintained park lines, long natural enduro descents and World Cup terrain, with exceptional vertical back to the lake at Loudenvielle - including <b>L'integrale</b>, billed as the longest green VTT descent in the Pyrenees at 13 km from the Peyragudes ridge down to the lake. The 2026 map signs Coustete, Candy, Six Pack, Matete, Kahn, World Cup, Privilege, L'integrale, Balestas, Val d'Aube, Spiderman, Magic Line, Blue Wave Agudes, Enduro Serie, Coumaou, Skyvall Bleu, Goutaou, AP4 Airline, Urge Line, Pourticou and Zebre, plus pumptracks at Loudenvielle and Peyresourde.<br/><br/><b>None of these trails is in OpenStreetMap.</b> The whole massif holds no named path, no <code>route=mtb</code> relation and no graded way, so this spot has a pin and no lines - see the operator's own trail map for the routes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Skyvall carries bikes from Loudenvielle to 1600 m, then the Privilege chairlift reaches the high trail starts. The 2026 full-area adult day pass starts at 33 EUR; a station-only or Skyvall-only pass starts at 28 EUR.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 8 May; closed from 19 October (published 2026 span). May, June, September and October are mostly weekends and holidays; daily operation is from 4 July through 30 August, and the upper chairlifts run on selected days.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tarbes</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr><tr><td>Toulouse</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.n-py.com/fr/peyragudes/bike-park">official N'PY bike park page</a>, its <a href="https://storage.googleapis.com/npy-website-media-prod/Peyragudes-VTT-plan-des-pistes-2026.pdf">2026 trail map</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/721753384">OSM Skyvall gondola</a>. Pin marks the Skyvall valley station at Loudenvielle, measured at 963 m; verify which lifts operate on your date.</i>]]></description>
