  <Placemark>
    <name>Saint-Lary Bike Park (Pyrenees) [26 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bouleaux chairlift summit 2215 m - maintained riding above Pla d'Adet</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>More than 40 km of marked green-to-black trails between 2215 m and 1700 m. Family Rider and Easy Rider provide genuine progression terrain, while Woodstock brings long flow and wood features; K-Bourre and Razorback supply the technical black riding. Ten maintained trails and an initiation zone make this one of the most complete parks in the French Pyrenees: Family Rider (green), Easy Rider and Ricou (blue), Full Mountain, Woodstock, All In, Vipere and Shorewood (red, the last built entirely of wooden bridges and the only one of its kind in the French Pyrenees), and K-Bourre and Razorback (black).<br/><br/><b>None of them is in OpenStreetMap.</b> Between 1700 m and 2215 m the map holds no named path at all - the highest is a 1692 m village chemin - so this spot has a pin and no lines. See the operator's own trail map for the routes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The detachable Bouleaux chairlift carries bikes. The 2026 adult day pass is 22.50 EUR from Pla d'Adet or 26 EUR including the cable car from Saint-Lary village.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates). The opening weekend uses the Bouleaux chairlift only; daily operation runs from 4 July through 30 August.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tarbes</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr><tr><td>Toulouse</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://saint-lary.altiservice.com/en/activities/bike-park/">official Saint-Lary bike park page</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/96286387">OSM Pic Lumiere cable car</a>. Pin marks the cable-car valley station in Saint-Lary village, measured at 821 m; check weather and lift status.</i>]]></description>
