  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>BikePark Wales (Wales, UK) [uplift price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Merthyr Tydfil 355 m - uplift base at Gethin Woods, the UK's largest gravity trail network</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around fifty all-weather trails: 2 green, 13 blue, 16 red, 14 black and 4 pro lines, plus a pump track. Kermit is the long green introduction and the progression through blue and red is unusually well judged; the blacks and pro lines are steep, technical and race-paced, which is why the park draws riders from the whole UK. Purpose-built surfacing means it rides through Welsh rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Van uplift, booked in advance, or a 5 km singletrack climb that takes about 30 minutes if you would rather pedal. Pay-as-you-go is roughly 7 GBP a run for 13 and over, 5 GBP for 12 and under, with cheaper bundles and weekday rates; full-day pass prices are dynamic, so check the booking calendar.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Normally open year-round on scheduled days. Booking availability, storms and trail work can affect individual dates.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Cardiff</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bristol</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bikeparkwales.com/mountain-bike-trails-wales">BikePark Wales trails</a> and <a href="https://www.bikeparkwales.com/uplift-passes">uplift passes</a>; uplift booking is strongly recommended.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-3.377800,51.718700,357</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
