  <Placemark>
    <name>Dyfi Bike Park (Wales, UK) [uplift price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Dyfi Forest - big-mountain gravity trails built by the Athertons</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A 650-acre destination with hand-built red through triple-black trails. Long, fast and technical descents combine natural rock and roots with large jumps and race-scale features. There is no beginner terrain: even the red trails require solid bike-park skills.<br/><br/><b>Red Bull Hardline</b><br/>The first Red Bull Hardline was created here in 2014, and the Dyfi Valley remained the original Welsh Hardline venue through its later editions. The invitation-only Hardline race course is separate from the public bike-park trail menu; ride only trails opened by Dyfi Bike Park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Land Rover shuttles provide uplift from the base. Prices and operating days vary through the booking calendar, so reserve directly with the park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Normally open year-round on selected booked days, subject to Welsh mountain weather, events and maintenance closures.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Aberystwyth</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Manchester</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.dyfibikepark.co.uk/the-park/">official Dyfi Bike Park history and trail information</a> and <a href="https://www.redbull.com/gb-en/event-series/red-bull-hardline">Red Bull Hardline series</a>; advance booking required.</i>]]></description>
