  <Placemark>
    <name>Vallée de Munster · Linge · Hohnack [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Munster 381 m - rail-served pedal base for the Linge and Hohnack enduro trails</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A natural, pedal-access enduro area on the two ridges above the Munster valley, with no lift and no park. Five traces are drawn here - one black, two red and two blue, about 10.6 km in total. The centrepiece is the <b>Mémorial</b>, a permanent enduro trail on the heights of Hohrod built and maintained by the local Trails Patrol association and open to riders year-round since 2018; it drops 422 m through the shell craters of the 1914-18 Linge battlefield and is mapped in OpenStreetMap as a one-way, bike-only cycleway. <b>Fastrod</b> falls 308 m from Hohrodberg straight into Munster, and the <b>Croix de Wihr</b> traverse links the Hohrodberg side across to the Hohnack ridge. On the Grand Hohnack above Labaroche, the <b>Stèle</b> is a 1.1 km red and <b>DH Grand Hohnack</b> is a short, very steep black at an average 32%. Alongside these, the tourist office signs six waymarked cross-country circuits (M1 Moraine, M2 Hohrodberg, M3 Lacs, M4 Gaschney, M5 Mittlach-Schnepfenried, M6 Petit Ballon), 20-41 km, all intermediate except the sportif M6.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no trail fee. Everything is pedalled or shuttled by road: Hohrodberg is roughly 320 m of climbing from Munster, the Linge ridge about 590 m, and the Grand Hohnack about 590 m via Gunsbach and Labaroche. The trailheads are spread over 7 km of ridge, so this is a riding area rather than one hillside. The Colmar-Munster-Metzeral railway puts the base station at the bottom of Fastrod.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; The Linge and Hohrod trails cross a protected First World War battlefield with cemeteries, an ossuary and unexploded ordnance still in the ground. Stay on the trail, do not dig or ride off-piste, and expect walkers on foot.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable roughly April to November. The valley suspends trail maintenance over the winter, and the forest ground stays greasy on roots and loam for a while after rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Colmar</td><td>Train</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Colmar</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Strasbourg</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.vallee-munster.eu/velo-et-vtt/circuits-vtt/">Vallée de Munster tourist office VTT circuits</a>, <a href="https://www.vojomag.com/enduro-de-la-vallee-de-munster-2018-les-alsaciens-savent-recevoir/">Vojo on the Enduro de la Vallée de Munster and the permanent Mémorial trail</a>, and OpenStreetMap. Access and trail status can change; verify locally.</i>]]></description>
