  <Placemark>
    <name>Vallée de Munster: Mémorial</name>
    <description><![CDATA[3.4 km red, difficult route in the Munster valley, dropping 422 m from 971 m to 549 m at an average 12%. This is the valley's permanent enduro trail, built and maintained by the Trails Patrol association and open year-round; OpenStreetMap holds it as a one-way, bike-only cycleway (<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/594166921">way 594166921</a>). <i>Trace drawn in gpx.studio and supplied for this map, simplified to ~8 m - indicative only. Natural forest singletrack shared with walkers on the 1914-18 Linge battlefield - ride sighted and stay on the trail.</i>]]></description>
