  <Placemark>
    <name>Timberland Mountain Bike Park (Rizal, PH) [250-550 PHP]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Timberland Heights, San Mateo - purpose-built trail park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A patrolled, colour-graded network from beginner flow to expert gravity, with berms, rollers, tabletops, bridges and rollable drops. Expect climbing between descents because there is no uplift.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Pedal access. Published passes are 250 PHP weekdays and 550 PHP weekends and holidays, plus the operator's current insurance or registration requirements.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round with a reduced wet-season schedule. <br/>Daily opening hours: 07:00-16:00<br/><small>Published hours; Wednesday-Sunday in the dry season and Thursday-Sunday in the wet season.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Metro Manila</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://timberlandmountainbikepark.com/pages/know-before-you-go">official Timberland rider information</a>.</i>]]></description>
