  <Placemark>
    <name>Lafur / Mazandaran Forest MTB (IR) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lafur 340 m - Hyrcanian forest valley in Savadkuh</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Dense beech forest, loamy village tracks, steep mountain roads and wet roots - a green contrast to the dry southern Alborz two hours south. Lafur sits in Savadkuh county in Mazandaran; the name means riverbank, and the forest runs to roughly 800 hectares as part of the UNESCO-listed Hyrcanian forests, bordered by Shirgah to the north, the Alborz to the south and Babol to the west. Operators ride it as a mix of gravel road, dirt road, tarmac and some singletrack. Shurmast Lake, Zangian Cave, the Veresk bridge and Alasht village are all within a short drive. There is no signed trail centre, and forest protection, land access and navigation all need local knowledge.<br/><small>Nothing is drawn here: an mtb-tag sweep of the valley returns zero features.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Arrange a guide and vehicle support in Mazandaran; use only permitted roads and tracks.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December. Best April-June and September-November - avoid saturated ground, snow and peak summer humidity.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/>
    <small>A protected hunting-free area, not a trail network: go with somebody local.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Tehran</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Babol</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://visitiran.ir/en/attraction/Lafur--Forest">Visit Iran on Lafur Forest</a> for the setting and the 800 ha figure, and <a href="https://www.adventureiran.com/tag/hyrcanian-forest/">Adventure Iran on Hyrcanian-forest riding</a> for what the surface is actually like. Pin placed on the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/11499158">Lafur protected area</a> (relation 11499158), measured at 341 m; the previous coordinate was rounded to 52.93,36.26 and carried a 641 m altitude that matched nothing nearby. This is a regional adventure pin, not a marked MTB park.</i>]]></description>
