  <Placemark>
    <name>Lar National Park / Damavand MTB (IR) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lar National Park 2,960 m - the Lar plain beneath Mount Damavand</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A serious point-to-point backcountry ride across alpine plateau, riverbeds, dirt tracks and high passes under Iran's 5,610 m volcano. Commercial itineraries rate it highly demanding and normally run it over several days with camps. The park is in Amol district, Mazandaran, on the north-western approach to Damavand.<br/><small>Nothing is drawn here: an mtb-tag sweep of the park returns zero features. The riding is plateau tracks and riverbeds, not mapped singletrack.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Guided trips use support vehicles and camps; permits and protected-area access must be arranged in advance.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 May; closed from 1 September. Snow, river levels and conservation closures control access.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/>
    <small>2,900-3,500 m throughout, with a national-park permit regime: do not ride here unguided.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Tehran</td><td>Guide vehicle</td><td>~2h to the western approach</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the <a href="https://damavand.camp/tours/mountain-biking/5-day-lar-plain-mtb/">5-day Lar plain MTB itinerary</a> and <a href="https://www.adventureiran.com/mountain-biking-lar-national-park/">Adventure Iran's trip report</a>. Pin moved onto the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/11497873">Lar National Park</a> boundary (relation 11497873), measured at 2,961 m; the previous coordinate was rounded to 52.05,35.90 and sat about 26 km east of the park, in the wrong valley.</i>]]></description>
