  <Placemark>
    <name>Shaxi / Dali Tea-Horse Trails (Yunnan, CN) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Shaxi 2,100 m - Tea-Horse Road town between Dali and Lijiang</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Old stone caravan roads, pine-forest paths, village tracks and high passes through Bai and Yi cultural landscapes. Shaxi is the anchor: a trading post for tea and horses since the Tang dynasty, at its height under the Ming and Qing, and UNESCO-recognised as one of the most intact tea-horse towns left in China. The historic Shaxi - Mapingguan - Misha track is the classic line and has seen renewed traffic as interest in the Tea Horse Road revived; the Shibaoshan Buddhist grottoes sit just west. Operators sell it as point-to-point weeks - Dali to Shaxi to Lijiang, or the longer Shangri-La to Tiger Leaping Gorge run - so it is guided expedition riding, not a signed bike park.<br/><small>Nothing is drawn here: an mtb-tag sweep of the Shaxi basin returns zero features.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bike lift. Commercial guides use vehicle transfers for the point-to-point stages. Confirm permissions - many of the famous hiking and heritage paths here are not automatically bike routes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 March; closed from 1 December. Best March-May and September-November; summer monsoon mud and winter snow affect the high routes.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/>
    <small>2,100-3,000 m, and heritage paths shared with walkers: ride considerately.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Dali</td><td>Car / guide vehicle</td><td>~2h</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Lijiang</td><td>Car / guide vehicle</td><td>~2h</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://yunnanexploration.com/tours/8-days-dali-shaxi-lijiang-cycling-tour-along-the-ancient-tea-horse-caravan">the Dali-Shaxi-Lijiang cycling itinerary</a>, <a href="https://bikeasia.com/tours/yunnan-the-tea-horse-trail">Bike Asia's Tea Horse Trail</a> and <a href="https://www.bikechina.com/">Bike China</a>. Pin moved onto the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/705132259">Shaxi town</a> node (705132259), measured at 2,103 m; the previous coordinate was rounded to 100.11,25.69 and sat 76 km south-east near Dali at a claimed 2,939 m. Use a local MTB guide and verify each route.</i>]]></description>
