  <Placemark>
    <name>Kenting MTB Trails (Pingtung, TW) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kenting Forest Recreation Area 210 m - park-gate access to the Cow Pastures trails</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Open coastal singletrack in the hills behind Kenting, at the southern tip of Taiwan. The Formosan Fat Tire Association's directions are the whole guide here: in through the main gates of Kenting National Park, then the first left. That reaches the Cow Pastures, a half-day ride of smooth open singletrack with quick downhill sections and some jump and drop playgrounds, plus miles of vague unmapped trails to poke at. Sea views back down to the ocean the whole way. Dajianshi Shan (318 m), the rock spire that is the park's landmark, sits just west of the pin. Heat and sun exposure are the real limit - locals say it can be unbearable even in spring and autumn.<br/><small>Nothing is drawn here: the whole Hengchun peninsula holds one 0.1 km mtb-tagged fragment in OpenStreetMap and no named trail. The trails are unsigned and known by word of mouth.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal from the park access roads. Free, but national-park rules apply. A local guide (@accompany_bike_studio) runs supported rides.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; typhoon season (Jul-Sep) can close or wash out trails, and summer heat is intense.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/>
    <small>Natural trails inside a national park: respect all signage, park rules and weather closures.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Kenting / Hengchun</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Kaohsiung</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~2h</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the <a href="https://formosanfattire.com/rides/kenting/">Kenting Formosan Fat Tire Association ride guide</a> for the access and the Cow Pastures, and the <a href="https://ziraneffect.com/">Ziran Effect blog</a>. Pin placed on the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/5355592454">Kenting Forest Recreation Area</a> node (5355592454), measured at 212 m; the previous coordinate was rounded to two decimals and sat on the coast at 28 m. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
