  <Placemark>
    <name>Peacock Flats / Kuaokala (Oahu, US) [permit access, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mokuleia 3 m - beach park trailhead parking, where the climb starts</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Rough ridge roads and steep, technical rainforest singletrack connect the Peacock Flats camping area and Kuaokala zone, with exposed ocean views and loose, eroded sections. This is remote natural riding, not a maintained bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Access through the Space Force tracking-station road is controlled; obtain the required state permit and carry identification. Expect a substantial pedal and route-finding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round when access is open; avoid storms, mud and high fire-risk closures.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Honolulu</td><td>Car + pedal</td><td>~1h30 to gate</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://dlnr.hawaii.gov/dofaw/fw-announcements/access-restored-to-public-lands-on-west-o%CA%BBahu-via-the-space-force-satellite-tracking-station-road/">Hawaii DLNR access notice</a>. Verify permits and gate arrangements before departure. Pin on the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/205436631">Mokuleia Beach Park</a> (way 205436631), the published parking for the Kuaokala-Mokuleia permit area; the riding is 1500 ft above, reached by the Mokuleia Access Road. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
