  <Placemark>
    <name>St Louis Heights / Waahila Ridge (Oahu, US) [access must be checked, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Wa'ahila Ridge 328 m - state recreation area at the top of St Louis Heights</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The forested ridge above St Louis Heights has steep roots, clay, narrow natural lines and short technical descents. It is shared hiking terrain rather than a sanctioned bike park, and bicycle permission can vary by segment.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal from town, but confirm locally that every intended trail permits bicycles; yield to walkers and do not ride closed or hiking-only paths.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Potentially rideable year-round, but wet red clay becomes slick and damaging. Access status is not sufficiently documented for a destination trip.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Waikiki</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Indicative local riding-zone pin only. Confirm legal bicycle access with Hawaii trail managers before riding.</i><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://dlnr.hawaii.gov/recreation/nah/oahu/">Hawaii DLNR trails</a>. Pin on the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/560399540">Wa'ahila Ridge State Recreation Area</a> (way 560399540), measured at 328 m, where the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/544969461">Waahila Mountain Bike Route</a> begins. The previous pin sat 500 m below in the suburb at 132 m. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
