  <Placemark>
    <name>Papenoo Valley (Tahiti, PF) [backcountry, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Tahiti's volcanic interior adventure route</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A rough valley road and connecting tracks enter a deep volcanic canyon through rainforest, river crossings and waterfall country. It is scenic backcountry and expedition-style riding, not a signed singletrack park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Ride out-and-back or arrange a local guide and 4x4 support. River depth, landslides and private or controlled sections can alter the route.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best in the drier May-October period; avoid heavy rain because rivers rise quickly and surfaces become hazardous.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Papeete</td><td>Car + bike</td><td>~45 min to valley mouth</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.tahititourisme.jp/natural-heritage/papenoo-valley-maroto/">Tahiti Tourisme Papenoo Valley</a> and local bike rental or guide advice.</i>]]></description>
