    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Morne Gommier MTB (Martinique, MQ) [shared tracks, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Panoramic southern Martinique hill riding</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Steep lanes, farm tracks and natural paths around Morne Gommier form scenic cross-country and short enduro-style loops above Le Marin. The terrain is more mixed-surface exploration than a marked trail centre.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no trail pass. Pedal from Le Marin or start near the viewpoint; confirm private-property boundaries and use a local guide for less obvious connections.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; December-May is generally drier. Avoid exposed routes during heavy rain, tropical storms and the hottest part of the day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Le Marin</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Fort-de-France</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.martinique.org/en/blog/activities-sports/mountain-biking-martinique">Martinique Tourism MTB guide</a>. Route choice and land access should be confirmed locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-60.8865,14.4675,155</coordinates></Point>
