    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Khardung La / Nubra MTB (Ladakh, IN) [vehicle drop, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Extreme-altitude descent from one of Ladakh's great passes</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The classic objective is a supported ride from the Khardung La road pass into the Indus or Nubra side, combining a very long high-altitude road descent with optional rough tracks and village routes. It is an expedition ride, not continuous singletrack or a bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Use a licensed local guide and support vehicle from Leh. Current road permits, checkpoints and route restrictions must be verified; independent foreign travel rules can change.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; The pass is above 5,300 m. Acclimatize in Leh first and treat altitude illness, cold, traffic and remote rescue as serious hazards.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Usually May-September, entirely dependent on snow clearance, road status and military or civil restrictions.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Leh</td><td>Guide vehicle</td><td>~2h to pass</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://leh.nic.in/tourism/adventures/">District Leh adventure tourism guide</a>, which lists Khardung La and Nubra among its mountain-bike areas.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>77.6046,34.2783,5358</coordinates></Point>
