  <Placemark>
    <name>Da Lat Pine Forest MTB (Vietnam) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Da Lat 1,480 m - Central Highlands pine-forest riding hub</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The spiritual home of mountain biking in Vietnam: French hill-station town, spring weather all year, and pine forest and lakes in every direction. The known lines are the Crazy 8, 37 km and the most physically demanding ride here, running from wide dirt tracks into technical singletrack through pine forest past farms and lakes; the Linh Son Pagoda loop, a moderate 21 km through the forest; and the dirt roads around the lakes east of town that narrow into singletrack. There is no signed gravity bike park - these are linked dirt roads and natural trails, best ridden with somebody who knows them.<br/><small>Nothing is drawn here: an mtb-tag sweep of the Da Lat plateau returns zero features.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Rent locally or book a guide and vehicle transfer from Da Lat - operators run Giant and Trek hardtails and full-suspension bikes. Bidoup-Nui Ba and the other protected areas have their own access rules.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 December; closed from 1 May. Best December-April in the dry season; May-November rain makes the red dirt and roots slippery, though guided rides run year-round when conditions allow.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/>
    <small>1,400-1,700 m, so it stays cool while the coast bakes.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Da Lat centre</td><td>Bike / shuttle</td><td>~25 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Da Lat airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://ptv-vietnam.com/adventure-travel/crazy-8-mountain-biking.html">Phat Tire Ventures on the Crazy 8</a>, <a href="https://localvietnam.com/blog/cycling-mountain-biking-in-dalat/">Local Vietnam's Dalat route guide</a> and <a href="https://vietnam.travel/things-to-do/8-things-to-do-in-dalat">Vietnam Tourism</a>. Pin moved onto the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/369486906">Da Lat</a> city node (369486906), measured at 1,478 m; the previous coordinate was rounded to 108.44,12.03 and sat 10 km north of town. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
