  <Placemark>
    <name>Jarvso Bergscykel Park (Sweden) [lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Dedicated Swedish downhill park with strong progression</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Purpose-built green, blue, red and black downhill lines combine smooth berms and jumps with rougher forest technical terrain. Registration is required before riding, with rental and instruction at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Lift-served bike park; purchase a bike pass and complete the rider registration.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Published 2026 season: 14 May-1 November, daily 22 May-30 August, then Friday-Sunday plus autumn holidays. <br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:00<br/><small>Published standard hours; some Fridays and Saturdays extend to 17:00.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Stockholm</td><td>Train / car</td><td>~3h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://jarvsobergscykelpark.se/en/info/opening-hours/">official 2026 opening hours</a>.</i> Pin corrected to the valley station of the Toppliften chairlift (OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/231539171">way 231539171</a>), measured at 177 m: the pin sat 515 m east of the lift base, below the hill; Jarvso's 115 graded ways descend to the Toppliften and Sydliften stations.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>16.158390,61.713170,177</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">jarvso-bike-park</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh freeride chairlift</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="open_from">05-14</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="closed_from">11-02</mwm:value>
      </mwm:properties>
      <mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
