  <Placemark>
    <name>Afriski Mountain MTB (Lesotho) [no summer lift confirmed]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>High-altitude Maloti Mountain riding above 3,000 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Natural and built lines around Afriski include short flow and downhill trails such as Break Back Mountain and Bosman's Way, with broader highland tracks extending toward Mahlasela Pass. Thin air, rock and severe weather make even short rides demanding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No summer bike uplift is currently confirmed. Pedal, arrange resort transport or ride as part of an organized event; do not assume the winter ski lift carries bikes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best September-May outside the main snow season. Storms, snow and high winds can occur at any time.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Butha-Buthe</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h</td></tr><tr><td>Johannesburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~5h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.visitlesotho.org.ls/place-to-visit/highlands-ski-route">Visit Lesotho</a> and current mapped Afriski trails. Check border, road and resort status.</i>]]></description>
