  <Placemark>
    <name>Sunrise Bike Park (Arizona) [63 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sunrise Park base 2851 m - valley station of the Spirit Ridge Quad, White Mountains, Arizona</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Arizona's only lift-served downhill riding: 32 trails from the top of Sunrise Mountain across four grades, on one of the tallest mountains in the state. Trail names come from the White Mountain Apache Tribe, who own and run the resort - Jaage', Shush (Bear), Ba'cho (Wolf) - alongside Bonito, Cartoon Forest, Easy Out and Lower Fungus. At 2851 m the base is high enough to escape the desert heat entirely.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Spirit Ridge Quad and connecting lifts. Adult lift tickets 63 USD a day or 40 USD for a half day. Specialized rentals at the base; helmets required, full-face and pads recommended and available to rent.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Friday to Sunday 10:00-18:00 in spring, then seven days a week from Memorial Day through the summer and into late October.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Pinetop-Lakeside</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Show Low</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Phoenix</td><td>Car</td><td>~4 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://sunrise.ski/summer/downhill-mountain-biking/">Sunrise Park Resort - downhill mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://sunrise.ski/summer/tickets/">Sunrise Park Resort - summer tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
