  <Placemark>
    <name>Lake Leatherwood Gravity Project (Arkansas) [shuttle fee]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lake Leatherwood Park 312 m - gravity project trailhead, Eureka Springs, Arkansas</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Seven downhill lines of about a mile each in a city park above Eureka Springs, and the spread is unusually complete for the size: smooth flowing trails for beginners, technical rocky descents for intermediates, and big jumps and drops at the expert end. Two stone platforms at the top serve as the launch pads for every line.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - shuttle.</b> A shuttle runs riders and bikes to the top for a fee; the trails themselves are in a public city park. Slaughter Trail Guides run the shuttle service.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The riding season, roughly spring to late autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Eureka Springs</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bentonville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Fayetteville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.eurekaparks.com/lake-leatherwood-bike-park">Eureka Springs Parks - Lake Leatherwood Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.oztrails.com/trail/lake-leatherwood/">OZ Trails - Lake Leatherwood</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
