  <Placemark>
    <name>China Peak Bike Park (California) [60 USD - closing]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>China Peak base 2151 m - valley station of Chair 1, Lakeshore, California</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/><b>The bike park is closing permanently at the end of the 2026 summer season</b> after fifteen years, a decision the operator put down to finances and rising insurance costs. In its final season it runs on a handful of dates only. The park itself is 26 trails over 21 miles in the Sierra above Huntington Lake, all served by a single chairlift.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chair 1 serves the whole network. Adult tickets 60 USD, valid a full day 09:00-16:00, with half days from 12:30 sold on site only.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/><b>Final season 2026, on selected dates only.</b> Check before travelling - the park will not reopen after this summer.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Fresno</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr><tr><td>Shaver Lake</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.skichinapeak.com/mountain-biking-scenic-chair-rides">China Peak Mountain Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.singletracks.com/mtb-trails/2026-continues-to-be-rough-on-resorts-as-another-bike-park-closes/">Singletracks - China Peak bike park closing</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
