  <Placemark>
    <name>Snow Valley Bike Park (California) [from 25 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Snow Valley base 2047 m - valley station of the Snow Valley Express, Running Springs, California</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Seven miles of trail in the San Bernardino National Forest, rebuilt into a genuine downhill park since Alterra took the resort over in 2023. The range runs from a meandering beginner trail through intermediates to black-diamond terrain. The Snow Valley Express is 4636 ft long and carries four riders a chair, the most in southern California.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Snow Valley Express. Tickets from 25 USD; a Quad Pack gives direct-to-lift access here and at Snow Summit for about 39 USD a day, and season passes run 109-399 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Select dates through the summer - check the calendar before driving up.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Running Springs</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>San Bernardino</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Los Angeles</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bigbearmountainresort.com/mountain-biking">Snow Valley and Summit Bike Parks</a> and <a href="https://www.bigbearmountainresort.com/mountain-biking/lift-tickets">Snow Valley + Summit Bike Park - lift tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
