  <Placemark>
    <name>Snowmass Bike Park (Colorado) [66 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Snowmass Base Village 2586 m - valley station of the Elk Camp Gondola, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>50 miles of trail and close to 3000 ft of vertical from Elk Camp back down to Base Village - the most vertical of any lift-served park in Colorado, with 25 miles of it purpose-built downhill. Valhalla is the original freeride line, 2.8 miles through aspen forest dropping 1400 ft over jumps, set-ups and wooden features. Vapor starts highest, off the Elk Camp chairlift, and is berm after berm through open meadow. At the hard end sit double blacks like Animal Crackers; at the easy end, greens like Verde.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Elk Camp Gondola and the Elk Camp chairlift both carry bikes, and one ticket covers both. Adult day ticket 66 USD, three days 158 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Daily from the third week of June to Labor Day, then weekends to the end of September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Snowmass Village</td><td>Walk</td><td>At the base</td></tr><tr><td>Aspen</td><td>Car / free bus</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~4 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.aspensnowmass.com/visit/activities/summer/biking/snowmass-bike-park">Aspen Snowmass - Snowmass Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.aspensnowmass.com/visit/activities/summer/biking/snowmass-bike-park/tickets-and-passes">Snowmass Bike Park - tickets and passes</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
