  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Steamboat Bike Park (Colorado) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Steamboat base 2104 m - valley station of the gondola serving the bike park, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 50 miles of downhill and freeride terrain on 2200 ft of lift-served vertical, all reached from a single high-speed gondola. Tenderfoot is the trail that defines the place for most visitors - 4.1 miles, the longest in the park and an easy cruise that lets riders who have never used a chairlift with a bike work out what they are doing. Above it the grades stack up quickly.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The gondola carries riders and bikes. Bike-park lift tickets are sold on the resort's tickets page; rental from the on-mountain shop runs about 89 USD for three hours or 119 USD for the day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-June to late September. Gondola replacement work has been under way at the top of the mountain, so check what is running before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Steamboat Springs</td><td>Car / free bus</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.steamboat.com/plan-your-trip/bike-park">Steamboat Resort - bike park</a> and <a href="https://www.steamboat.com/plan-your-trip/bike-park-tickets">Steamboat Resort - bike park lift tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
