  <Placemark>
    <name>Trestle Bike Park - Winter Park (Colorado) [89 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Winter Park base 2768 m - valley station of the Trestle Bike Park lifts, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 40 miles of lift-served downhill across dozens of trails, and the park that more or less set the template for American bike parks. The progression is the point: green flow at the bottom of the mountain, then blues that add jumps and berms, then black and double-black lines with rock gardens, drops and big built features. The Boulevard is the longest single descent at 1587 ft of drop.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Gondola plus the Olympia and Explorer lifts, all bike-carrying. Adult day ticket 89 USD at the window or 74 USD bought at least 48 hours ahead; kids 64 USD, 59 USD in advance. A Trestle 2-Pack works out at 55 USD a day. Season pass 494 USD adult, 404 USD ages 13-22, 299 USD ages 5-12.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Weekends from late spring, then daily from mid-June through to the autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Winter Park town</td><td>Walk / bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car or Winter Park Express train</td><td>~1 h 45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.trestlebikepark.com/daily-tickets/">Trestle Bike Park - daily tickets</a> and <a href="https://www.winterparkresort.com/things-to-do/activities/mountain-biking">Winter Park Resort - mountain biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
