  <Placemark>
    <name>Vail Bike Park (Colorado) [65 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Golden Peak 2511 m - valley station of the Riva Bahn Express, Vail Bike Park, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>45 lift-served trails with more than 22,000 ft of total descent available across the mountain - one of the biggest lift-served networks anywhere. It leans towards long cross-country-flavoured descents rather than pure park laps: the intermediate Grand Traverse runs over 5 miles from just below the top of the Eagle Bahn Gondola, and the 2.3-mile Golden Gate drops around 1000 ft and is one of the gentler singletrack options on the hill.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Eagle Bahn Gondola at Lionshead and the Riva Bahn Express at Golden Peak both haul bikes. Day ticket 65 USD for 13 and over, 45 USD ages 5-12. Note that a bike haul pass is charged separately from a scenic lift ride, and Epic Pass holders still have to buy one.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-June to early October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Vail Village</td><td>Walk / bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.vail.com/explore-the-resort/activities-and-events/summer-activities/mountain-biking.aspx">Vail - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://discovervail.com/things-to-do/mountain-biking/">Discover Vail - mountain biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
