  <Placemark>
    <name>Powder Ridge Bike Park (Connecticut) [14-28 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Powder Ridge base 118 m - valley station of the bike-park chairlift, Middlefield, Connecticut</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Connecticut's first lift-served bike park, opened in 2016. Full-length descents from the summit include Red-tail, Viper, Shredwood, Timberline and Fisher Cat, with Pipe, Copperhead, Rattler and Lift Line as lower-mountain options. Three jump lines - small, medium and large - and a pump track were added in 2018, and there is an airbag for working on tricks.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairlift access to the summit. Tickets have run around 14 USD on Fridays and 28 USD at weekends, with a season pass around 224 USD; the airbag is charged separately at about 15 USD for five jumps. Rentals available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The warmer months.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Middletown</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Hartford</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>New Haven</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://powderridgepark.com/activities/mountain-bike/">Powder Ridge Park - mountain bike</a> and <a href="https://mtbparks.com/Connecticut/310-Powder-Ridge-Bike-Park/View-details.html">MTB Parks - Powder Ridge Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
