  <Placemark>
    <name>Basin Gravity Park - Bogus Basin (Idaho) [49 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bogus Basin base 1884 m - valley station of the Morning Star Express, Idaho</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>14 lift-served trails in three distinct zones, half an hour from downtown Boise, on a non-profit mountain that has put serious effort into building a gravity scene from nothing. The range runs from beginner to pro, and Rabid Badger is one of the largest jump lines in the region.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Morning Star Express high-speed quad, fitted with easy-load bike racks. Day pass 49 USD for 13 and over, 29 USD ages 4-12; twilight passes 29 USD and 19 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-June, snow depending, through to the last weekend in September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Boise</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://bogusbasin.org/your-mountain/things-to-do/summer-activities/mountain-biking/">Bogus Basin - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://bermstyle.com/basin-gravity-bike-park-boise-idaho/">Bermstyle - Basin Gravity Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
