  <Placemark>
    <name>Jiminy Peak Bike Park (Massachusetts) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Jiminy Peak base 380 m - valley station of the Grand Slam chairlift, Hancock, Massachusetts</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Lift-served riding in the Berkshires, and it is honest about who it suits: a mix of singletrack and downhill cruisers best ridden by experienced riders, with full suspension and body armour recommended and helmets required. Not a progression park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Grand Slam chairlift covers the lower mountain whenever the Mountain Adventure Park is open; the Berkshire Express reaches the summit 12:00-16:00 on Saturdays, Sundays and holidays from late June to early September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer, with summit access at weekends from late June to Labor Day.<br/>Daily opening hours: 12:00-16:00 (summit)<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Pittsfield</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Albany</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.jiminypeak.com/Summer/Attractions/Mountain-Biking/">Jiminy Peak - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://berkshiresoutside.org/place/jiminy-peak-hancock-ma/">Berkshires Outside - Jiminy Peak</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
