  <Placemark>
    <name>Spirit Mountain Bike Park - Duluth (Minnesota) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Spirit Mountain base 219 m - valley station of the bike-park chairlift, Duluth, Minnesota</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Minnesota's main lift-served park, 12 downhill trails above Lake Superior with the lake in view for most of the descent, and it plugs straight into Duluth's much larger trail network. Happy Camper is the gentle way in - 4700 ft of machine-built flow, all rollers and berms. Candyland runs 1.5 miles of beginner-to-intermediate flow with large berms, tabletops and hip jumps. Smorgasbord is the step up, a mile of intermediate freeride with big berms, jumps, a drop and rock gardens.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift serves the park, running Thursday to Sunday on the full summer schedule; early and late season hours vary, so check before travelling. Tickets on the resort's site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late spring to mid-autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Duluth</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Minneapolis</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://spiritmt.com/summer/mountain-biking/">Spirit Mountain - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.coggs.com/spirit-mtn">COGGS - Spirit Mountain</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
