  <Placemark>
    <name>Disco Bike Park - Discovery (Montana) [20 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Discovery base 1744 m - Disco Bike Park, Georgetown Lake, Montana</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A small flow-style park on the back side of Discovery, dropping about 1050 vertical feet, built for every level and with the option of keeping the wheels down or taking the wall rides, bridges, jumps, logs and drops built into it. There is a pump course near the base for children starting out - the park explicitly welcomes riders from about seven upwards.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift serves the park. A single ride is 20 USD; if you would rather pedal up, trail access alone is 10 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Saturdays and Sundays 11:00-17:00 from mid-May to mid-October, weather depending. <b>The bike park is closed for the whole of August.</b><br/>Daily opening hours: 11:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Philipsburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Anaconda</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Missoula</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.skidiscovery.com/bike-park/">Discovery Ski Area - bike park</a> and <a href="https://mbaction.com/montanas-discovery-ski-area-to-open-downhill-trails-this-summer/">Mountain Bike Action - Discovery downhill trails</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
