  <Placemark>
    <name>Legacy Bike Park (Montana) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Legacy Bike Park 1600 m - shuttle base near Blacktail Mountain, Lakeside, Montana</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A private park established in 2021 between Flathead Lake and Glacier National Park, built around shuttle laps: technical, flow and downhill trails running from gentle beginner lines to serious descents, plus a couple of pump tracks. The operation is as much a venue as a trail network - trainings, competitions, live music and a campground.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - shuttle.</b> A bike shuttle runs to keep laps going. A ticket is required to enter and must be bought in advance to get the gate code. Primitive camping on 36 reservable sites at 30 USD a night.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The summer season. Road access has been shared with Blacktail at the start of recent seasons, so check before driving in.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lakeside</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Kalispell</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Whitefish</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://legacybikepark.com/">Legacy Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://legacybikepark.com/pages/faq">Legacy Bike Park - FAQ</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
