  <Placemark>
    <name>Waterville Valley Bike Park (New Hampshire) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Snow's Mountain 471 m - valley station of the Snow's Mountain chairlift, Waterville Valley, New Hampshire</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The lift-served park runs off the Snow's Mountain chairlift and opens onto over 50 miles of trail across the valley, from flowing greens to steep technical black diamonds. The lift-served side leans beginner and intermediate with a few harder sections; the wider valley network is where the cross-country riding is.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Snow's Mountain chairlift. Tickets and a full rental fleet - trail, road, fat and full-suspension bikes - at the Adventure Center, which also does repairs.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Weekends 10:00-15:45 from late May to mid-June, daily 10:00-16:45 from mid-June to early September, then weekends and holidays 10:00-15:45 to late October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Campton</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Concord</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.waterville.com/adventure-center">Waterville Valley - Adventure Center</a> and <a href="https://www.visitwatervillevalley.com/biking">Visit Waterville Valley - biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
