  <Placemark>
    <name>Angel Fire Bike Park (New Mexico) [62-81 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Angel Fire base 2612 m - valley station of the Chile Express, New Mexico</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>54 trails and over 60 miles of downhill on 2000 ft of vertical - the largest bike park in the Rocky Mountains, and the one that put lift-served riding on the map in the southwest. Easy Street is the long way down at 5.1 miles; above it the terrain runs from beginner cruisers through technical descents and jump lines. You drop in at 10,650 ft, so the first lap is an altitude adjustment whatever your fitness.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Chile Express, which Angel Fire bills as the longest and fastest summer quad chairlift in the world. Adult tickets 62-81 USD depending on the date.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-May to the end of October, 09:00-16:00.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Taos</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Santa Fe</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr><tr><td>Albuquerque</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.angelfireresort.com/activities/summer-activities/bike-park/">Angel Fire Resort - bike park</a> and <a href="https://www.newmexico.org/listing/angel-fire-bike-park/9099/">New Mexico True - Angel Fire Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
