  <Placemark>
    <name>Gore Mountain Bike Park (New York) [26 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gore base lodge 463 m - valley station of the Northwoods Gondola, North Creek, New York</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A 14-mile lift-served network in the Adirondacks descending 1700 vertical feet, and the character shifts as you go: dirt roads and switchbacks, open alpine ground near the top, then singletrack in the trees. State-run, and the ticket is cheap for what you get.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Northwoods Gondola and Adirondack Express. Skyride tickets 26 USD for ages 13-64, 18 USD for ages 7-12 and 65 and over, 20 USD military, free for under-7s, and they cover all-day access to the open lift. Helmets and a signed waiver are required, and e-bikes are not allowed on the trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Opening weekend in early July, then Thursday to Sunday 10:00-16:00 to the end of August, and weekends to mid-October.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>North Creek</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Lake George</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Albany</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://goremountain.com/tickets-passes/summer-attractions/">Gore Mountain - summer attractions</a> and <a href="https://visitnorthcreek.org/project/gore-mt-summerfall-activities/">Visit North Creek - Gore Mountain summer activities</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
