  <Placemark>
    <name>Mt. Bachelor Bike Park - Bend (Oregon) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>West Village 1941 m - valley station of the Pine Marten Express, Mt. Bachelor, Oregon</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 20 miles of gravity trail, and the ground changes completely as you descend: the upper mountain off the Pine Marten lift is intermediate-to-advanced riding across open volcanic terrain, all cinder and lava rock, before dropping into forest lower down. Little Pine is the beginner area and is a genuinely gentle introduction to lift-served riding. Central Oregon's main downhill destination, with the enormous Bend trail network half an hour away.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Pine Marten Express, a nine-minute ride. A bike-park ticket or season pass is required for lift access; check the resort's current rate.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late June to early October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bend</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Portland</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mtbachelor.com/the-mountain/bike-park/info/">Mt. Bachelor - bike park</a> and <a href="https://traveloregon.com/things-to-do/destinations/parks-forests-wildlife-areas/mt-bachelor-bike-park/">Travel Oregon - Mt. Bachelor Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
