  <Placemark>
    <name>Timberline Bike Park - Mount Hood (Oregon) [50 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Jeff Flood Express base 1478 m - Timberline Bike Park, Mount Hood, Oregon</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A purpose-built park on the lower slopes of Mount Hood below the historic Timberline Lodge, opened in phases from 2023 and still the newest lift-served riding in Oregon. Two green beginner trails, a handful of blues split between technical and freeride-oriented, and several technical blacks, all off the Jeff Flood Express.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Jeff Flood Express chairlift. Day ticket 50 USD for 13 and over, 40 USD for 12 and under; season pass 249 USD and 199 USD, which also includes two free days each at Mt. Bachelor, Grand Targhee, Schweitzer and Whitefish.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Opens in early July, weather permitting, and runs Wednesday to Sunday 10:30-17:00, until 19:00 on Fridays.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:30-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Government Camp</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Portland</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://timberlinelodge.com/things-to-do/mountain-biking/">Timberline Lodge - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://traveloregon.com/things-to-do/destinations/parks-forests-wildlife-areas/timberline-bike-park/">Travel Oregon - Timberline Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
