  <Placemark>
    <name>Windrock Bike Park (Tennessee) [150 USD 3-day shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Windrock Park 322 m - shuttle base for the Windrock Bike Park, Oliver Springs, Tennessee</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>15 miles of downhill-only shuttle trails inside a 73,000-acre off-road park. The trails are machine-built but uniformly aggressive - rated difficult to extreme and aimed squarely at expert riders. Not a progression park; come knowing how to ride.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - shuttle.</b> Buses run every 10 minutes carrying 25 riders and bikes, 10:00-17:00, five days a week (currently closed Tuesday and Wednesday) with weekend operation year round. A three-day shuttle pass is 150 USD and a season pass 450 USD for 1 May to 31 October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round, with shuttles at weekends outside the main season.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Oak Ridge</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Knoxville</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://windrockbikepark.com/">Windrock Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://windrockbikepark.com/pages/trails">Windrock Bike Park - trails</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
