  <Placemark>
    <name>Solitude Bike Park (Utah) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Moonbeam base 2474 m - valley station of the Moonbeam Express, Solitude, Utah</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A new park, opened in autumn 2023, with seven purpose-built downhill trails designed by Gravity Logic and more than 25 miles of singletrack across the resort in summer. Big Cottonwood Canyon puts it at proper altitude, so it stays cool when the Salt Lake valley below is baking.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Everything is reached from the Moonbeam Express. A summer pass at 399 USD covers unlimited bike haul, hiking and scenic rides; Twilight Nights give bike-park access for 25 USD. Trek and Norco rentals for adults and children at the Moonbeam base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Daily 10:00-18:00 from mid-June to mid-August, with lifts running to 20:00 on Tuesday and Thursday Twilight Nights; then Thursday to Sunday from mid-August and weekends only in September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Salt Lake City</td><td>Car up Big Cottonwood Canyon</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Park City</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.solitudemountain.com/things-to-do/solitude-bike-park">Solitude Mountain Resort - bike park</a> and <a href="https://www.solitudemountain.com/plan-your-trip/bike-park-tickets">Solitude - bike lift tickets and season pass</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
