  <Placemark>
    <name>Powder Mountain Bike Park (Utah) [from 25 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Timberline base 2410 m - Powder Mountain bike park, Eden, Utah</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>1268 ft of vertical and over 10 miles of trail, all of it high - Powder Mountain sits well above 8000 ft, so the riding stays cool through the summer. The park is young and still being built out, with a stated goal of eleven or more trails as the flow network and terrain features expand.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Hidden Lake chairlift serves the bike park, Thursday to Sunday, with tickets from 25 USD. Bike hire with helmet and pads from 60 USD a day. Lift-served biking has been suspended in past summers for on-mountain construction, so confirm it is running before you drive up.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly mid-June to September, Thursday to Sunday.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Eden / Ogden Valley</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Ogden</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Salt Lake City</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://powdermountain.com/blog/lift-accessed-mountain-bike-operations">Powder Mountain - lift-accessed mountain bike operations</a> and <a href="https://www.skiutah.com/blog/authors/lexi/guide-to-mountain-biking-at-powder/">Ski Utah - guide to mountain biking at Powder Mountain</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
