  <Placemark>
    <name>Brown County State Park (Indiana) [7-9 USD gate + 5 USD trail]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Brown County State Park 258 m - the Midwest's benchmark natural trail network</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>An IMBA Bronze-Level Ride Center, designated an IMBA Epic trail system in 2011 and still the reference ride in the Midwest. Around 35 miles of purpose-cut singletrack in the steep-sided ravines of Indiana's "Little Smokies": the operator counts five beginner trails, two intermediate, three advanced and three expert. Hesitation Point (2.1 mi, advanced) drops off the park's best-known overlook, Bobcat Loop (2.0 mi) is the expert line, and Hobbs Hollow, Aynes, Green Valley, Limekiln and Walnut fill in between. This is short, punchy Midwestern riding - the whole park lies between about 200 and 310 m - so the reward is trail quality and flow rather than sustained descent.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; every trail is pedalled. Two fees stack: a park gate permit at 7 USD for Indiana vehicles or 9 USD out of state (50 / 70 USD annual), plus an Indiana off-road cycling permit at 5 USD a day or 20 USD a year, required on every trail above green level and sold at the gatehouse, the park office or online.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Indiana clay: the trails close when they are wet, and riding them soft causes lasting damage. Check the park's trail status line before driving.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round in a typical year, with closures whenever the ground is wet or thawing. Summer is reliably dry; spring is the worst of it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Indianapolis</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h05</td></tr><tr><td>Louisville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h40</td></tr><tr><td>Cincinnati</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://browncountymtb.org/trails">Brown County Mountain Biking</a>, <a href="https://www.browncountystatepark.net/mountain_biking_trails.htm">Brown County State Park trail and fee pages</a> and OpenStreetMap. Fees and trail status change; verify before travelling.</i>]]></description>
