  <Placemark>
    <name>Tsali Recreation Area (North Carolina) [2 USD, alternating days]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Tsali 668 m - four loops above Fontana Lake, in the Nantahala National Forest</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A long-standing southern Appalachian classic: about 40 miles of singletrack and old logging road on a peninsula between Fontana Lake and the Great Smoky Mountains. Four stacked loops, all rated moderately difficult - Right Loop (13.9 mi), Left Loop (11.9 mi), Mouse Branch (8.7 mi) and Thompson (7.3 mi). The riding is flowing contour singletrack with lake and Smokies views rather than gravity: expect rolling terrain and long traverses, not sustained descent.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. A 2 USD day-use fee is collected at the trailhead. Everything is pedalled from the one car park.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Bikes and horses alternate by day, and getting this wrong means a wasted drive. Right and Left Loops are open to bikes Monday, Wednesday, Friday and Sunday; Mouse Branch and Thompson on Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday. The schedule varies by season - check the Forest Service listing before you go.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round in a typical year; the trails are lower and drier than the Pisgah high country, but they close after heavy rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bryson City</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Asheville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h40</td></tr><tr><td>Knoxville</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/r08/northcarolina/recreation/tsali-recreation-area">USDA Forest Service - Tsali Recreation Area</a> and OpenStreetMap. The bike/horse rotation and fees change; verify with the Forest Service.</i>]]></description>
