  <Placemark>
    <name>Cuyuna Country State Recreation Area (Minnesota) [7 USD parking]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Miner's Mountain Rally Center 374 m - red-dirt riding on the Cuyuna Iron Range</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>An IMBA Silver-Level Ride Center and the Midwest's most distinctive network: about 50 miles of purpose-built trail across some 800 acres of abandoned iron-ore mine, threaded between flooded pits with startlingly blue water and built on red mine tailings that drain fast and hold a tyre. More than 30 named routes, from green flow and a skills area through rolling berms and rollers to steeper gravity-oriented lines with rock features and jumps. The relief is the honest limit - the whole range lies between roughly 365 and 430 m, so these are short, repeatable descents rather than long ones, and OpenStreetMap holds 64 named runs of which only one has enough drop to draw as a descent.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Riding and walking the trails is free, but a Minnesota State Parks vehicle permit is required to park at the trailheads: 7 USD a day or 35 USD a year. The Rally Center at Miner's Mountain is the main hub; Mahnomen, Sagamore, Portsmouth and Yawkey are the other units.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; The single track closes to everyone, on foot or bike, the moment it rains, and reopens only when the tread has firmed up - usually a few hours, longer when it is cold. It also closes during the spring freeze-thaw and for the November firearms deer season. Check the Cuyuna Lakes MTB conditions page before driving.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly May to October for dirt, plus a winter fat-bike season on groomed trail. Closed through the spring thaw and for about two and a half weeks of firearms deer season each November.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Brainerd</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Minneapolis</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr><tr><td>Duluth</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.cuyunalakesmtb.com/seasonalguidlines">Cuyuna Lakes MTB seasonal guidelines and conditions</a>, <a href="https://www.dnr.state.mn.us/state_parks/cuyuna/mtnbiking.html">Minnesota DNR</a> and OpenStreetMap. Closures change daily; check before travelling.</i>]]></description>
