  <Placemark>
    <name>Allegrippis Trails - Raystown Lake (Pennsylvania) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Allegrippis skills park 293 m - 36 miles of IMBA-built flow above Raystown Lake</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Designed by mountain bikers and built by IMBA on US Army Corps of Engineers land, and widely held to be some of the best flow trail in North America. About 36 miles of stacked-loop singletrack: where most Pennsylvania riding is rough, rooty and rocky, Allegrippis is smooth, fast and bermed, packed with rollers and long swooping traverses above the lake. Ray's Revenge, Sidewinder, Sleek Dog, Dirt Surfer, Whale Tail, Quick Drink, Berry Patch, Old Logger's and Locomotive make up the core, with green, blue and black skills-park lines at the trailhead. OpenStreetMap has it unusually well tagged - most trails carry an IMBA grade and half of them are signed one-way.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no fee. Everything is pedalled from the Allegrippis trailhead near Seven Points.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Most of the network is signed one-way. Ride it in the marked direction - it is what makes a flow system this fast safe to share.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable roughly April to November, with August the busiest month. The trails close when wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Huntingdon</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Harrisburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h40</td></tr><tr><td>Pittsburgh</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h40</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://raystown.org/listing/allegrippis-trails-at-raystown-lake/276/">Raystown Lake visitor bureau</a>, <a href="https://trailism.com/epic-ride-8-allegrippis-raystown-pennsylvania/">Trailism</a> and OpenStreetMap. Verify trail status before travelling.</i>
    <br/><small>No descent lines are drawn here. All 36 named ways in OpenStreetMap were measured against the digital elevation model and the trails themselves top out at about 2% average gradient over the whole loop - Ray's Revenge runs 6.7 km for 12 m of net drop. Allegrippis is a rolling flow network between roughly 240 and 415 m, not a gravity hill; the only lines with real descent in the bbox are Army Corps service roads. This row is closed on terrain, not on sources.</small>]]></description>
