  <Placemark>
    <name>Walden&#x27;s Ridge Park (Signal Mountain, Tennessee) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Walden's Ridge Park upper car park 458 m - top of the Chattanooga area's gravity trails</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The first purpose-built, progressive downhill trails in the Chattanooga region, opened in early 2023 after seven years of work by Wild Trails, the Town of Signal Mountain and their partners, to a plan drawn up with IMBA. Around 10 miles of trail across 200 acres on the eastern flank of Signal Mountain, with the emphasis on intermediate and advanced bike-only gravity lines, and about 800 feet - some 230 m - of elevation to work with between the upper and lower car parks. Beginner through expert, plus bouldering, running and hiking trails on the same ground.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no entry fee. Park at the upper lot and drop, or pedal up from the lower lot at 227 m; the park is laid out so both work.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; A young park still being built out, and the gravity trails are bike-only and directional. Check Wild Trails for current trail status and any build closures.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round in a typical year; the Cumberland Plateau stays mild, but the trails close when wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Chattanooga</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Nashville</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr><tr><td>Atlanta</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://wildtrails.org/waldens-ridge-park/">Wild Trails</a>, <a href="https://www.waldensridgepark.com/">Walden's Ridge Park</a> and OpenStreetMap. Trail status changes; verify before travelling.</i>]]></description>
