  <Placemark>
    <name>Bolton Valley Bike Park (Vermont) [40 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bolton Valley 656 m - valley station of the Vista Quad, Vermont</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around two dozen downhill trails plus several climbing routes, over 900 ft of descent from Vista Peak, half an hour from Burlington. The park reopened in 2021 after a ten-year hiatus and the rebuild covers the whole range - beginner flow, intermediate jump and flow lines, and steep fall-line New England tech for experienced riders.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Lift service to the top of Vista Peak. Adult lift ticket 40 USD, 30 USD for 17 and under; downhill season pass from 199 USD. Wednesday to Friday from noon to dusk, all day Saturday and Sunday.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late spring to early autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Burlington</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Montpelier</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.boltonvalley.com/summer/mountain-biking/mtb-day-tickets/">Bolton Valley - bike park lift tickets</a> and <a href="https://vmba.org/plan_your_ride/bolton-valley-resort/">VMBA - Bolton Valley Resort</a>. Pin on the valley station of the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/43746400">Vista Quad</a> (way 43746400), measured at 656 m; it climbs 292 m to Vista Peak at 948 m. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-72.848940,44.420400,656</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
