  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Burke Mountain Bike Park (Vermont) [48 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Burke base 372 m - valley station of the Sherburne Express, East Burke, Vermont</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>24 trails over 25 miles with 2115 ft of vertical, ten of them lift-served, and a long reputation as one of the better-built parks in the East. The Sherburne Express covers most of it; a summit shuttle van reaches three expert-only descents from the very top. Kingdom Trails, the pedal network next door in East Burke, is a separate operation and a separate pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Sherburne Express chairlift, plus a summit shuttle van. Adult lift ticket 48 USD; a single shuttle ride 10 USD, or unlimited shuttles added to a day pass for 15 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Weekends from early June, then Thursday to Sunday 10:00-18:00 from mid-June.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>East Burke</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>St Johnsbury</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Burlington</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.skiburke.com/bike-park">Burke Mountain Resort - bike park</a> and <a href="https://mbaction.com/burke-mountain-bike-park-opening-2026/">Mountain Bike Action - Burke Mountain bike park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-71.916026,44.587327,372</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
