  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Killington Bike Park (Vermont) [70 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Snowshed base 671 m - valley station of the Snowshed Express, Killington, Vermont</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>35 trails, 30 miles and 1972 vertical feet - the biggest lift-served park in the Northeast. Snowshed at the base holds the beginner terrain and plenty of intermediates; the K-1 gondola runs 1.25 miles to the summit of Killington Peak at 4241 ft, the second-highest peak in Vermont and the highest lift-served summit in the state, where the terrain turns properly big-mountain by East Coast standards.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Three lifts carry bikes: the Snowshed Express Quad, the Ramshead Express Quad and the K-1 Express Gondola. Adult day ticket from 70 USD, youth 17 and under from 53 USD; two days 119/91 USD and three days 136/104 USD. Full trail, freeride and downhill rental fleet at the Snowshed Lodge bike shop.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Snowshed opens Memorial Day weekend, Ramshead from mid-June and K-1 from early July, weekends early on and daily through the summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Rutland</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h</td></tr><tr><td>New York</td><td>Car</td><td>~4 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://killington.com/bike-park-tickets">Killington Bike Park - tickets</a> and <a href="https://killington.com/bike-trail-map">Killington Bike Park - trail map</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-72.795870,43.625220,671</coordinates></Point>
