  <Placemark>
    <name>Stratton Bike Park (Vermont) [55 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Stratton base 607 m - valley station of the Stratton gondola, Vermont</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 10 miles of downhill across more than 15 trails, from chill greens to genuine black diamonds, and the park has kept adding routes since it opened in 2019. The spread of difficulty is deliberate - it is built so that new and experienced riders can ride together rather than split up at the top.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The gondola carries bikes to the summit; with a bike lift ticket you can also ride up without the bike for the view or the Fire Tower walk. Day ticket about 55 USD; adult season pass 249 USD, junior 199 USD. A VMBA annual membership at 60 USD includes lift tickets to several Vermont downhill parks including this one. Tickets from The HUB next to the gondola base or the Junior Mountain Sports School.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-June to mid-October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Manchester</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h</td></tr><tr><td>New York</td><td>Car</td><td>~4 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.stratton.com/things-to-do/activities/stratton-bike-park">Stratton Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.stratton.com/plan-your-trip/bike-park">Stratton Mountain Resort - bike park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
