  <Placemark>
    <name>Bryce Bike Park (Virginia) [35 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bryce base 386 m - valley station of the bike-park quad, Basye, Virginia</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eight quad-accessed trails - one green, four blue and four black - in the Shenandoah Valley, ranging from short beginner runs to top-to-bottom descents over two miles. Sundowner is the friendly one; Hooch is the double-black jump line. Small, custom built, and well regarded for how much it fits into modest vertical.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A quad chairlift. Lift tickets 35 USD. Trek downhill, enduro and children's bikes plus protective gear for hire at the park, with Terra Method certified instructors. The lodge has a shop, a restaurant and bar, and hoses for washing down afterwards.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The warmer months.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Harrisonburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Winchester</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Washington DC</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://bryceresort.com/summer/bike-park">Bryce Resort - downhill mountain bike park</a> and <a href="https://visitshenandoahcounty.com/listing/bryce-resort-downhill-mountain-bike-park/433/">Visit Shenandoah County - Bryce bike park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
