  <Placemark>
    <name>Massanutten Bike Park (Virginia) [40 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Creekside base 550 m - valley station of the Creekside lift, Massanutten, Virginia</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two clearly separated halves. The Low-Side off the Creekside lift is flowing, gentle green terrain with skills features, built for beginners and first-time downhill riders. The High-Side, reached by the Peak Express, gets steeper, faster and more technical - this is where the park earns its reputation as the best lift-served riding in Virginia.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Creekside lift and the Peak Express. A downhill bike park pass is 40 USD. The resort's separate Western Slope pedal network is a different ticket at 10 USD a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Bike park and shop open Wednesday, Saturday and Sunday 10:00-16:00, weather dependent.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Harrisonburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Charlottesville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 15</td></tr><tr><td>Washington DC</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.massresort.com/play/mountain-biking/bike-park/">Massanutten Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://mtbparks.com/Virginia/306-Massanutten-Bike-Park/View-details.html?mapinfo=1&tmpl=component">MTB Parks - Massanutten Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
