  <Placemark>
    <name>The Summit Bike Park - Snoqualmie (Washington) [from 46 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Summit Central 940 m - valley station of the Silver Fir Express, Snoqualmie Pass, Washington</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 10 miles of trail, all off one chairlift, and it covers a genuine range: about 2 miles of green, a little over 2 miles of blue, and 2.5 miles of black and double-black expert lines with advanced rock features. The character swings from classic flowing Pacific Northwest forest singletrack to rowdy rock slabs - the newest of the region's bike parks and the closest one to Seattle.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Silver Fir Express serves every trail. Tickets from about 46 USD, cheapest in the resort's online store. Rentals, a full repair shop and a bike-park guide service on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly early June to late September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>North Bend</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Seattle</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.summitatsnoqualmie.com/activities/biking">Summit at Snoqualmie - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.summitatsnoqualmie.com/bike-park-tickets-and-passes">Summit Bike Park - tickets and passes</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
