  <Placemark>
    <name>Grand Targhee Bike Park (Wyoming) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Grand Targhee base 2312 m - valley station of the Dreamcatcher lift, Alta, Wyoming</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>17 miles of lift-served downhill on 2200 vertical feet, on the quiet west side of the Tetons. Nice Marmot is the intermediate favourite, two miles of machine-built trail from the summit; Blondie is the opposite - experts only, top-to-bottom fall line. Two lifts, the Dreamcatcher and the Shoshone, serve the park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Dreamcatcher and Shoshone lifts. A bike park lift ticket or season pass is required; rates on the resort's bike park pages.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>July to September, with dates shifting on snow and weather.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Driggs, Idaho</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Jackson</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 45</td></tr><tr><td>Idaho Falls</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.grandtarghee.com/activities-events/activity-finder/bike-park">Grand Targhee - bike park</a> and <a href="https://www.grandtarghee.com/tickets-passes/lift-tickets/bike-park-lift-tickets">Grand Targhee - bike park lift tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
