  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Jackson Hole Bike Park (Wyoming) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Teton Village 1937 m - valley station of the Sweetwater Gondola, Jackson Hole, Wyoming</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>14 trails across the difficulty range on 1200 ft of lift-served vertical, under the Tetons - the setting is as much of the draw as the riding. Lap times are short: the Teewinot chairlift and the Sweetwater Gondola both get you back up quickly.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Sweetwater Gondola and the Teewinot chairlift. Friday Night Bikes gives 20 USD bike park tickets and half-price downhill rentals from 16:00; Sunday Funday runs specials and competitions through the season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-June to early September, 10:00-17:00 Saturday to Thursday and 10:00-18:00 on Fridays.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Teton Village</td><td>Walk</td><td>At the base</td></tr><tr><td>Jackson</td><td>Car / START bus</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.jacksonhole.com/summer-activities/bike-park">Jackson Hole Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.jacksonhole.com/maps/biking-summer">Jackson Hole - summer biking map</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
