  <Placemark>
    <name>Virgin Freeride / Red Bull Rampage Zone [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Red Bull Rampage finish corral 1205 m - the arch and spectator parking on Rampage Center Road, Virgin, Utah</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>This is the Rampage venue itself, not a trail network. The pin sits at the finish corral and arch on Rampage Center Road, with the start gates on the mesa rim 600-900 m to the south and south-east and the riders' compound between them; the site moved here from the original 2001-2004 arena 6.5 km north on Smith Mesa. The competition lines are cut fresh by each rider's dig crew, exist only for the event and are on BLM land that is closed to the public during build and race weeks - they are not public trails and are not drawn here.<br/><br/>
    The one documented public expert descent nearby is <b>Flying Monkey</b>, from the southern rim of Smith Mesa 8 km north of the corral: 2.53 miles of narrow, steep and loose trail with sharp turns, jumps, unavoidable obstacles, sudden drop-offs and extreme exposure, through the same red-desert freeride landscape. Closer in, the only mapped riding is the Windmill and Gander singletrack south of the venue, which is flat blue-graded desert cross-country rather than gravity, so it is left off the map.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal the Mesa Road / Flying Monkey access roads or arrange a vehicle drop where legal; the BLM recommends leaving vehicles before the access road becomes rough.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Flying Monkey is rated extremely difficult by the BLM. It has 20% or steeper grades, crumbling surfaces and places where a mistake could cause serious injury or death. There are no convenient places to stop or turn around.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best from mid-September to mid-May. Avoid wet clay, summer heat and active event or land-management closures.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Virgin</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min up Rampage Center Road</td></tr><tr><td>St George</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Virgin</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~15 min to Mesa Road for Flying Monkey</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.blm.gov/visit/flying-monkey-trail">BLM Flying Monkey trail description, access and safety guidance</a> and <a href="https://www.redbull.com/us-en/events/red-bull-rampage/">Red Bull Rampage event information</a>. Pin on the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/8345824273">Red Bull Rampage Finish Corral/Arch</a> (node 8345824273), on the finish-corral parking (way 898017837) at the edge of Rampage Center Road, measured at 1205 m. The previous pin sat on the outer spectator lot 950 m to the north-east. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-113.167857,37.168886,1205</coordinates></Point>
