  <Placemark>
    <name>Pisgah National Forest [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Black Mountain trailhead 658 m - main gravity access in the Pisgah Ranger District, North Carolina</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Pisgah Ranger District around Brevard holds roughly 69 mountain-bike trails and well over 300 miles of rideable singletrack, and its reputation is for raw, rocky, root-covered ground rather than built flow. Black Mountain, 11 km, opens with a hard climb and then drops into a fast descent full of off-camber roots and chunk. Bennett Gap runs 4.7 km with 430 m of descent against only 75 m of climb along a ridge, with views to Looking Glass Rock and the Avery Creek valley. Farlow Gap is the notorious one - 5 km, double-black, among the steepest and rockiest descents in the forest. Nothing here is groomed; expect wet roots and loose rock as the normal condition.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Free to ride and free to park at most trailheads - you earn the descents on long gravel forest-road climbs.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round. The trails ride wet and greasy through winter and spring, and some sections close seasonally - check the ranger district before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Brevard</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Asheville</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/r08/northcarolina/recreation/pisgah-national-forest">USDA Forest Service - Pisgah National Forest</a> and <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/r08/northcarolina/recreation/trails/bennett-gap-trail">Forest Service - Bennett Gap Trail</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
