  <Placemark>
    <name>Soquel Demonstration State Forest [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Highland Way parking 509 m - entrance to Soquel Demonstration State Forest, California</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A 2681-acre working forest established in 1990 and run by CAL FIRE, and the best-known riding in the Santa Cruz mountains. The Flow Trail, built by the Mountain Bikers of Santa Cruz, is the draw - a machine-built ribbon of big berms, smooth jumps and rollers through the redwoods that rides like a downhill pump track. Braille is its opposite: steep, raw and technical, with drops and jumps, for riders who want the tech rather than the rhythm. Corral, Ridge and Sawpit fill in around them. Long climbs and demanding descents - this is an intermediate-to-advanced forest.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift, and no shuttle service.</b> Free to enter and free to park at the Highland Way lot, but you climb back to the car every lap and the climb is substantial.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round. The redwood soil holds water, so give it time to dry after rain - riding it wet does real damage.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Santa Cruz</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>San Jose</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.fire.ca.gov/what-we-do/natural-resource-management/demonstration-state-forests/soquel-demonstration-state-forest">CAL FIRE - Soquel Demonstration State Forest</a> and <a href="https://santacruztrails.org/trails/soquel-demonstration-state-forest/">Santa Cruz Mountains Trail Stewardship - Soquel Demo</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
