  <Placemark>
    <name>Monarch Crest Trail [commercial shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Monarch Pass 3459 m - shuttle drop for the Monarch Crest point-to-point, Salida, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>An IMBA Epic and one of the best-known point-to-points in North America: 58.5 km with 1744 m of descent against 568 m of climbing, 85 percent singletrack, from a high point of 3646 m down to 2274 m. The name is misleading - the profile looks like a downhill run, but there is close to 900 m of climbing to do at altitude, which makes it a very long and very tough intermediate ride rather than an easy one.<br/><br/>
    Three sections make up the route. The <b>Monarch Crest Trail</b> itself runs the Continental Divide south from Monarch Pass to Marshall Pass, mostly above treeline with the San Juans and Sawatch in view the whole way, then carries on along the Colorado Trail to the Silver Creek turn. <b>Silver Creek</b> is the payoff - 7 km of fast rocky descending. <b>Rainbow Trail</b> finishes it with 18 km of narrow, rolling singletrack that has more climbing in it than riders expect, exiting on dirt road to Highway 285. Average grade is 4 percent, maximum 18 percent.<br/><br/>
    E-bikes are allowed on the first and last ten miles only, and are prohibited on the middle section between Marshall Pass and the start of the Rainbow Trail.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - commercial shuttle.</b> Point-to-point: shuttles leave Salida or Poncha Springs and drop at the Monarch Pass trailhead on US 50, and you finish back down the valley. Several outfits run it through the season; book ahead and verify the current price.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Usually snow covered until around the 4th of July, so July to mid-October. Afternoon thunderstorms are the rule rather than the exception at this altitude, and the route is committing and remote once you leave Monarch Pass - carry layers, food and more water than a 58 km ride would normally need.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Salida</td><td>Car / shuttle to Monarch Pass</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Poncha Springs</td><td>Car / shuttle</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/3671983/monarch-crest-imba-epic">MTB Project - Monarch Crest IMBA Epic</a> and <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/psicc/recarea/?recid=12613">San Isabel National Forest - Monarch Crest</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
