  <Placemark>
    <name>Trans Madeira (Portugal) [six-day enduro, shuttle event]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Island-crossing stage race through Madeira and Porto Santo</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Trans Madeira links high volcanic ridges, laurel forest, exposed rock, loam and coastal finishes across six long days. It is a race-led way to experience an unusually diverse island network, with 6-8 hours on the bike per day and some stages using trails opened under special event permits. The 2026 editions run 18-23 May and 28 September-3 October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Event shuttles and logistics are included for registered riders; there is no public lift system. The published event package is 2250 EUR. Outside the race, use a licensed local guide or shuttle and verify land access because the race route is not a permanent signed trail.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Madeira riding operates year-round, but rain, wind, fire risk and land-management closures can affect high trails.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>Race-only and specially permitted stages may not be available outside the event.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Funchal Airport</td><td>Event transfer / car</td><td>Island-wide</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://trans-madeira.com/">official Trans Madeira event site</a>. Confirm current trail access with the organizer or a local guide.</i>]]></description>
