  <Placemark>
    <name>Plaisir de Merle Trails (Simondium, South Africa) [permit, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Wine-estate trail network on the Simonsberg, 15 min from Hellsend</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A full network cut into the Simonsberg slopes above the Plaisir de Merle cellar: Meulstroom Up and Plaisir Easy Up carry the climbing, with Plaisir Flow Trail, Flow Trail Main, Grootrivier Down and Sky To Meulstroom Down as the descents, plus the long Plaisir Sky Traverse high on the mountain and singletrack such as Akkerboom Kloof, Cape Holly, Porcupine and Brown Hyena Trap Trail.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Self-pedalled climbs on dedicated up-trails. A Wine Lands Trails permit is required; buy it before riding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round. Summer fire danger and winter storms can close the estate.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Hellsend / Helshoogte Pass</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Stellenbosch</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Cape Town</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: trail names and layout from <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>; permits via <a href="https://winelandstrails.com/">Wine Lands Trails</a>. Confirm current access with the estate.</i>]]></description>
