  <Placemark>
    <name>Iron Throne Bike Park (Hartbeespoort, South Africa) [R50 trails + R250 cableway]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Hartbeespoort 1230 m - valley station of the Harties Cableway</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>South Africa's only cable-car-served gravity park, on the Magaliesberg escarpment above Hartbeespoort Dam. The cableway lifts you 350 m to the ridge at 1580 m and the downhill and enduro trails drop back to the valley station: steep, rocky and loose granite terrain, with the Purple, Blue and Green routes as the marked lines. It has hosted South African downhill championships as well as national enduro and cross-country rounds, and the operator rates it for intermediate and experienced riders rather than beginners.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Harties Cableway gondola carries bikes. Two tickets are needed: an R50 trail fee, bought at the Iron Throne brewery, plus an R250 cableway pass from the cableway ticket office, which is valid for a month rather than a day. Confirm both before travelling, as the trail park and the cableway are separate businesses.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; 08:00-17:00. Highveld summer thunderstorms close the cableway, and the rock is slick when wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Pretoria</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Johannesburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.hartiescableway.co.za/">Harties Cableway</a> and <a href="https://www.facebook.com/ironthronetrailpark/">Iron Throne Trail Park</a>; pin placed on the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/142660448">cableway valley station</a> (way 142660448), verified at 1231 m. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
