  <Placemark>
    <name>Giba Gorge MTB Park (Durban, South Africa) [from R70, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Giba Gorge 387 m - park entrance on Ingweni Road</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A privately run park in a forested valley beside the N3 outside Pinetown, and the gravity and jump hub of KwaZulu-Natal. Over 45 km of marked and maintained trail through indigenous forest, colour-graded green, blue, black, orange, purple and yellow, with roughly 10 km of that built specifically for gravity riders. The jump lines are the draw: a progression from a small kids' line through intermediate sets to a professionals-only line that drops in off a bridge and finishes on a quarter pipe, plus permanent dirt jumps and a BMX pump track. Gravity Dice is the biggest single descent at about 84 m. The relief is modest, so this is a features-and-flow park rather than a big-mountain one.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Pedal the climbs. Rider day passes from R70; the park runs a cafe, bike shop and washing facilities on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open 365 days a year, 07:00-17:00, with the gate closing at 16:30. Subtropical summer rain can close trails at short notice.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Durban</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Pietermaritzburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://gibagorge.co.za/">Giba Gorge MTB Park</a> for fees, hours and trail total; gravity and jump-line detail from <a href="https://www.sa-venues.com/things-to-do/kwazulunatal/giba-gorge-mountain-bike-park/">SA-Venues</a>. Pin placed on the OSM-mapped park entrance at 1 Ingweni Road, the address the operator publishes, verified at 387 m. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
