  <Placemark>
    <name>Thaba Trails (Johannesburg, South Africa) [R80, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Thaba Trails 1580 m - venue entrance and Cycle Hub on Klipriver Drive</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A 450-hectare private reserve 8 km from central Johannesburg, with colour-coded marked loops of 10, 25 and 40 km and over 80 km of singletrack in total. The riding is hard-climbing, rocky and technical highveld singletrack with long natural descents, and it is widely called the toughest network in Gauteng. <small>Note on scope: Thaba has no purpose-built gravity infrastructure - no downhill runs, jump lines, dirt jumps or pump track - so it sits on this map as a technical trail-riding venue rather than a gravity destination.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Self-pedalled climbs. Cycling permits are R80 a day, R600 for ten entries, R900 for twenty and R2500 for the year, under a strict no-pay-no-ride policy. Bike service and sales on site at The Cycle Hub, plus a cafe.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; closed on Mondays. Highveld summer thunderstorms are the main disruption.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Johannesburg centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Pretoria</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://thabatrails.co.za/trails/">Thaba Trails</a> for routes and permit prices and <a href="https://www.wildjoburg.co.za/the-venue/">WildJoburg</a> for the venue and address. Pin placed on the OSM-mapped Thaba Trails Mountain Bike Park and Cycle Hub node at 101 Klipriver Drive, verified at 1577 m. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
