  <Placemark>
    <name>Antongona Highlands MTB (Madagascar) [guide recommended]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Natural highland riding west of Antananarivo</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Guided circuits cross rolling red-earth hills, rice fields, village tracks and rough natural paths around the sacred hills of Antongona. This is adventure enduro and trail riding rather than a maintained bike park; rain can turn the clay slick and route-finding is not self-evident.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no unified trail fee. MBike Madagascar offers guided outings and transfers from Antananarivo; agree the route, bike, transport and price before departure.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>There is no formal trail season. Avoid heavy rain and do not enter sacred or village land without local permission.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Antananarivo</td><td>Guide transfer / car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://adventure.mbike.mg/en/a-moins-de-150-kms-d-antananarivo/37-antongona-loop-family-mtb-mtb.html">MBike Madagascar Antongona route</a>. Pin placed on the <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/551219565">Rova d'Antongona</a> (OSM way 551219565), the sacred hills the circuits run around, measured at 1467 m; it previously sat on the village of Sabotsin'Antongona 1.6 km east. Use a local guide and confirm permissions and conditions.</i>]]></description>
