  <Placemark>
    <name>Sintra Enduro Trails (Portugal) [commercial shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Atlantic forest enduro near Lisbon</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A broad natural network across Serra de Sintra, with loamy forest singletrack, granite rock, roots, steep technical descents and Atlantic-facing lines. The trails are not a unified signed bike park, junctions are easy to miss and the protected landscape is busy with walkers, so a local guide is strongly recommended.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No mechanical lift or unified trail fee. Commercial operators offer guided vehicle shuttles linking the main descents, while self-guided riders can pedal forest-road climbs. Book shuttle access in advance and do not assume every mapped trail is legal or open.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no formal MTB season.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>Summer fire restrictions, storms, forestry work and protected-land rules can close trails. Avoid saturated trails and give way to walkers.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lisbon</td><td>Car / train plus guide transfer</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Sintra station</td><td>Bike / guide shuttle</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://visitsintra.travel/pt/descobrir/active-sintra/atividades-terrestres/btt/go2cintra">Visit Sintra MTB listing</a> and <a href="https://sintraflowriders.com/index.php/shuttles/">Sintra Flow Riders shuttle information</a>. Confirm route legality, closures and meeting points with a local operator.</i>]]></description>
