  <Placemark>
    <name>Margalla Second Ridge MTB (Pakistan) [organized transport]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Hard backcountry ridge ride above Islamabad</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A long, remote mountain route from the Makhniyal side of the Margalla Hills, combining rough ridge riding, technical natural sections and substantial descents toward Masta Village, Gokina Valley or Khanpur. MTB Islamabad describes its organized Second Ridge ride as hard and suitable for experienced riders; the longer one-way hiking line loses roughly 1800 m while crossing shared, unsignposted terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. MTB Islamabad's June 2026 ride charged PKR 2000 for rider transport from Islamabad; this was an organized event price, not a permanent shuttle tariff. Join a current club outing or arrange a knowledgeable local guide and vehicle rather than attempting the remote route alone.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; This is shared backcountry and protected forest terrain, not a maintained bike park. Give way to hikers, confirm that cycling is permitted on the selected line, carry water and repair equipment, and avoid fire closures or monsoon storms.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 October; closed from 1 June (conservative cooler and drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>There is no formal MTB season. Heat, monsoon rain, wildfire and local restrictions can make the route unsafe or inaccessible.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Islamabad</td><td>Organized vehicle / car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://cyclingequipments.com/events/margalla-second-ridge-msr-trail-ride/">MTB Islamabad's 2026 Second Ridge ride</a>, <a href="https://www.wikiloc.com/hiking-trails/second-ridge-makhnyal-to-khanpur-154799466">long-route profile</a> and the <a href="https://iwmb.gov.pk/trails/">Islamabad Wildlife Management Board trail information</a>. Confirm current cycling permission and route access locally.</i>]]></description>
