  <Placemark>
    <name>Lower Mustang Enduro (Nepal) [expedition, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kali Gandaki valley 2910 m - jeep road below Kagbeni, at the bottom of Fast and Flat</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Lower Mustang is Nepal's premier big-mountain enduro landscape: fast dry singletrack, loose rock, exposed jeep tracks and technical ancient paths beneath the Annapurna and Dhaulagiri massifs. Signature objectives include Lupra, Ghyaula Pass and long descents around Jomsom and Muktinath; advanced expeditions may continue toward Thorong La at extreme altitude.<br/><br/>The nine traces on this spot are spread across the whole riding area rather than one hillside, so the pin sits at the middle of it: on the Beni-Lo Manthang jeep road between Ekle Bhatti and Kagbeni, where Fast and Flat comes out. Fast and Flat ends here and the Lupra Pass descents are 3 km away; Purang, Jhong, Next to the Wall and Under The Temple sit around Muktinath 7-8 km up the valley, and the Thorong Pass crossing runs from 11 km out to a 5406 m col. Jomsom, the airstrip you fly into, is 7 km back down the valley. Expect a vehicle or a long pedal between them.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Access requires pedalling, hike-a-bike and support vehicles where roads permit. Book a specialist expedition covering permits, acclimatization, guiding, lodging and mechanical support; this is not a trail-center day ride.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Altitude, exposure, wind, cold, remote rescue and rapidly changing trail or permit rules are serious hazards. Acclimatize properly and do not attempt high passes unsupported.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (broad expedition window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>Spring and autumn are preferred. Winter snow and cold close high routes; summer monsoon impacts are lower than elsewhere in Nepal but flights, roads and river crossings remain weather-sensitive.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Pokhara</td><td>Flight / expedition vehicle</td><td>~25 min flight to Jomsom, then 7 km up the jeep road</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.nepalmountainbike.com/blog/epic-himalayan-enduro-mtb-trips-in-nepal-the-ultimate-adventure">Nepal MTB's Mustang enduro guide</a> and <a href="https://www.nepalmountainbike.com/enduro-tour/himalayan-enduro-freeride-expedition-nepal">guided Himalayan enduro expedition</a>. Trail geometry drawn in gpx.studio and supplied for this map; pin placed at the lower end of the Fast and Flat trace on the <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/179321524">Beni-Lo Manthang jeep road</a> (OpenStreetMap), measured at 2910 m. Verify permits, altitude plan and transport with a licensed operator.</i>]]></description>
