  <Placemark>
    <name>Kincaid Park Singletrack (Alaska) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Anchorage's large urban singletrack playground</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A dense network of roughly 39 miles of rolling trails, including purpose-built mountain-bike singletrack with banked turns, short punchy climbs and fast descents. It suits progression and energetic trail laps more than sustained downhill, but gives Anchorage a substantial all-level dirt network minutes from the city.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift, shuttle or trail ticket. Pedal interconnected loops from designated Kincaid trailheads and follow one-way signs where posted; the wider park is shared with walkers, runners and wildlife.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Moose and bears occur inside the park. Carry appropriate deterrent, give wildlife a very wide berth and never ride closed or muddy trails.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 15 October (typical dirt-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>Actual dirt opening depends on snowmelt and drying. Winter fat-bike access follows separate grooming and trail rules.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Downtown Anchorage</td><td>Car / bike</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.anchorage.net/things-to-do/bicycle-tours-and-rentals/">Visit Anchorage's official Kincaid trail overview</a>. Check local trail conditions and closures before riding.</i>]]></description>
