  <Placemark>
    <name>Gudauri Bike Trails (Georgia) [summer lifts]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-accessed Caucasus downhill above the Georgian Military Highway</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Gudauri's high alpine summer terrain includes marked bike routes and a documented downhill trail of roughly 4.8 km. Open grassland, loose rock and big mountain weather create a raw resort experience rather than a dense machine-built park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Designated summer lifts carry bicycles. Published indications are 15 GEL for a Gudauri lift ride, with the Gudauri, Kobi, Firni and Truso installations operating in the main summer period; verify which lift and trail are active on the day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 July; closed from 16 September (published typical summer-lift window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 11:00-17:00<br/><small>Wind, storms and maintenance can close exposed lifts without notice. Confirm bike carriage and current trail marking.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tbilisi</td><td>Car / minibus</td><td>~2h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://georgia.travel/resorts/gudauri">Georgia Travel's official summer-bike and lift overview</a> and <a href="https://www.newgudauri.com/about-1?lang=en">published lift hours, bike access and downhill length</a>. Verify the live resort schedule.</i>]]></description>
