  <Placemark>
    <name>Bakuriani Bike Park (Georgia) [gondola, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Didveli 1856 m - Nodo gondola valley station</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Didveli is the mountain-bike sector, with five marked descents: two easy, two intermediate and one difficult. The intermediate track runs about 2.5 km down the right-hand side of the gondola line. Riding is downhill-only on the marked trails. The wooded, rooty terrain makes a useful contrast to exposed Gudauri, and the descent continues into the town below if you ride the whole hill out.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The resort names <b>Nodo</b> (gondola) and <b>Deka</b> (chairlift) as the Didveli lifts that run in summer. They chain 1856 m to 2160 m and then 2165 m to 2526 m, so 670 m of lift-served vertical, and roughly 800 m of descent if you ride out to the town at about 1700 m. Passes are sold at the Didveli cable-car counter. The Crystal 1 and Crystal 2 lifts on the other side of Didveli are the winter race lines and do not appear in the summer bulletin. Exact 2026 prices were not published, so confirm before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The 2025 summer season opened on 28 June, with the Didveli lifts running daily 11:00-18:00; closed from 1 October (estimated snow-free indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: 11:00-18:00<br/><small>Summer hours are from the 2025 bulletin and were not reconfirmed for 2026. No trail lines are drawn: OpenStreetMap has not mapped any mountain-bike trail in the Bakuriani massif, and the public GPS-trace archive holds nothing on the bike sector either. Confirm trail legality, lift carriage and maintenance locally before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tbilisi</td><td>Car / train and taxi</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://georgia.travel/bike-tour-bakuriani-resort-first-track">Georgia Travel's official Bakuriani bike route</a> and the resort operator's <a href="https://mta.ski/en/presscenter/SummerBakuriani2025">summer season bulletin</a>, which names Nodo and Deka as the Didveli summer lifts. Pin on the valley station of the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/249697044">Nodo gondola</a> (way 249697044), measured at 1856 m; it previously sat on the Crystal 1 valley station, which is a winter-only line. Verify current operations locally.</i>]]></description>
