  <Placemark>
    <name>Shahdag Mountain Cycling (Azerbaijan) [no bike lift documented]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Purpose-built downhill paths in Azerbaijan's main mountain resort</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Shahdag advertises specialized downhill cycling paths for multiple ability levels amid the high Greater Caucasus landscape. Resort rental makes it accessible without transporting a bike, though the published product is less developed and less precisely mapped than a conventional European bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bicycle-carrying lift is documented, even though pedestrian lifts operate in summer. Confirm whether access is pedal, vehicle-supported or lift-assisted before buying. Published adult e-bike rental is 25 AZN for 20 minutes, 42 AZN for 40 minutes or 50 AZN for one hour.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (estimated summer indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00<br/><small>Estimated resort activity hours. Check live activity status, trail map, bike carriage and weather before travelling.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Baku</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h</td></tr><tr><td>Qusar</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.shahdag.az/en/activity/velosiped">official downhill-path and bike-rental page</a> and <a href="https://shahdag.az/en/about-shahdag">official summer-activity overview</a>. Confirm the current access method directly with Shahdag.</i>]]></description>
