  <Placemark>
    <name>Aburi / Akuapem MTB Trails (Ghana) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ghana's established mountain-bike base above Accra</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Three marked self-guided routes of roughly two to three hours start around Aburi, while local guides link a much larger network of singletrack, dirt roads, forest, villages and waterfalls across the Akuapem Range. The riding is natural trail and adventure enduro rather than a purpose-built bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or permanent shuttle. Bike rental and guided day or multi-day tours are available locally; stronger riders pedal the rolling ridge network.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 May (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Published garden hours used as the visitor window. Tropical rain can make clay, roots and river crossings unsafe.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Accra</td><td>Car / guide transfer</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://aburi.ghana-net.com/">Aburi's marked MTB trail and opening-hours guide</a> and <a href="https://www.ghanabike2.com/biking.html">local guided trail-network operator</a>. Pin placed on <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1501642466">Ghana Bike + Hike Tours</a> (OSM node 1501642466) in Aburi, measured at 448 m - the operator the guided network runs through, and the one tagged on the region's only OSM cycle route. The <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/334386186">Aburi Botanic Gardens</a>, which the marked routes and the published hours belong to, are 350 m north. Confirm rental and trail conditions locally.</i>]]></description>
