  <Placemark>
    <name>East Nimba Mountain Trail (Liberia) [reserve guide, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Historic mine road climbing Liberia's highest mountain landscape</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A former LAMCO mountain road climbs through East Nimba Nature Reserve past Blue Lake, changing from rainforest to savanna and exposed former mining terrain. Liberia's tourism authority explicitly identifies the trail for bikers, hikers and drivers; side trails and the tri-border route require reserve guidance.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Register and pay the entrance fee at the Nimba Ecolodge and Reserve reception, then arrange a guide and confirm whether vehicle support is allowed for the intended route.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; This is a protected biodiversity reserve. Remain on the authorized road or guide-approved trail, avoid wet ground and follow every ranger instruction.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 May (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: guided daylight access only<br/><small>Confirm reserve opening, road state and guide availability before the long journey.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Monrovia</td><td>Car to Yekepa</td><td>~5h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://enjoyliberia.travel/pages/mount-nimba/">official Liberia Tourism biking, reserve and access guide</a>. Arrange permission and a reserve guide in advance.</i>]]></description>
