  <Placemark>
    <name>Congo Nile Trail (Rwanda) [multi-day, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Rwanda's signature Lake Kivu mountain-bike journey</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Congo Nile Trail follows roughly 227 km of steep lakeside country from Rubavu toward Rusizi through tea and coffee landscapes, villages and beaches. Its four to seven stages mix unpaved roads, rough tracks, sustained climbs and natural descents; it is an expedition-style MTB route, not a shaped bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Ride point-to-point with luggage transfer or book a local guide, rental bike and support vehicle. The marker identifies the usual northern start in Rubavu.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Carry offline navigation and repair equipment. Confirm the current itinerary and advice near the DRC border, and never cross an international border accidentally.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (principal dry-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight riding only<br/><small>The route is available year-round, but rain substantially changes dirt-road and trail conditions.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kigali</td><td>Bus / support vehicle to Rubavu</td><td>~3h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the <a href="https://rdb.rw/rdb-tourism-launches-mountain-biking/">Rwanda Development Board's national MTB program</a> and the <a href="https://congoniletrail.com/">Congo Nile Trail guide and rental service</a>. Verify stage conditions and accommodation before departure.</i>]]></description>
