  <Placemark>
    <name>Vallée de Ferney MTB (Mauritius) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Authorized conservation-valley bike routes</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>La Vallée de Ferney permits bicycles on its open tracks through native forest and grassland. Four routes cover 5, 8, 13 and 18 km; the longest gains about 970 m and is rated difficult. This is scenic trail and cross-country riding with natural descents, not a bike park, and riders must bring their own bikes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or shuttle. Pedal each loop from the reserve reception. Published admission is 500 MUR per visiting adult and 250 MUR per child, with lower resident rates.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Stay on authorized open tracks in this conservation area. Access can be restricted for private events between June and September, and weather can close routes.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure (normally open year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: activities 08:30-14:00; reception until 17:00<br/><small>Latest permitted start varies by route, from 10:30 for 18 km to 14:00 for 5 km. Book ahead.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mahébourg</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://ferney.mu/activities/hiking-trail/">official Ferney bicycle access, routes, prices and opening hours</a>. Confirm route availability when booking.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
