    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Station VTT de Cilaos (Réunion) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Nine graded circuits inside Réunion's mountain cirque</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Cilaos has an official MTB station with nine mapped circuits for multiple ability levels; all nine official ONF traces are drawn on this map. Routes combine highland roads, forest tracks and natural technical descents beneath the cirque's immense volcanic walls; this is a signed trail network rather than a shaped downhill park. The marker is at the Mare à Joseph trail hub, where the largest group of individual circuits starts.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bike lift or permanent shuttle is documented. Pedal from Cilaos or book a local guide and vehicle where permitted. Trail access is generally free.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; The cirque is steep, exposed and prone to rockfall, landslides and abrupt weather. Check the official map, road access and ONF trail closures before riding.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 December (cooler and generally drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>The network is normally year-round when routes are authorized and conditions permit.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saint-Louis</td><td>Car via Route de Cilaos</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: the <a href="https://www.onf.fr/vivre-la-foret/%2B/15f7%3A%3Areseau-de-pistes-vtt-et-vttae-du-cirque-de-cilaos.html?lang=fr">official ONF Cilaos circuit guide and nine GPX downloads</a>. Verify current closures locally.</i>]]></description>
