  <Placemark>
    <name>Cardrona Bike Park (New Zealand) [184 NZD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cardrona 1860 m - NZ's highest bike park, McDougall's Chondola top</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Ten kilometres of peak-to-pub downhill with 345 m of vertical drop, plus a network of flow and technical lines at the South Island's highest lift-served park. The Whitestar Express chairlift opens additional expert terrain above the gondola mid-station. The famous Cardrona pub is the finish line.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The McDougall's Chondola and Whitestar Express chairlift carry bikes during the summer season. 2026 day pass NZ$184 adult, with multi-day and season options available. Bike rental and guiding at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from December; closed from March (southern hemisphere summer).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Queenstown</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr><tr><td>Wanaka</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://cardrona-treblecone.com/">Cardrona</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>168.94,-44.876,1552</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">cardrona-bike-park</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro chairlift gondola</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="open_from">12-01</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="closed_from">04-01</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="price_day">184 NZD</mwm:value>
      </mwm:properties>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>

  <Placemark>
    <name>Mt Buller Bike Park (Victoria, AU) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mt Buller - Victoria's lift-served alpine gravity park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A network of downhill and enduro trails descending from the alpine village at 1600 m through snow gum forest. Purpose-built flow lines and technical black descents make use of the ski-area chairlift infrastructure during the green summer months.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairlift access for bikes during summer operation. Confirm the current bike ticket, lift schedule and trail status with Mt Buller before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from December; closed from March (southern hemisphere summer).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Melbourne</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mtbuller.com.au/winter">Mt Buller</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>146.449,-37.146,1592</coordinates></Point>
