  <Placemark>
    <name>Hillbilly Bike Park - Huckfest (Ål, Hallingdal, Norway) [four weekends, check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ål skisenter 596 m - valley station of the Parallellheisen tow, home of Huckfest</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The freeride venue behind <b>Huckfest</b>, the FEST Series big-jump festival in Ål that Mads "Makken" Haugen and Aasmund Thorsen started as the Hillbilly Huckfest in 2013 and that has drawn Kurt Sorge, Nico Vink, Andreu Lacondeguy and Haugen himself down what the operator calls Europe's toughest slopestyle track. Seven trails, all between red and black: the <b>SpareBank1 line</b> is the slopestyle course itself, big jumps, technical features and steep switchbacks; <b>Genghis Khan</b> is the crowd favourite, fast and flowing with sharp terrain changes; <b>Siloløypa</b> is narrow and varied, <b>On the Edge</b> steep and technical, <b>Old Line</b> rough and natural, and Veslestølvegen the wide way down. Ål skisenter gives up to about 220 vertical metres per lift ride and roughly 440 m across the park as a whole.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Lift-served by the ski centre's drag lifts, the longest of which (Parallellheisen) climbs from 596 m to 961 m. Uplift runs only on the park's open weekends; the operator will open the lift outside those dates for groups of five or more on request. No public price is published - contact Hillbilly MTB.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; This is a jump park before it is a trail network, and the operator grades nothing below red. The slopestyle line is built for the festival's field; the gaps are not optional.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Four weekends between late June and mid-September, published each spring - the 2025 season ran 28-29 June, 12-13 July, 8-10 August and 13-14 September, 11:00-16:00. Check the current dates before travelling; outside them the lift only turns for booked groups.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Oslo</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr><tr><td>Ål station</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Geilo</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.visital.no/en/tur/hilbilly-bike-park/">Visit Ål - Hillbilly Bike Park</a>, <a href="https://www.fest-series.com/huckfest">FEST Series - Huckfest</a> and OpenStreetMap. Opening weekends and prices change every year; confirm with Hillbilly MTB.</i>
    <br/><small>Only two of the seven trails are in OpenStreetMap - Sparebank1-løypa and Siloløypa, both near the base - so Genghis Khan, On the Edge, Old Line and Veslestølvegen are named here but not drawn. A third way carrying the operator's name, <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/293036869">Hillbilly knotesti</a> (mtb:scale 4), sits 9 km south at 1040 m, is 215 m long and climbs slightly, so it is not a descent and is not drawn either.</small>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
