  <Placemark>
    <name>La Pinilla Bike Park (Segovia, ES) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Pinilla - Madrid's closest lift-served bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Close to 30 km of chairlift-served descent through pine forest in the Ayllon range, which makes this one of the largest bike parks in Spain and the nearest one to Madrid. Trails are graded green, blue, red and black across the whole range, and two new descents were added recently; the operator does not publish a count per colour. Full-face helmet is compulsory.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The chairlift carries bikes and serves every downhill circuit. Day pass sold through the resort shop; daily insurance covering medical assistance and rescue on the trails is 5 EUR extra. Rental through the on-site partner.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Runs on Saturdays and Sundays through the summer season.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:00; last lift 17:30<br/><small>Published weekend hours; check the operator calendar for extra days.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Madrid</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr><tr><td>Segovia</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://lapinilla.es/bike-park/">La Pinilla Bike Park</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i> Pin corrected to the valley station of the Super Express chairlift (OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/60960182">way 60960182</a>), measured at 1517 m: the pin sat on the line of the abandoned Antiguo Telecabina Pico del Lobo, 1.5 km from any lift that still runs; the resort base, where the Super Express chairlift and the Telecabina Gran Plato both start, is at a measured 1517 m.]]></description>
