  <Placemark>
    <name>Jay Peak Bike Park (Vermont, US) [tram/chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Jay Peak 564 m - base of the aerial tram, Jay, Vermont</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Northern Vermont's lift-served gravity park with the iconic tram and chairlift providing uplift. Trails range from beginner flow to technical black diamond downhill through the Green Mountains, with the bonus of an indoor waterpark at the base for recovery.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Jay Peak tram and chairlift carry bikes during summer. Check the current bike ticket and schedule with Jay Peak before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Montreal</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Burlington, VT</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://jaypeakresort.com/">Jay Peak</a>. Pin on the valley station of the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/199923159">Jay Peak aerial tram</a> (way 199923159), measured at 564 m; the tram climbs 597 m to 1161 m. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
