  <Placemark>
    <name>Panorama Bike Park (Invermere, BC, CA) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Panorama 1184 m - valley station of the Mile 1 Express, Purcell Mountains</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A well-established BC park with the Mile 1 Express chairlift serving downhill and enduro trails through the Purcells. Old-school technical lines combine with newer flow trails, plus an alpine zone for high-elevation riding. The operator's own summer report splits the network into DH Biking (20 trails, freeride and technical), Enduro Biking, the pedal-access Fire Hall trails and a base-area XC network; the lines drawn here are the DH and enduro trails OpenStreetMap holds.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairlift carries bikes during summer operation. Check the current bike ticket and schedule with Panorama before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Invermere</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Calgary</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.panoramaresort.com/panorama-today/summer-report">Panorama's summer trail report</a>, <a href="https://www.panoramaresort.com/explore/dh-mountain-biking">its DH biking page</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/31290817">OSM Mile 1 Express lift</a>. Pin marks the OSM Mile 1 Express valley station, verified at 1184 m.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
