  <Placemark>
    <name>Revelstoke Bike Park (Revelstoke, BC, CA) [gondola/chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Revelstoke 535 m - base of the Revelation gondola, Revelstoke Mountain Resort</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The longest vertical descent of any bike park in Canada at over 1700 m with the gondola and chairlift serving upper and lower mountain terrain. Fifty-plus kilometres of trail ranging from machine-built flow to steep, rooty natural black diamond lines through old-growth cedar forest.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Revelation gondola and Stoke chairlift carry bikes during summer operation. Check the current bike ticket with Revelstoke before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Revelstoke</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Kelowna</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.revelstokemountainresort.com/">Revelstoke</a>. Pin on the valley station of the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1361895818">Revelation Gondola</a> lower section (way 1361895818), measured at 535 m; gondola and Stoke chair together reach 2225 m. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
