  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Washington Bike Park (Vancouver Island, BC, CA) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mount Washington 1179 m - base of the Eagle Express chairlift, Vancouver Island</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The only lift-served bike park on Vancouver Island with chairlift access to downhill and enduro trails through coastal forest. Panoramic views across the Strait of Georgia to the mainland, plus a dedicated skills park at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairlift carries bikes during summer operation. Check the current bike ticket and schedule with Mount Washington before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Courtenay / Comox</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Nanaimo</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://mountwashington.ca/">Mount Washington</a>. Pin on the valley station of the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/66339684">Eagle Express</a> chairlift (way 66339684), measured at 1179 m; it climbs 391 m to 1570 m. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
