  <Placemark>
    <name>Kaprun - Maiskogel and Kitzsteinhorn (Salzburg, AT) [35 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kaprun 765 m - MK Maiskogelbahn valley station and the end of the Maiskogel Trail</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two very different halves. The Maiskogel Trail is 4.6 km of wide berms, rollers and small jumps straight back to Kaprun - the friendliest introduction to gravity riding in the Pinzgau. Above it the Kitzsteinhorn freeride trails start from the glacier terminal at nearly 3000 m and drop through high alpine scree and rock to the Alpincenter, which is about as high as lift-served riding gets in Austria and stays rideable when the valleys are baking.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Bike carriage is included in the ticket on the Maiskogelbahn, the 3K K-onnection and the Gletscherjet. Adult day ticket 35 EUR (child 17.50 EUR); a single ride up is 16.50 EUR.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 23 May; closed from 4 October (published 2026 dates). The glacier trails open later and depend on snow.<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Salzburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr><tr><td>Munich</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h20</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.kitzsteinhorn.at/en/summer/kitzsteinhorn/mountainbike">Kitzsteinhorn</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
