  <Placemark>
    <name>Big White Bike Park (British Columbia, CA) [59 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Big White village 1660 m - Plaza Chair loading, ticket office and bike shop</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Okanagan's lift-served park, sitting high enough at 2145 m that it rides cool and dry through a British Columbia summer. Machine-built flow and jump lines dominate, with steeper technical tracks through the sub-alpine spruce below them, and around 480 m of vertical to the village. Quiet compared with the coastal parks, and the trail surface - fine volcanic soil - is genuinely good.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The day ticket includes unlimited lift access on the Bullet Express and is 59 CAD for adults aged 19-64, plus GST. Season passes are sold through the resort's online store. Friday evening extended riding is included on the day when it runs.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 July; closed from 8 September (published 2026 dates - a short, reliable high-summer season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kelowna</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bigwhite.com/summer/mountain-biking/bike-park-info">Big White Ski Resort</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Big White publishes no trail list of its own - it points riders at Trailforks - so the drawn lines are ungraded; the grades on the ground are the resort's.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
