  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Sima Bike Park (Yukon, CA) [40 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mount Sima 890 m - base area: chairlift load, lodge, bike shop and rentals</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Whitehorse's lift-served park, a short drive from downtown, with two blue flow runs (including a 3.9 km machine-built line), an expert black and two extreme double-black lines - Lefty Loosey and Drop the Clutch among them, with Righty Tighty on the intermediate side. Compact vertical (around 260 m) but a good mid-week evening lap spot.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Day ticket 40 CAD adult, 35 CAD youth (U18) and 65+.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 22 June; closed from 7 September (typical window; check the operator before travel).<br/>Daily opening hours: 11:00-19:00, extended to 22:00 Wednesdays and Fridays for Bike Nights<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Whitehorse</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Whitehorse airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://mountsima.com/">Mount Sima</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
