  <Placemark>
    <name>Mystic Bike Park - Bright (Victoria, AU) [100 AUD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mystic Park trailhead 330 m - shuttle pick-up on the edge of Bright</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The centre of gravity riding in the Victorian High Country: Elevation Parks describes a 40-plus trail network of over 45 km on Mystic Mountain's pine-plantation slopes, from green flow to double black, with the uplift serving 20-plus of them. Everything from technical natural pine-tree singletrack to fast gravity flow and big jump lines, and the Hero Trail - Australia's first full-scale public freeride and jump trail. Host venue for World Cup and national-level racing. Bright itself is a genuine mountain-bike town, which makes this an easy place to spend a week.<br/>The 22 lines drawn here run from 797 m on Mystic Downhill to about 320 m in town, so roughly 470 m of vertical and 22 km of the network. Marketing copy putting Mystic at "800 m of vertical" does not match the hill: the summit is 790 m and the town is at 320 m.<br/><small>Hero Trail's upper half, Tombstone, Hotwheels, Sugar Glider and Flowmingo are on the operator's list and are not in OpenStreetMap, so they are not drawn.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Elevation Parks runs the uplift from the trailhead. Two things are needed and they are now sold separately: a one-day Gravity Pass at 100 AUD buys unlimited shuttles to several drop zones, and on top of that every rider at Mystic must hold a Mountain Pass - 20 AUD for a day, 50 AUD for seven days, 145 AUD annual local or 275 AUD all-mountain (adult rates; child roughly half). Mountain Passes stopped being bundled with the Gravity Pass on 1 August 2025. Book ahead - the uplift sells out even off-peak, and walk-ins pay a surcharge. On-site bike hire and skills coaching.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; winter is the wettest stretch.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:00<br/><small>Published uplift hours: 09:30-16:00 in autumn, winter and spring, and 08:00-14:30 in summer to dodge the heat. The trails themselves are open outside uplift hours to anyone with a Mountain Pass.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bright</td><td>Bike</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Albury</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Melbourne</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: Elevation Parks' <a href="https://www.elevationmystic.com/pass-options/gravity-pass/">Gravity Pass</a> and <a href="https://www.elevationmystic.com/pass-options/mountain-pass/">Mountain Pass</a> pages for the prices, hours and the 40-plus trail count, and <a href="https://www.elevationmystic.com/bright-mtb-trails/">recommended rides</a> for the trail line-up. Pin placed on the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/7856403356">Mystic Park trailhead node 7856403356</a>, measured at 329 m. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
