  <Placemark>
    <name>Arkytox Bike Park (Aguascalientes) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Presa Los Arquitos 1908 m - trailhead just west of the dam</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Twenty graded trails: 9 blue, 9 red and 2 black. A community-driven park specialising in enduro riding, with a well-balanced mix of technical handling sections and fast, flowy tracks suitable for progressing riders - the bulk of it blue and red, so it rewards riders working their way up rather than only experts. Built and maintained by the active local trail-building community.<br/><small>No trail lines are drawn here: none of Arkytox's trails exist in OpenStreetMap. Follow the park's own channels for the current map.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal-up / self-shuttle access. Free entry, open 24 hours daily.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round.<br/>Daily opening hours: 24 hours<br/>
    <small>Peak times: Sunday mornings and weekend afternoons. Least crowded: Monday and Thursday evenings.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Aguascalientes</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 h 30</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the park's own <a href="https://www.instagram.com/arkytox_bike_park/">Instagram</a> and <a href="https://www.facebook.com/ARKYTOX/">Facebook</a>, which carry the trail count and current conditions. Pin placed on the south shore of the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/319516438">Presa Los Arquitos</a> (way 319516438), 40 m past the west end of the dam (way 319516428), measured at 1908 m. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-102.390968,21.923868,1908</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">arkytox</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park no-lift enduro</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="open_from">01-01</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="closed_from">01-01</mwm:value>
      </mwm:properties>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Yuca Xtreme Bike Park (Aguascalientes) [100 MXN]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Yuca Xtreme 2,110 m - shuttle trailhead in the Sierra Fria foothills, Jesús María</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>High-altitude pine-oak forest riding on the western edge of the Aguascalientes highlands; the operator gives its address as Mesa de Pinos, Sierra Fria, Pabellón de Arteaga. Seven graded trails: one black, three red and three blue. Loose soil over sharp granite rock gardens, natural double-track conversions, technical rock drops, and fast off-camber enduro singletrack - the mix rewards a rider who can handle loose ground more than one chasing airtime. The site doubles as an adventure camp with rappel, canopy, climbing, hiking and fishing.<br/><small>Nothing here is in OpenStreetMap: no bike-park tag, no mtb-tagged way, and no feature named Yuca or Mesa de Pinos anywhere in the Sierra Fria.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No mechanical lift. Uplift is organised 4x4 pickup shuttles (remontes) along the forest logging roads, or long fire-road pedal climbs. Private property, so a day pass is required; around 100 MXN, unconfirmed. Book ahead.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 November (estimated season for high pine forest, not published).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00<br/>
    <small>Estimated hours; confirm shuttle schedules and reservation requirements with the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Aguascalientes</td><td>Hwy 45 N to Pabellón de Arteaga, then Hwy 70 W to San José de Gracia and dirt roads into the Sierra Fría</td><td>~45 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~6 h</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the park's own <a href="https://www.facebook.com/yucaxtremebikepark/">Facebook page</a>, the <a href="https://www.yumping.com/en/camps/yuca-extreme--e19664235">Yuca Extreme camp listing</a> for the address and activities, and <a href="https://es.wikiloc.com/rutas/mountain-bike/mexico/aguascalientes">Wikiloc's Aguascalientes MTB routes</a> for the terrain and the shuttle arrangement. Pin and grade mix checked on the ground by this map's maintainer and supplied as a waypoint; the coordinate measures 2,109 m against the 2,108 m carried in the file. Prices, schedules and shuttle availability can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-102.378567,21.997678,2109</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">yuca-xtreme</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="tags">beginner intermediate expert bike-park enduro shuttle</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="open_from">04-01</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="closed_from">11-01</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="price_day">100 MXN</mwm:value>
      </mwm:properties>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Murciélagos Bike Park (Puebla) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Murciélagos 2,290 m - trailhead on the sierra above the Tehuacán valley, Ajalpan</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A sustainable-trail project on the dry desert slopes of the Ajalpan municipality, built and maintained by the Murciélagos crew as much for local mobility and eco-tourism as for riding. About seven graded trails: one black, two red and four blue. Loose shale, natural step-downs, canyon-wall berms and narrow singletrack lined with cactus - a classic steep downhill profile up top that loosens into enduro lines lower down. Built to suit e-bikes as well; the long one is Coyote, roughly 8 km with about 1,040 m of descent, and Aguacate is the fast, rock-strewn technical line.<br/><small>Nothing here is in OpenStreetMap: an mtb-tag and bike-park sweep of the area returns no features at all.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No chairlift. Self-organised pickup shuttles (camionetas) take the dirt access track to the upper launch points, or pedal up the rural fire roads. Hostería El Trébol at the foot of the mountain is the check-in: pay the trail-maintenance fee there and arrange the shuttle, a guide, food, parking or a bed. The crew also offers phone or in-person trail assistance. The fee is not published; ask when you book.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 November (estimated typical season, not published).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-18:00<br/>
    <small>Estimated hours; confirm shuttle schedules and hostel services with the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Tehuacán</td><td>Route 150/135D toward Ajalpan, then the dirt track from Hostería El Trébol</td><td>~45 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Puebla</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h 30</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the crew's own <a href="https://www.pinkbike.com/directory/15363/murcielagos-bike-park-trail-building-and-mtb-experiences/">Murciélagos Bike Park Trail Building and MTB Experiences</a> listing for the project and the Hostería El Trébol access, and <a href="https://es.wikiloc.com/rutas/mountain-bike/mexico/puebla/ajalpan">Wikiloc's Ajalpan MTB routes</a> for the terrain and the shuttle arrangement. Pin and grade mix checked on the ground by this map's maintainer and supplied as a waypoint; the coordinate measures 2,288 m against the 2,281 m carried in the file. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
