  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park KRB (Hidalgo) [290 MXN]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>KRB 2,710 m - shuttle base in the pine forest above Mineral del Chico</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Shuttle-served enduro and downhill park in the dense pine forest of the Parque Nacional El Chico, 2 km from the village of Mineral del Chico. Trailforks lists 15 routes, aimed at intermediate to advanced riders; Manzano, Kali and Thiago are the ones riders mention most, and the terrain is steep and chunky with wooden bridges, drops and natural rock gardens.<br/><small>Nothing here is in OpenStreetMap: the only named features in the bbox are the village, the Mineral del Monte road and the combi routes.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Vehicle shuttle, run by KRB Bike. The Sunday group shuttle is around 290 MXN including the pass; confirm current rates and which days the shuttle runs. Cabin lodging on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/>
    <small>Shuttle schedules vary and group days are booked in advance; confirm before travelling.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Mineral del Chico</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pachuca</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 30</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the operator's <a href="https://www.facebook.com/krbbike">KRB Bike page</a> and its <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/region/krb-bike-park-70793">Trailforks region</a> for the route count and names. Pin altitude measured at 2,710 m, 1.9 km from the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/290904567">Mineral del Chico</a> village node; the coordinate itself is a shuttle-base estimate rather than a mapped feature. Prices, schedules, trail status and shuttle availability can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
