  <Placemark>
    <name>Meteoro Bike Park (Querétaro) [40 MXN parking]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Meteoro 1,860 m - trailhead and parking at Tlacote el Bajo</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A dense community-built network on the semi-desert hillsides west of Santiago de Querétaro, and one of the best-mapped spots in Mexico: OpenStreetMap holds <b>55 named trails</b> here, every one carrying an IMBA difficulty grade, green through red. Rocky volcanic soil, dry hardpack, tight switchbacks, step-ups and natural rock jumps, with named lines like La Reyder, Canal Blanco, Tarántula, Minotauro, El Laberinto del Fauno, Hakuna Matata and Los Garambullos. The operator also counts eight cross-country circuits, eight shorter enthusiast circuits and an XCM "Monumental" loop, plus a skills area, a pumptrack, a dirt-jump zone and built drops, berms and bridges.<br/>The catch is the terrain: the whole hill spans <b>1,837 m to 1,917 m</b>, so 80 m of relief in total. This is a cross-country, skills and progression network ridden in short laps, not a gravity park - the longest run drops 56 m over 1.3 km at 4%.<br/><small>Eleven of the 55 clear this map's drop test and are drawn; the other 44 are real trails that never lose enough height to read as descents. Most are tagged one-way, so ride them in the mapped direction.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No chairlift. Pedal up the dirt perimeter tracks, or arrange a pickup-truck shuttle through the local trail access points. Trail access is free; secure parking at the base is around 40 MXN.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/>
    <small>No published hours; the network is ridden in daylight.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Querétaro</td><td>Avenida Revolución / Carretera a Tlacote west, then dirt access roads</td><td>~30 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 30</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the park's own <a href="https://www.facebook.com/p/Meteoro-Bike-Park-100063781111451/">Facebook page</a> for the circuit line-up, its <a href="https://www.pinkbike.com/directory/18046/meteoro-bike-park/">Pinkbike directory entry</a>, a rider's <a href="https://www.wikiloc.com/mountain-biking-trails/meteoro-bikepark-madagarantula-queretaro-105262024">Wikiloc track</a>, and OpenStreetMap for the trail network itself. Pin and grade mix checked on the ground by this map's maintainer and supplied as a waypoint; the coordinate measures 1,859 m against the 1,858 m carried in the file. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
