  <Placemark>
    <name>Barrancas del Cobre Adventure Park (Divisadero, Chihuahua) [MTB routes, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Parque de Aventura Barrancas del Cobre 2,265 m - canyon-rim park at Divisadero</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Mountain-bike routes inside the Copper Canyon adventure park on the rim above Divisadero, in the Sierra Tarahumara. The park grades its routes for beginner, intermediate and advanced riders; the main line follows the canyon edge from Divisadero with technical climbs and descents and a gradual loss of height, and finishes at a cable-car station you can ride back up to the park. The rim runs at about 2,200-2,300 m and the canyon floor is more than 1,000 m below, so the exposure is the attraction. The park is also a zipline, via-ferrata and cable-car complex with a Tarahumara museum, not a dedicated bike park.<br/><small>Nothing rideable here is in OpenStreetMap; the park itself is mapped as a polygon.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bike lift. Pedal or vehicle drop to the start; the rim route ends at the cable car. Bike rental and guided routes are sold at the park, and the MTB rate is not published separately from the park's activity packages.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 March; closed from 1 November (the park names March to October as the best window for riding here).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/>
    <small>Remote sierra terrain at altitude; carry water and navigation, and confirm which activities are running.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Divisadero / Areponápuchi</td><td>Bike</td><td>~15 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Creel</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Chihuahua</td><td>Car / Chepe train</td><td>~4-5 h</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mexicodesconocido.com.mx/ciclismo-de-montana-en-barrancas-del-cobre-sierra-tarahumara.html">Mexico Desconocido on mountain biking in Barrancas del Cobre</a> for the routes and the cable-car return, and the <a href="https://chepe.mx/actividades/actividades-turisticas-divisadero/parque-de-aventura/">Chepe adventure-park page</a> for the park itself. Pin placed on the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1126116573">Parque de aventura Barrancas del cobre</a> polygon (way 1126116573), measured at 2,265 m. Previously pinned and named as "San Rafael", which is a different place 7 km away. Prices, schedules and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
