  <Placemark>
    <name>La Fragua Bike Park (Guanajuato) [50 MXN]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Fragua 2,650 m - private mountain property in the Sierra de Santa Rosa</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Shuttle-served enduro and downhill park on private land in the Sierra de Santa Rosa, a few kilometres above Guanajuato city, and a national championship venue. Trailforks lists 13 trails; the longest is Xumu at 6.9 km, nine of them allow e-bikes, and the mix runs from sculpted flow with gap jumps, berms and wooden bridges down to steep rock-strewn downhill-only lines. The sierra tops out around 2,700 m here, so a full shuttle day stacks a lot of descent without any single run being enormous. Food service, camping and a driver service - you bring the vehicle and they supply a driver for a set of runs.<br/><small>Nothing here is in OpenStreetMap.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Vehicle shuttle; e-bikes allowed. Private day pass, around 50 MXN, plus the shuttle or driver service on top; confirm current rates.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 November (estimated high-sierra season, not published).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00<br/>
    <small>Estimated hours; confirm shuttle schedules and day-pass requirements with the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Guanajuato City</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~4 h</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the park's own <a href="https://www.facebook.com/lafraguabikepark/">Facebook page</a>, <a href="https://escapadas.mexicodesconocido.com.mx/actividades/la-fragua-bike-park/">Mexico Desconocido</a> for the access and services, and its <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/region/la-fragua-bike-park-41140/">Trailforks region</a> for the trail list. Pin altitude measured at 2,650 m, 2.5 km from the OSM Santa Rosa de Lima node; the coordinate is a sierra-access estimate rather than a mapped feature. Prices, schedules, trail status and shuttle availability can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
