  <Placemark>
    <name>Punta Venado Bike Park (Playa del Carmen) [price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Punta Venado 10 m - basecamp at km 278 of the Playa del Carmen-Tulum highway</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The first purpose-built mountain-bike park on the Yucatan peninsula, between Xcaret and Paamul. The operator counts more than 25 km of singletrack at three graded levels - green, blue and black - through mangrove, jungle and cenote country, over fossilised coral that is jagged and unforgiving: this is technical cross-country with almost no elevation, not gravity riding. Loops finish on a Caribbean beach. Del Jaguar and the Earthquake trail are the punchy limestone rock-garden lines riders single out. Full-suspension rental bikes, guided rides and a sister site called The Cave Bike Park.<br/><small>Nothing here is in OpenStreetMap. Flat by design - do not expect a descent.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and nothing to shuttle: pedal-powered cross-country on flat ground. Trail access is sold at the gate and the operator does not publish the rate online - riders report around 500 MXN, and rental bikes about 1,000 MXN. Phone or WhatsApp ahead.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; closed Mondays.<br/>Daily opening hours: 07:00-15:00<br/>
    <small>Reported hours, Tuesday to Sunday. Tropical heat and humidity all year; the wet season runs June to October. Confirm schedules and rental availability.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Playa del Carmen</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cancún</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Tulum</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the park's own <a href="https://www.pvbikepark.com/">official site</a> (address at km 278, contact) and <a href="https://www.pvbikepark.com/operation-info">operation info</a>, plus <a href="https://playarida.com/mountain-bike-trails-playa-del-carmen/">a local shop's guide</a> for the 25 km and the three grades. The entry price is the one figure no published source states; it is reported, not confirmed. Pin measured at 10 m on the highway frontage. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
