  <Placemark>
    <name>Terra na Veia Bike Park (Ceará) [30 BRL]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Terra na Veia 40 m - 783-hectare estate at Maracanaú, below the Serra de Maranguape</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Open since 2011 and the main mountain-bike trail park in Ceará, on a 783-hectare estate with its own weir. Roughly 30 km of trail across more than twenty singletracks, of which about nine carry a grade: five red, three blue and one green. Red dirt and sand-rock over low hills, with fast flowy singletrack through dense vegetation, rock gardens, sinuous turns, built wooden gaps and a dirt-jump area. Tropical enduro in character rather than downhill. A restaurant, rental bikes, trail guides, stand-up paddling and kayaking on the lake round it out.<br/><small>Nothing here is in OpenStreetMap.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No mechanical lift, and with only tens of metres of relief there is nothing to shuttle: every lap is pedalled or pushed back up. Day-use pass around 30 BRL.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; the park itself runs at weekends. Ceará's wet season is roughly February to May.<br/>Daily opening hours: 07:00-18:00<br/>
    <small>Published Saturday and Sunday hours; check before making a weekday trip.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Fortaleza</td><td>BR-020 / CE-060</td><td>~40 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Maracanaú</td><td>Car / bike</td><td>~15 min</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the park's own <a href="https://www.facebook.com/terranaveia/">Facebook page</a>, a <a href="http://pedalace.blogspot.com/2013/06/bike-park-terra-na-veia.html">Pedala Ceará write-up</a>, and <a href="https://www.strava.com/">Strava's Maracanaú mountain-bike segments</a> for the terrain. The operator and its own street address put the estate in Maracanaú, not Maranguape as this entry once said; its own domain no longer resolves. Pin and grade mix checked on the ground by this map's maintainer and supplied as a waypoint; the coordinate measures 39 m against the 36 m carried in the file. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
