  <Placemark>
    <name>Águas da Serra Bike Park (Paraná) [20-30 BRL]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>São Luiz do Purunã 1,045 m - village on the Escarpa Devoniana, park nearby</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Downhill and enduro terrain on the private Estância Águas da Serra, on the Escarpa Devoniana escarpment at São Luiz do Purunã. About five gravity trails, some of them shared with cross-country riders, horses and motorcycles, plus a rescue road; the character is steep off-camber ground, deep ruts and gullies, high-speed gap jumps and rock features, the best known being the Drop do Pedrão. A long-standing testing ground for gravity riders out of Curitiba. Pool, camping, playground, fishing tanks and a restaurant on site.<br/><small>Nothing here is in OpenStreetMap. Trail names beyond the Drop do Pedrão are not published; earlier text here listed "Pista 1" to "Pista 4", which no source supports.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no shuttle: push or pedal back up. A fee covers the trails and the facilities, around 20-30 BRL. The property is private and access is arranged by phone.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round, mainly at weekends and on public holidays; winter and spring are the wettest months on the escarpment.<br/>Daily opening hours: weekend and holiday hours<br/>
    <small>Private property - call ahead rather than turning up.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Curitiba</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Campo Largo</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: an <a href="http://www.allmountainbike.com.br/2016/04/trilhas-da-serra-bike-park.html">All Mountain Bike report on the park</a> for the trail count, features and access, and its <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/region/aguas-da-serra-bike-park-45222/">Trailforks region</a>. Pin placed on the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/416646661">São Luiz do Purunã</a> village node (416646661), measured at 1,045 m - a village proxy, because the estância itself is not mapped. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
