  <Placemark>
    <name>Canal Aventura Bike Park (Paraná) [20-40 BRL]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Canal Aventura 970 m - former mate farm at Piraquara, below the Serra do Mar</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>An Atlantic Forest bike park on a 244-hectare historic yerba-mate farm at Piraquara, 25 minutes from Curitiba on the BR-277 and on the Nascentes do Iguaçu cycling route. More than a dozen purpose-built trails, roughly 20 km in total, through forest, hills and mountain views: flow sections mixed with mud, wet roots, off-camber chutes, small gaps and wooden bridges. Trails are named after regional wildlife - Serelepe (518 m, blue, 30 m of descent) and Trilha Pico Paraná among them. Lodge with fifteen suites, pools, sauna, gym and a restaurant, so it works as a weekend base rather than a lap spot.<br/><small>Nothing here is in OpenStreetMap except the park itself. Earlier text here listed Jaguarundi, Macaco Prego, Urubu-rei and Graxaim, which no reachable source confirms, and said the operator's site was offline - it is not.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal or push up the climbing routes; shuttles run occasionally for race events. Day-use entry around 20-40 BRL.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round, best from April through October; the Serra do Mar foothills are wet and the trails hold water outside that window.<br/>Daily opening hours: weekends and holidays<br/>
    <small>Mainly a weekend and holiday operation; confirm before travelling.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Curitiba</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Piraquara</td><td>Car / bike</td><td>~10 min</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the park's own <a href="https://www.facebook.com/cabikepark/">Facebook page</a> and <a href="https://www.canalaventura.com.br/">website</a>, plus its <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/region/canal-aventura-bike-park-45660/">Trailforks region</a> for the trail data. Pin moved onto the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/866646132">Canal Aventura Bike Park</a> object (way 866646132) on Trilha do Serelepe, measured at 970 m; it had been 33 km away at 1,486 m. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
