  <Placemark>
    <name>Keppoch Mountain (Nova Scotia, Canada) [shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Weekend shuttle drop-off around 218 m above Antigonish</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Almost 30 km of purpose-built mountain-bike trails range from beginner flow to expert natural and technical descents. The community-operated park also has a skills area, bike wash and repair station, and hosts downhill and enduro events.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Weekend bike shuttles carry riders to the upper trail network; pedal access is also possible. Buy a day or season pass through Keppoch and check capacity before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Published 2026 shuttle opening: 23 May. Standard service runs Saturday-Sunday, 10:00-17:00, generally through late October.<br/><small>Potential Friday evening services are announced separately.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Antigonish</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Halifax</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.thekeppoch.ca/events/bike-shuttle-opening-weekend">official 2026 shuttle opening</a> and <a href="https://novascotia.com/listing/keppoch-mountain/">Tourism Nova Scotia park information</a>. Pin marks the upper Summit West trailhead, elevation-checked at 218 m.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-62.113390,45.538780,218</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">ca-ns-keppoch</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert natural no-lift dh enduro freeride</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">05-23</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">10-26</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sugarloaf Bike Park (New Brunswick, Canada) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sugarloaf 45 m - valley station of the chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 49 km of riding and 36 listed trails combine Gravity Logic-built flow, jump lines, drops and wooden features with rocky expert downhill and year-round cross-country trails. The lower mountain includes a family skills park and pump track.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The chairlift serves the downhill network. Published 2026 full-day tickets are CAD 47.52 adult and CAD 39.60 youth/student/senior; rentals and one-ride tickets are available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Published 2026 bike-park season: 30 May-27 September. Weekends in spring and fall; Thursday-Sunday from late June through early September.<br/>Typical hours: 10:00-19:30 Thursday-Saturday and 10:00-16:30 Sunday in high summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Campbellton</td><td>Car / bike</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bathurst</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://sugarloafbikepark.ca/bike-park/">official bike-park overview and trail totals</a>, <a href="https://sugarloafbikepark.ca/tickets-passes/">2026 tickets and schedule</a> and the OSM-mapped chairlift. Pin marks its upper endpoint, verified at 195 m.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-66.695306,47.981508,47</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">ca-nb-sugarloaf</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">05-30</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-28</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sugarloaf Bike Park: top of the chairlift</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Chairlift top station 195 m - Atlantic Canada's original lift-access bike park</b><br/><br/>
    Top station of the chairlift, where the descents start. See the main Sugarloaf Bike Park pin for trails, prices and access.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-66.687140,47.976650,195</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">ca-nb-sugarloaf</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>None</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Poley Mountain Bike Park (New Brunswick, Canada) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Poley Mountain 90 m - valley station of the Quad Chair</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact gravity park with beginner-friendly flow, natural intermediate and expert descents, jumps and technical forest sections. Riders can combine the lift-served network with pedal-access multi-use trails; bike rentals are available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Quad Chair carries bikes. Poley sells day access and 2026 summer passes with or without chairlift access; the published adult lift-included season pass is CAD 300.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Published 2026 summer bike season runs June-October, with regular Friday-Sunday operations.<br/><small>Daily hours, lift choice and trail status vary; consult the current report before travelling.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sussex</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Saint John / Moncton</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.poleymountain.com/">official 2026 summer bike information</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/257027285">OSM Quad Chair way 257027285</a>. Pin marks the upper lift endpoint, verified at 278 m.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-65.381210,45.681907,89</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">ca-nb-poley</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">11-01</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Poley Mountain Bike Park: top of the Quad Chair</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Quad Chair top station 278 m - lift-served riding in the Waterford hills</b><br/><br/>
    Top station of the Quad Chair, where the descents start. See the main Poley Mountain Bike Park pin for trails, prices and access.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-65.376522,45.675925,278</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">ca-nb-poley</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>None</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark><name>Family Bike Park Zieleniec (PL) [cable car]</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Gryglowka and Nartorama - nearly 10 km of lift-served trails</b><br/><br/>Five signed routes range from gentle beginner flow to the steep natural Crazy Dad line. Cable cars carry bikes to the route starts; rentals and instruction are available.<br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://zieleniec.pl/en/lato/family-bike-park-zieleniec">official Family Bike Park Zieleniec</a>.</i>]]></description><styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>16.395700,50.336900,856</coordinates></Point><ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">zieleniec</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro gondola</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">05-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">10-31</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData></Placemark>
  <Placemark><name>Wierchomla Bike Park (PL) [chairlift]</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Dwie Doliny Wierchomla Mala - lift-served downhill and enduro</b><br/><br/>A Beskid gravity park with marked downhill and freeride lines, plus pedal-access forest routes. Expect natural roots and rocks between shaped sections.<br/><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://www.polska.travel/park-rowerowy-wierchomla/">Poland Travel park profile</a> and <a href="https://www.wierchomla.com.pl/">Wierchomla resort</a>.</i> Pin corrected to the valley station of the Wierchomla I chairlift (OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/203984316">way 203984316</a>), measured at 588 m: the pin had no lift of any kind within 4 km; the Dwie Doliny system's own Wierchomla I chairlift is 8.5 km north-east.]]></description><styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>20.822100,49.428930,588</coordinates></Point><ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">wierchomla</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-30</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData></Placemark>
  <Placemark><name>Bike Park Kluszkowce (PL) [chairlift]</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Wdjar mountain above Kluszkowce - compact gravity riding</b><br/><br/>A purpose-built park on the Wdjar ski slope with downhill, flow and jump lines including the A-line. The chairlift serves bike routes during summer operations.<br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://czorsztyn.pl/">Czorsztyn municipality and resort information</a>; confirm current schedules locally.</i> Pin corrected to the valley station of the Wyciag A chairlift (OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/144084428">way 144084428</a>), measured at 610 m: the pin sat in Kluszkowce village, 1.9 km from the Wdjar lift base the description describes riding from.]]></description><styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>20.314100,49.458540,610</coordinates></Point><ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">kluszkowce</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-30</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData></Placemark>
  <Placemark><name>Wadi Degla Protectorate MTB (Egypt) [no lift]</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Desert valley trail network on Cairo's southeastern edge</b><br/><br/>Wadi Degla is a protected 30 km limestone valley with rocky and sandy tracks used by Cairo mountain bikers. This is natural cross-country and all-mountain riding, not a formal lift park.<br/><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://cairo.gov.eg/ar/">Cairo Governorate reserve information</a> and local MTB route documentation.</i>]]></description><styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>31.340500,29.961500,129</coordinates></Point><ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">egypt-wadi-degla</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert natural no-lift enduro</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">01-01</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">01-01</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData></Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Pilatus: Pilatustrail</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>2.8 km technical natural trail</b><br/><br/>Named singletrack in the Pilatus area, with roots, tight turns and variable terrain. This is a natural mountain trail, not a maintained bike-park line.<br/><br/><i>Geometry simplified from <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/120875145">OpenStreetMap way 120875145</a>. Lift and access context: <a href="https://www.pilatus.ch/en/">Pilatus Bahnen</a>. Confirm bike carriage and local trail restrictions before riding.</i>]]></description>
