  <Placemark>
    <name>Abries-en-Queyras Bike Park (Hautes-Alpes) [14 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Abries 1550 m - valley station of the Gilly chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Four graded descents off the Gilly chairlift, one per colour: D1 La Verte de Gilly, a green introduction to flowing enduro; D2 La Peymian, blue, more technical with roots; D3 La Varenc, red, fast and steep; D4 La Viso, black and committing. Seven further enduro lines add up to 500 m of climbing each and descents approaching 1000 m of drop. The Queyras is one of the emptiest corners of the French Alps, and it rides that way.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Gilly six-seat chairlift from Abries at 1550 m. Day pass 14 EUR - among the cheapest lift-served riding in France. Wash-down and a repair area at the lift base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open daily in July and August except Tuesdays; check the operator for shoulder-season weekends.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00<br/><small>Closed on Tuesdays. Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Guillestre</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Briancon</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://lequeyras.com/en/according-to-my-nature/experiences/the-bike-park-a-bed-of-roses/">Queyras tourist office</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
