  <Placemark>
    <name>Montclar Bike Park (Alpes-de-Haute-Provence) [18.50 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Montclar 1335 m - valley station of the Belvedere chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Seven runs off the top of the Belvedere chairlift, all on 650 m of vertical and all long: the blue Chau Devant, 5 km of banked turns and smooth going under the larches; the reds A Fond la Souche, 12.6 km, wild and steep with bridges and tree-trunk crossings, and La Sentinelle, 8.5 km, the oldest and most flowing; and the blacks La Barjo, 4.5 km of steep, broken ground, La Molotof, 4.4 km straight under the chairlift with big jumps and bridges, and the short enduro-style La Merci Qui. A quiet park with a real reputation among downhill riders.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Belvedere chairlift from Montclar at 1335 m up to 1960 m. Day pass 18.50 EUR, sold at the lift or from the machine opposite the Hotel Saint-Jean.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from mid-May; closed from the end of October (operator's published window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gap</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Marseille</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.montclar.com/vtt/bike-park/">Station Montclar</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
