  <Placemark>
    <name>Cerkno Bike Park (Slovenia) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cerkno 955 m - valley station of the Pocivalo chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Seven trails, five of them lift-served and two enduro variants you pedal back up for. Marjetica is the easiest, a proper flow line with shaped berms and rollers that a beginner can ride and a quicker rider can jump; Snezet is the other flow trail, with profiled berms and small jumps. Everything finishes on the Pocivalo plateau. A sunny, south-facing hill, which is why the season runs from March to November - far longer than anywhere in the high Alps.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A fast six-seat chairlift fitted with bike hooks. The top station has a cycling centre with rental, a service point and guided rides. Prices are set each season by the resort - check before travel.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from mid-March; closed from mid-November (operator's stated long season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Ljubljana</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Nova Gorica</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="http://www.ski-cerkno.com/en/47">Ski Center Cerkno</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
