  <Placemark>
    <name>Airolo - Pesciuem (Ticino) [36 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Airolo 1180 m - valley station of the Airolo-Pesciuem cable car</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Six mapped descents: <b>Pineta Bike</b> and <b>Bosco Trail</b> (blue), <b>Runcasc Trail</b>, <b>Bosco Trail Variante</b> and <b>Sasso Trail</b> (red), and <b>Pascolo Bike</b> (black), which runs 6.4 km and 894 m from Sasso della Boggia to the valley. A growing Ticino park rather than a finished one, and it shows in a good way: the Runcasc and Bosco trails are recent additions and more are being cut. The mix is technical singletrack, flowing sections and old gravel and dirt roads, some hand-dug with no drops or jumps at all, some proper flow line - blue and red rather than black. Suitable for a first lift-served day and still interesting if you ride fast. The Swiss Enduro Series stops here.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Airolo-Pesciuem cable car from 1180 m to 1735 m, with a second cable car on to Sasso della Boggia and chairlifts around Ravina. Day pass about 36 CHF; the Pesciuem package at 30 CHF bundles a return with the daily menu at La Stua. Bike and e-bike hire on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from mid-June; closed from late October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Airolo station</td><td>Walk</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Lucerne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.airolo.ch/en/summer-activities/MTB-mountainbike-itineraries-airolo.php">Airolo tourism</a>, whose per-trail pages carry an official GPX export for each descent; the lines here come from those files. Note the Runcasc page prints a 563 m drop as "267 m" - its own GPX, and the cable car's 1180-1735 m span, say otherwise.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
