  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Grossglockner Resort - Kals (East Tyrol) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kals am Grossglockner 1345 m - valley station of the Kals I gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Three trails, 8.4 km between them, with the Grossglockner filling the view the whole way down. The Gornerwald is the original and the natural one, starting at the mid station and losing over 700 m across 4.7 km. The Adler runs 3.7 km through some 60 corners with small jumps and rollers and links into it, giving a long combined descent. The Temblerfelder is the short 650 m practice line, jump-heavy and aimed at riders learning to leave the ground.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Kals I gondola from 1345 m to the mid station at 1965 m, with Kals II continuing to 2390 m. Prices are set by the resort each summer - check before travel.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from mid-June; closed from the end of September (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lienz</td><td>Bus</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Salzburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.gg-resort.at/sommer/biken-im-sommer">Grossglockner Resort</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>12.640480,47.005910,1347</coordinates></Point>
