  <Placemark>
    <name>Soriska Planina Bike Park (Slovenia) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Soriska planina 1290 m - valley station of the Lajnar chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The operator says it plainly: experienced riders only. Zwau is the classic downhill - steep, tight corners, roots and jumps - and doubles as the race track for the Slovenian downhill cup. The Drauh enduro trail crosses varied natural ground with technical sections and long views. The line called Flow Trail is not one: sharp turns, rolling ground and enough demand on bike control to catch out anyone taking the name at face value. The long descent from the top of Lajnar through Kovce down to Podbrdo is the one to do once.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The two-seat Lajnar chairlift from 1290 m to 1520 m, running weekends and daily in the main summer season. Return, single, four-hour and day tickets; check the operator for current prices.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Weekends from mid-May, daily mid-July to late August, then weekends into October.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Skofja Loka</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Ljubljana</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://soriska-planina.si/bike-park">Soriska Planina</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
