  <Placemark>
    <name>Nauders - 3-Laender Enduro Trails (Tyrol) [50 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Nauders 1410 m - valley station of the Bergkastelbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Thirty singletrails, about 60 km of them and 2500 m of descent, spread across the corner where Austria, Italy and Switzerland meet - the three countries in the name, and you really can ride all of them in a day. Mostly natural enduro rather than shaped bike-park berms, with built flow lines and a beginner trail park filling in the easy end. The centrepiece on the Nauders side is the Bergkasteltrail, the longest run in the area at roughly 5 km from Stieralm to the valley, with northshores, doubles and tables at S1-S2. Start on the Zirmtrail: the operator recommends it for a first lap. Unusually dry ground for the Tyrol.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Six cable cars serve the network. On the Austrian side the Bergkastelbahn gondola climbs from Nauders at 1410 m to about 2180 m, with the Mutzkopf lift as the second Nauders access; the rest are at Reschen and St. Valentin over the Italian border. Day ticket 50.50 EUR adult, 38.50 EUR youth, 23 EUR child; half day from 14:00 is 29.50 EUR, three days 124.50 EUR, and a season pass 335.50 EUR. Shoulder-season weeks in mid-May and mid-October are about 15 percent cheaper.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-May to mid-October, matching the cable-car season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Landeck</td><td>Bus</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Innsbruck</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.3-laenderendurotrails.com/en">3-Laender Enduro Trails</a>, <a href="https://www.nauders.com/en/Your-Nauders/In-Summer/Biking/Enduro-Bike">Nauders tourism</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
