  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Bodetal - Rosstrappe (Harz, Germany) [35 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Thale 185 m - valley station of the Rosstrappe chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Six numbered trails dropping off the Rosstrappe cliff above the Bode gorge, up to 3.3 km long. Brunhildenritt (01) is an enduro line, easy up top and medium lower down; Harzer Roller (02) is the easy flow trail for beginners and families; Bodopass (03) is another easy line with big sweeping curves; the Rosstrappendownhill (04) is the hard one, with tables, doubles, road gaps, steep turns, a mud hole and a long bike bridge; Felsenweg (04a) is its connection; and Schwarze Koehlerliesel (05) is the black trail for experienced riders. Beginner and advanced options have been separated since 2020.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Rosstrappe chairlift from Thale at 185 m. The park itself is free to ride - you only pay for the lift. Day pass 35 EUR, single ride 5.50 EUR, with 10- and 20-point cards in between and cheaper rates for children aged 4-14.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Easter to October, daily, weather permitting.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-18:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Thale station</td><td>Walk</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Magdeburg</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bikepark-bodetal.de/">Bikepark Bodetal</a>, <a href="https://www.bodetal.de/urlaub-im-bodetal/seilbahnen-thale-erlebniswelt/bikepark-bodetal">Seilbahnen Thale</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
