  <Placemark>
    <name>Monte Alpet Bike Park - San Giacomo di Roburent (Piedmont) [18 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>San Giacomo di Roburent 980 m - valley station of the Monte Alpet chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Five named lines off Monte Alpet, all christened after musicians and getting harder in order: Beatles is the easy one, Bob Marley flows along an open ridge on natural rollers with a view over the plains (7-9 minutes), Rolling Stones mixes open ground with beech woods and technical features (7-10 minutes), Jim Morrison runs through beech and pine with roots, jumps and banked turns (8-12 minutes), and Nirvana is the hardest. A workshop, bike and protection rental, e-bikes, courses, a bike wash and a shuttle from nearby towns are all on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A two-seat chairlift from San Giacomo di Roburent at about 980 m up to Monte Alpet at 1611 m. Bike day pass 18 EUR, half day 13 EUR, five days 75 EUR, seven days 105 EUR.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Spring to late summer; the operator publishes opening days by phone rather than online.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mondovi</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Turin</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://mtbpiemonte.com/bike-park-monte-alpet/">MTB Piemonte</a> and <a href="https://www.visitcuneese.it/dettaglio-punto-di-interesse/-/d/monte-alpet-bike-village">Visit Cuneese</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i><br/><i>The park's own domain montealpetbikevillage.com has lapsed; reach the Bike Village on +39 0174 227560.</i>]]></description>
