  <Placemark>
    <name>La Grave Bike Park - La Meije (Hautes-Alpes) [from 28 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Grave 1455 m - valley station of the Glaciers de la Meije cable car</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Not a bike park in the shaped-and-signed sense: the cable car drops you at 3200 m on the Ruillans pass and the six itineraries off it carry no green-blue-red grading at all, because none of them would be green. Everything is technical and physical and expects real mountain experience. Warm up on Avag One, Desoutter or Cote Fine, which come closest to bike-park trails; Chavala, Vallons and the famous King Stone Road are proper singletrack, and from the top station King Stone Road gives 1800 m of unrelenting descent. The gentler counterpart is the FFC-marked network on the sunny side of the valley, 19 routes graded 1 green, 4 blue, 8 red and 6 black across more than 300 km of signed trail.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Glaciers de la Meije cable car from La Grave at 1455 m to the Ruillans pass at 3200 m. A mountain-bike day is 28 to 39 EUR depending on date; a five-ascent MTB card to 3200 m is 100 EUR.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-June to mid-September, the cable car's summer window.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Briancon</td><td>Bus</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Grenoble</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bike-oisans.com/vtt/bike-parks-en-oisans/la-grave-la-meije/">Bike Oisans</a>, <a href="https://www.hautesvallees.com/la-grave/en/que-faire/en-ete/vtt/vtt-au-telepherique/">Hautes Vallees tourism</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
