  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Area Streuboeden - Fieberbrunn (Tyrol) [66 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Fieberbrunn 835 m - valley station of the Streuboeden gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Four signed lines off the Streuboeden side, all of them on the friendly side of the grading: the Schweinestberg Line is the long one at 3.8 km of S1, the Streuboeden Line adds 2.8 km more of S1 from the second gondola section, and the Iglmoos Trail is the S2 option at 1.8 km. Beginners get the Haensn Practice Line, about 900 m of S0 served by its own tow lift, plus a shortcut variant and an airtime section for working up to jumps. A new 10-seat Streuboedenbahn replaced the old lift in 2024.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Streuboedenbahn gondola from Fieberbrunn at 839 m to the middle station at 1214 m (F1), a second section above it (F2), and the F5 Obingleitn tow for the practice line. The regional bike day ticket, valid on nine lifts across the Kitzbuehel Alps, is 66 EUR adult, 49.50 EUR youth and 33 EUR child; if you only want one ride, ascent and descent is 37 EUR adult plus 5 EUR to carry the bike.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>14 May to 1 November 2026. On the Lange Freitage, every Friday from 10 July to 4 September, the gondola runs until 19:00.<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00 (F1 and F2), 09:30-17:00 (F5)<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Fieberbrunn station</td><td>Walk</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Salzburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.fieberbrunn.com/linesandtrails">Fieberbrunn lines and trails</a>, <a href="https://www.fieberbrunn.com/en/summer/summer%20lifts/single%20trips">Fieberbrunn summer lifts</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
