  <Placemark>
    <name>Weissensee Bike Park (Carinthia) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Weissensee 960 m - valley station of the Weissensee Bergbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Three natural downhill routes, about 11.5 km together, all of them starting at the Naggler Alm and finishing by the lake. The Weissensee Trail is the short technical one at 2.7 km for 370 m of drop - root paths, hairpin bends, steep curves and a wave track - and the operator still calls it suitable for beginners. W13, the Panorama Trail, is 3.2 km for 376 m and the one to ride for the view. W12, the Naggl Trail, is the long one at 5.1 km for 380 m, varied the whole way and the pick for advanced riders, with root sections, tight corners and steep turns. A bike wash waits at the bottom.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A four-seat chairlift climbs 368 m from the lake at 956 m to 1324 m in about twelve minutes, with dedicated bike carriers, and every summer ticket includes carrying the bike up. Hourly, daily and multi-day fares are sold; the operator does not publish the bike day rate online, so ask at the valley station. Children under 10 ride free with a parent, bike included, and guests at PremiumCARD accommodation ride free. You can also pedal up on Route 5.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>1 May to 26 October 2026, with individual closure days. 09:00-16:00 in May and from late September, 09:00-17:00 from 4 June to 22 September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Hermagor</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Villach</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.weissensee.com/en/Summer-World/Bike-World/Trails">Weissensee bike world</a>, <a href="https://www.sommerbergbahnen-kaernten.at/bergbahnen/weissensee/">Carinthia summer mountain railways</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
