    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Trailpark Erbeskopf (Hunsrueck, Germany) [25 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Thalfang 695 m - valley station of the Erbeskopf lifts</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Five marked trails on the highest hill in Rhineland-Palatinate (816 m), right against the Hunsrueck-Hochwald national park. Blue Viper is the gentle one for beginners and families; Wild Cat and the newer Per Anhalter durch die Galaxis are the reds; Dirt Diggers is rougher; and the black Schinderhannes-Line has the stone fields, root carpets and jumps. Three further trails are still in planning. The Basecamp at the valley station has seating facing the slope, Commencal full-suspension and full-face rental, protectors and a bike wash. Helmets are compulsory and riders under 14 must be accompanied.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Erbeskopf ski lift. Day ticket 25 EUR adult, 20 EUR under-18; half day 20 EUR and 15 EUR; season pass 250 EUR and 170 EUR. If you would rather pedal up, the trail-only Strampel ticket is 10 EUR. Cash only. A shuttle from Kell to the Hunsrueckhaus can be booked in advance: 39 EUR for up to four people with an e-Kangoo and bike trailer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly April to October, weekends and Wednesdays only: Wednesday 12:00-19:00, Saturday and Sunday 10:00-17:00.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Trier</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Frankfurt</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://trailpark-erbeskopf.de/">Trailpark Erbeskopf</a> and <a href="https://trailpark-erbeskopf.de/elementor-449/">Trailpark Erbeskopf trail list</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
