  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikewelt Schoeneck (Vogtland, Germany) [24 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Schoeneck 630 m - valley station of the Hohe Reuth chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Five trails and about 5 km of riding, plus a 14,000 m2 practice area that is unusually large for a park this size. The Erich Popp Flowtrail is the 1.35 km beginner line; the Bockmuehlen Jumpline stacks up 34 jumps; Roll and Rock is the black downhill; and the Mosenbank-Pfad and Baerwurz-Trail are the two natural singletrails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A modern four-seat chairlift with bike transport. Day ticket 24 EUR adult, 15 EUR child; four hours 16 EUR and 9 EUR; ten rides 20 EUR and 13 EUR; two days 42 EUR and 26 EUR; season pass 240 EUR and 158 EUR.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The hybrid part is the schedule: the chairlift runs Friday to Sunday, and daily during the summer and autumn holidays. Monday to Thursday the place works as a trail centre - the trails are there, the lift is not.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Plauen</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Leipzig</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://schoeneck-vogtland.de/bike-und-wanderwelt/bikepark">Bikewelt Schoeneck</a>, <a href="https://schoeneck-vogtland.de/sommer/radfahren/bikepark/preise">Bikewelt Schoeneck prices</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
