  <Placemark>
    <name>Breckenridge Bike Park - Peak 8 (Colorado) [34 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Breckenridge 2910 m - valley station of the BreckConnect gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About ten lift-served singletrack descents on Peak 8, threading pine forest and crossing streams at close to 3000 m, which is high enough that the altitude is part of the difficulty. Swinger is the long flow line at 6.8 km, Edge runs 6.4 km with rolling terrain, Game Trail is 6.1 km of technical rock and water crossings, Dwights is the 4.7 km expert run with steep pitches and tight turns, and Frosty's Challenge drops steeply for 2 km into Wanderer. Aspen Alley fills in the middle. The town's much larger pedal-up network - Peaks Trail, Baker's Tank, the Flume trails - starts from the same base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The BreckConnect gondola carries bikes from town to the Peak 8 base; the Colorado SuperChair takes them up the mountain. An unlimited SuperChair day is 34 USD, a single ride up Rip's Ride 11 USD, and the gondola bike haul 23 USD. Prices are dynamic - check the day you go.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer, once the snow clears Peak 8, into early autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Frisco</td><td>Bus</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.breckenridge.com/travel-guide/mountain-biking-in-breckenridge.aspx">Breckenridge Resort biking guide</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail names and geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
