  <Placemark>
    <name>Whiteface Mountain Bike Park (New York) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Wilmington 365 m - valley station of the Cloudsplitter gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Twenty-seven trails on the biggest vertical drop in the eastern United States, and the spread is genuinely wide: expert-only natural singletrack from the summit of Little Whiteface, machine-built cruisers lower down, and a set of built features, jumps and rollers in between. The summit trails are the ones with the reputation - Whiteface has hosted national downhill racing - while beginners and intermediates get their own drop-off point partway up.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A daily bike pass covers unlimited rides on the Cloudsplitter gondola, a 15 to 20 minute haul to the summit of Little Whiteface, plus the shuttle bus that runs twice an hour to the intermediate and beginner start. ORDA sells the summer bike pass through its booking system rather than publishing a fixed rate, so check the price for your date.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-June through the autumn foliage season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lake Placid</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Montreal</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.whiteface.com/things-to-do/mountain-biking/">Whiteface Mountain (ORDA)</a> and <a href="https://apps.cio.ny.gov/apps/mediacontact/public/view.cfm?parm=96289439-FDA2-E443-566007D4642CA68D">New York State / ORDA press release</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
