  <Placemark>
    <name>Val Saint-Come Bike Park (Quebec) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Saint-Come 310 m - valley station of the main chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The most developed gravity riding in Lanaudiere, under 90 minutes from Montreal: nine finished trails plus extra lines, twelve in all, over 300 m of vertical, and what the resort claims is the largest jump line in eastern Canada. Beginner through expert, with a pro line at the top end. A cafeteria, restaurant-bar, rental fleet, workshop, bike wash and an inn with direct trail access are all on the mountain, and vanlife parking is free all summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A detachable chairlift with triple bike racks reaches the summit in three minutes. Day tickets are sold through the resort's own ticket shop; season passes are 165 CAD adult, 98 CAD child, 428 CAD for two adults and a child and 478 CAD for two adults and two children.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The 2026 bike season opens 20 June. Thursday 10:00-17:00, Friday and Saturday 10:00-19:00, Sunday 10:00-17:00.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Joliette</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Montreal</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.valsaintcome.com/velodemontagne/">Val Saint-Come mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.valsaintcome.com/ouverture-du-bike-park-2025-a-val-saint-come-le-10-juillet-une-saison-de-velo-de-montagne-a-ne-pas-manquer/">Val Saint-Come season announcement</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
