  <Placemark>
    <name>MbPark - Ski Mont-Blanc (Quebec) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Saint-Faustin-Lac-Carre 345 m - valley station of the Quad Faustin</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>MbPark opened in 2023 with 200 m of vertical, the biggest lift-served descent in the Laurentians, and its trails are named after the periodic table. Boule-a-mite is the easy 2.7 km way down; Azote (2.2 km), Cobalt (1.4 km) and Helium (900 m) are the intermediate lines; Carbone (1 km), Californium (800 m) and Baryum (700 m) step it up; and Hydrogene is the hard one, built in short steep sections. A pump track sits at the base next to the bar and restaurant, with rental and repair on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A dedicated lift carries riders and bikes to the summit. Prices are on the resort's tariff page; a full day started at 30 CAD for children aged 12 and under in 2026.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>June to October, weather permitting - the resort asks riders to check conditions before setting out.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mont-Tremblant</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Montreal</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://skimontblanc.com/en/velo-de-montagne/tarifs-velo-de-montagne-saison-2026/">Ski Mont-Blanc MbPark tariffs</a>, <a href="https://oberson.com/en/blogs/bike/best-bike-parks-quebec">Oberson bike-park guide</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail names and geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
