  <Placemark>
    <name>Isaberg Mountain Resort (Smaland, Sweden) [385 SEK]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Isaberg 240 m - valley station of the Superior lift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The biggest bike park in southern Sweden, and a lot of trail for a hill of 240 m: more than 25 marked lines colour-coded green to black, with flow trails, enduro descents, cross-country loops and freestyle areas sharing the same lift. Pelikanen is the green flow trail (2 km), Albatrossen the blue-red step up, Jaettestigen and The Nor Way the reds, and No Mercy - 620 m of steep, fast enduro - and Piece of Cake the blacks. Three downhill trails were added recently: two red enduro lines and a red jump trail down the steeper part of the ski slope.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift carries riders and bikes. BikePass 385 SEK adult, 330 SEK junior (7-14) for a day; four hours 270 and 235 SEK; two days 630 SEK; season 2995 SEK adult, 2550 SEK junior. Single rides are 70 SEK and the reloadable chip card another 70 SEK. <b>Passes are capped per day, so book online before you arrive.</b> Riders under 125 cm need someone over 140 cm with them on the chairlift.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Lift-served riding from early May. Daily from midsummer to mid-August (weeks 26-32), weekends either side, and on into the autumn weekends through week 44.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gislaved</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Gothenburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.isaberg.com/en/activities/mountainbike/mtb-trails/">Isaberg MTB trails</a>, <a href="https://www.isaberg.com/en/activities/mountainbike/bikepass-buy-info/">Isaberg BikePass</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
