  <Placemark>
    <name>Gressoney - Weissmatten (Monterosa, Aosta Valley) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gressoney-Saint-Jean 1370 m - valley station of the Weissmatten chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A small, young bike operation on the Weissmatten side of Gressoney-Saint-Jean, where the chairlift carries bikes to 2023 m and a single demanding downhill track drops back to the village - close to 700 m of vertical, and squarely for confident riders. The wider valley adds lift-served descents from Punta Jolanda in Gressoney-La-Trinite and from the Stafal lifts towards Passo dei Salati and Colle Bettaforca, so a few days here can be strung together across three lift systems.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Weissmatten chairlift, 1348 m to 2023 m, takes bikes. The operator publishes its summer tariff as a PDF each season rather than on a page - a promotional lift ticket during the late-June Festa della Birra was 6 EUR, with under-nines free alongside a paying adult, which is not the normal rate. Rental in the village at Bergland or Monterosa Experience.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late June for the beer-festival weekend, Thursday to Sunday in July, then daily from 1 to 30 August. 08:45-13:00 and 14:30-17:00.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Pont-Saint-Martin</td><td>Bus</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Turin</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://visitmonterosa.com/esperienze/orari-e-tariffe-impianti-di-risalita-gressoney-saint-jean-estate-2026-21498">Visit Monterosa lift hours and tariffs</a>, <a href="https://www.gressoneymonterosa.it/en/bike-21529">Gressoney Monterosa bike</a> and <a href="https://www.lovevda.it/it/banca-dati/5/impianti-di-risalita/gressoney-saint-jean/seggiovia-weissmatten/4127">Regione Valle d'Aosta lift database</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
