  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Sybelles - Le Corbier (Maurienne) [10 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Le Corbier 1570 m - valley station of the Sybelles Express</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Sixteen marked downhill runs across the Sybelles domain above Le Corbier: one green, eight blue, five red and three black, which makes it one of the more beginner-heavy gravity areas in the Maurienne. Saute Mouton is the blue to start on, reached from the Sybelles Express and built with alternative lines so it stays interesting as you get faster. The Mont Corbier descent is the classic long run.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Sybelles Express detachable chairlift, working between 1570 m and 2220 m. A day is 10.30 EUR, or 8.20 EUR with a Skiogrande card; a two-person day comes to 20 EUR. Passes are bought at the lift ticket offices in the resort centre. Downhill bike rental including lift and protection runs around 85 EUR a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>4 July to 28 August 2026.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saint-Jean-de-Maurienne</td><td>Bus</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Grenoble</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.le-corbier.com/vtt-itineraire-montagne/">Le Corbier MTB</a> and <a href="https://www.sybelles.ski/en/experiences/les-sybelles-by-bike/mountain-biking-fat-biking/">Les Sybelles by bike</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
