  <Placemark>
    <name>Viola St Gree Bike Park (Piedmont) [20 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Viola 1055 m - valley station of the Pian del Bal chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the better-regarded downhill parks in Italy, in the Maritime Alps above Cuneo, and the trail set is unusually long for the vertical: Ottovolante is the easy one at 2.9 km for 579 m of drop, Sentiero Blu a 4 km blue flow line, Freccia Rossa 3.4 km of red for 502 m, the Freeride Line 3 km of natural ground, and the Black Line the expert descent. Saltimbanco, newer at 4.5 km, is the one built purely for line, speed and flow.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The San Grato-Pian del Bal two-seat chairlift, renewed in 2011, is the same lift the skiers use. Day 20 EUR adult, half day 18 EUR (09:00-13:00 or 13:00-17:00); under-12s 18 and 16 EUR; season pass 240 EUR adult, 190 EUR child.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late April to November, weekends, Mondays and public holidays, weather permitting.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mondovi</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Savona</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="http://www.stgree.net/">St Gree Performance</a>, <a href="https://www.visitcuneese.it/dettaglio-punto-di-interesse/-/d/bike-park-viola-st-gree">Visit Cuneese</a> and <a href="https://www.mtb-mania.it/bike-park-viola-st-gree-in-piemonte/">MTB Mania</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
