  <Placemark>
    <name>Idre Fjall Bikeland (Dalarna, Sweden) [165 SEK]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Idre Fjall 580 m - valley station of the Sydgondolen</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Idre Fjall calls the whole thing Bikeland, and the character is flowing curves rather than sharp ones - a good place to try lift-served riding for the first time and still worth a day if you can already ride. Green lines include Akka, Fjallet runt and Gondoljaren; the blues are Alla kan, Askeleden, Jippi Blue and the blue versions of Ner ska du and Straight Rhythm; the reds add drops and technical features - Enduroleden, Stigdrommar and the red versions of Ner ska du and Straight Rhythm. A separate cross-country network shares the hill.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A lift day for downhill is 165 SEK for an adult; the cross-country trail pass alone is 100 SEK a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn - mountain biking is the resort's headline warm-season activity.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mora</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr><tr><td>Stockholm</td><td>Car</td><td>~5h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.idrefjall.se/en/biking/">Idre Fjall Bikeland</a>, <a href="https://www.idrefjall.se/cykling-pa-idre-fjall/downhill/">Idre Fjall downhill</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail names and geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
