  <Placemark>
    <name>Gesundaberget Bike Park (Dalarna, Sweden) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gesunda 270 m - valley station of the Knapp drag lift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A hill of 514 m standing 353 m above Lake Siljan, and one of Sweden's more serious downhill venues: four machine-groomed trails from green to black plus around ten natural lines from blue to, in the operator's own words, extremely black - among them a downhill track that has held national championship rounds. The longest run is about 1.8 km. Mapped lines on the hill include Magic Carpet, G.M.X, Xcelerator, Caro-Line, Stokspar, Zigzag and Skogsmus. The view over Siljan has three stars in the Michelin Green Guide.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift to the top, where a trail map shows the marked descents. Helmets and body armour can be rented. The operator quotes lift prices on request - bokning@tomteland.se or +46 250 287 70 - rather than publishing them.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mora</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Stockholm</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="http://www.gesundaberget.se/">Gesundaberget Royal Park</a>, <a href="https://www.freeride.se/sveriges-7-basta-bikeparks/">Freeride magazine</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail names and geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
