  <Placemark>
    <name>Mt Baw Baw Bike Park (Victoria, Australia) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mt Baw Baw 1455 m - valley station of the Maltese Cross t-bar</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One serious descent and a set of pedal trails, on Melbourne's closest alpine resort. DH1 has a reputation across Australian riding: a big wall ride, then the old chairlift line and the Jeep Track, 300 m of vertical that the fastest riders take in a little over three and a half minutes, with B-line bypasses around the harder features for riders working up to it. Around it, Upper Tyers, Tanjil Link and Mueller's are the cross-country lines, and the Summit, Village and McMillan trails are the gentle ones.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No mechanical uplift in summer</b> - the resort is explicit that for DH1 you arrange your own shuttle. <b>Access to the trails is free.</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The green season runs roughly October to May, and DH1 specifically from the end of November to late April, seven days a week apart from major event weekends.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Warragul</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Melbourne</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mountbawbaw.com.au/activities/mountain-bike-trails/">Mt Baw Baw mountain bike trails</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
