  <Placemark>
    <name>Le Massif de Charlevoix Bike Park (Quebec) [75 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Petite-Riviere-Saint-Francois 440 m - base of the Le Massif gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The longest vertical drop east of the Canadian Rockies, and nearly 55 km of trail built on it: 23 gravity-fed enduro runs, two skills zones, a pro line, family loops and longer adventure routes. Histoire sans fin is the marathon descent at over 5 km; Easy Rider and 6 Pack are the approachable lines; La Cigale and La Fourmi the technical ones; Basilic, Bus Jaune, La Grande Liguori, Ping Pong and Funk Funghi fill the middle. Cerise sur le Sundae is 3 km of beginner riding with the St Lawrence below you the whole way.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The gondola carries riders and bikes. Day pass 75 CAD adult, 60 CAD half day; 53 CAD for 13-17 and 38 CAD for 7-12; under-7s free; a family of four 216 CAD. Season pass from 376 CAD adult on presale. Rocky Mountain rental fleet on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>20 June to 12 October 2026.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Baie-Saint-Paul</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Quebec City</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.lemassif.com/en/activities-events/charlevoix-attractions/mountain-bike-trail-quebec">Le Massif mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail names and geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
