  <Placemark>
    <name>ZugerbergTrail (Zug, Switzerland) [27 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Schoenegg 560 m - valley station of the Zugerberg funicular</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One trail, done properly. The ZugerbergTrail runs 2.1 km from the Zugerberg mountain station via Juchenegg down to Schoenegg, the funicular's valley station, and it is packed: berms, jumps, wallrides, bridges, ladder bridges, drops, gap jumps, rock gardens and roller sections, with a bypass around every obstacle. Graded easy to moderate, which undersells how much fun it is to ride fast. It is a joint project of IG Mountainbike Zug, the Korporation Zug and the Zugerberg Bahn, shaped and maintained by volunteers since 2016 - hence the Shape Days on the calendar.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Zugerberg Bahn funicular carries riders and bikes. A bike day pass is 27 CHF, bought at the valley station, and the money goes into trail upkeep.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn, subject to the funicular's maintenance windows and the trail-status light on zugerbergtrail.ch - check it before you drive.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Zug station</td><td>Bus</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Zurich</td><td>Train</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://zugerbergtrail.ch/">ZugerbergTrail</a>, <a href="https://www.zbb.ch/freizeit-oase/zugerberg-erlebnisse/zugerberg-trail/">Zugerberg Bahn</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail names and geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
