  <Placemark>
    <name>Boyne Mountain Bike Park (Michigan) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Boyne Falls 220 m - valley station of the Mountain Express</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around 82 marked trails, at least 3 green, 4 blue, 6 black and 2 double black, on roughly 130 m of vertical in northern Michigan. Small drop, big trail count - the riding is built flow and jump lines rather than descent, and it is the main lift-served gravity venue in the Great Lakes region.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Mountain Express and several other chairlifts from 220 m to about 350 m. Check the operator for the summer bike ticket.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly mid-May to mid-October.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:00<br/><small>Estimated; not yet checked against the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Petoskey</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Detroit</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.boynemountain.com/">Boyne Mountain Resort</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
