  <Placemark>
    <name>Mission Ridge (Wenatchee, Washington) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mission Ridge 1395 m - valley station of Chair 4</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Set what you expect here carefully. Mission Ridge is a 2000-acre ski area twelve miles from Wenatchee on the dry eastern side of the Cascades, and there is mountain biking on and around it - but it is natural trail shared with dirt bikes rather than a built, lift-served bike park, and the resort publishes no bike-park trail list, grading or summer bike tariff.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No published lift-served bike operation.</b> Ride the area trails under your own power, or check with the resort before assuming a lift will run.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn, once the snow clears.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Wenatchee</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Seattle</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.missionridge.com/">Mission Ridge Ski and Board Resort</a> and <a href="https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/7039232/mission-ridge">MTB Project - Mission Ridge trail</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
