  <Placemark>
    <name>Azuga Mountain Bike Resort (Prahova valley, Romania) [60 RON]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Azuga 984 m - valley station of the Sorica gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Azuga Bike Resort has some of the strongest downhill riding in Romania, laid out on the Sorica side of the Prahova valley - the same face as the FIS-homologated Sorica ski piste, over 2100 m long with 561 m of drop, so the terrain underneath the trails is serious.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Azuga gondola, which runs year round and carries bikes on external racks: 980 m to 1540 m in about six minutes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The gondola runs through the summer for riders and walkers.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Brasov</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bucharest</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://azugaresort.ro/">Azuga Ski and Bike Resort</a> and <a href="https://info-turism-azuga.ro/agrement/">Azuga tourism</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
