  <Placemark>
    <name>Flottsbro Bikepark (Huddinge, Sweden) [230 SEK]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Flottsbro 9 m - valley station of the chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The most developed downhill system in Stockholm county, twenty minutes from the city, graded UK-style and covering everything from first-timer to experienced. The trails are built for speed and flow rather than raw steepness - the hill does not have the vertical for anything else - and the park runs private lessons and technique workshops for riders starting out. Full-suspension bikes, helmets and body armour all rent on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A lift serves the hill; the park sells day and season Bikepasses.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>1 May (Valborg) to the end of October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Stockholm centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Huddinge station</td><td>Bus</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.flottsbro.se/en/bike-park-downhill-in-stockholm/">Flottsbro Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.flottsbro.se/bike-park-i-stockholm/bikepass/">Flottsbro Bikepass</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
