  <Placemark>
    <name>Skalafell Bike Park (Iceland) [3500 ISK]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Skalafell 446 m - valley station of the Stolalyfta chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Iceland's first bike park, designed and built in 2010 on a ski hill within reach of Reykjavik, and it grows by roughly one trail a year. Several descents drop the mountain alongside the hiking paths. Bike rental on site through Pukinn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Iceland's longest ski lift carries riders and bikes up; walkers can ride it too.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer, once the ground has dried out - the opening date moves with the weather, so check before driving up.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Reykjavik</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Keflavik airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://skidasvaedi.is/en/skalafell/skalafell-bike-park/">Skalafell Bike Park (Skidasvaedin)</a> and <a href="https://icebikeadventures.com/iceland-bikepark/">Icebike Adventures, who built the trails</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
