  <Placemark>
    <name>Sugarbush Bike Park (Vermont) [60 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lincoln Peak 496 m - valley station of the Super Bravo Express</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around 41 marked runs at Lincoln Peak, with at least 2 green, 15 blue, 5 black and 4 double-black - a full-spectrum park and one of the larger ones in Vermont. Roughly 470 m of lift-served vertical on classic New England forest, so rock, root and steep pitches rather than manicured flow.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Super Bravo Express quad from 496 m to about 965 m, with the Gate House quad serving the lower mountain. Around 60 USD for a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly mid-June to mid-October, weekends at the shoulders.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><small>Estimated; not yet checked against the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Burlington</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.sugarbush.com/">Sugarbush Resort</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
