  <Placemark>
    <name>RED Mountain Bike Park (Rossland, BC) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Red base 1160 m - valley station of the Silverlode chair</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Lift-accessed riding came to Rossland when RED opened its bike park, built by Gravity Logic, and it plugs into a valley with more than 200 km of trail around it - beginner routes through to expert terrain. Rossland has been a mountain-bike town far longer than it has had a lift-served park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift. Tickets are cheaper bought online, up to 10 percent off; everyone needs a 5 CAD RFID card, free with a season pass. Rentals are 65 CAD a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Tuesday to Sunday, 09:00-17:00, through to 21 September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Rossland</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Spokane</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.redresort.com/bikepark/">RED Mountain Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.redresort.com/summer-tickets/">RED Mountain summer tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
