  <Placemark>
    <name>Horseshoe Valley Bike Park (Ontario) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Horseshoe Valley 269 m - valley station of the Trailblazer chair</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Fourteen trails covering every level on the hill above Barrie, all reached from one lift. Modest vertical, but the lift is quick enough that lap counts do the work. A Dual Access ticket pairs a day here with a Hardwood trail ticket next door.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Copeland Express, a high-speed six-person chairlift. Day tickets and season passes are sold online; twilight tickets are half price every Tuesday from 30 June to 1 September 2026.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Friday to Sunday in May, June, September and October; seven days a week in July and August. 10:00-20:00.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-20:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Barrie</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Toronto</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://horseshoeresort.com/biking/">Horseshoe Valley Resort biking</a> and <a href="https://horseshoeresort.com/bike-lift-tickets-rentals/">Horseshoe bike lift tickets and rentals</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
