  <Placemark>
    <name>Mont-Belu Bike Park (La Baie, Quebec) [31 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Baie 24 m - valley station of the chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Six enduro trails, a jump line and the Fjord trail on the hill above La Baie in the Saguenay - natural descents rather than machine-shaped flow, which is what the place is known for. Bypass sections have been cut through the hardest parts so beginners and intermediates can ride the same trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A T-bar runs Wednesdays 16:00-20:00 and Sundays 10:00-16:00 only. Outside those hours the mountain is open around the clock thanks to a 3 km climbing trail, about 25-30 minutes at a steady pace. Day and season passes, with student and child rates, sold at the hill or through Chicoutimi bike shops.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saguenay</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Quebec City</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://montbelu.com/page/velo-de-montagne">Centre de ski Mont-Belu - velo de montagne</a> and <a href="https://saguenaylacsaintjean.ca/attrait/quoi-faire/mont-belu">Saguenay-Lac-Saint-Jean tourism</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
