  <Placemark>
    <name>Granite Gorge Mountain Park (New Hampshire) [30 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Roxbury 251 m - valley station of the Pinnacle double chair</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A revived ski area on Pinnacle Mountain five miles east of Keene, whose bike park opened in 2023 and is still growing: three trails so far - Reptar, Chuck It and Bombs Away - covering wide flowing ground and steeper lines with rock, stumps, beams and jumps. The skills park is free during opening hours and needs no lift ticket.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift, and the rule is simple - if the park is open, the lift is running. Recent rates were 30 USD for a Saturday or Sunday day and 15 USD for the Friday 16:00-19:00 session. Bar and grill at the base, plus scenic lift rides, events and concerts.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Friday evenings and weekends through the summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Keene</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://granitegorge.com/bike-park/">Granite Gorge Mountain Park - bike park</a> and <a href="https://explorekeene.org/places/biking/granite-gorge-mountain-park/">Explore Keene</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
