  <Placemark>
    <name>Manzherok Bike Park (Altai, Russia) [1500 RUB, 2023 rate]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Manzherok 377 m - valley station of the Chuysky Trakt gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The resort's own bike-park page lists six graded runs on Malaya Sinyukha above Lake Manzherok, about 12.1 km of trail in total: Pikhtovaya (4,960 m, 210 m of descent), Novichok (3,410 m / 70 m), Sinyukha (1,920 m / 169 m), Uchebnaya (800 m / 35 m, the practice line), Skalistaya (760 m / 111 m) and Nunatak (470 m / 128 m). Green through black, with built drops, counter-slopes, steep turns and wooden skills features, and a downhill school running regular masterclasses. This was the first purpose-built bike park east of the Urals; the original downhill park measured about 7 km, so the network has roughly doubled. Eco-trails through the Guardian of the Greater Altai park share the mountain in summer.<br/><small>No trail lines are drawn here: none of the six runs is in OpenStreetMap. A named-way, mtb-tag and bike-park sweep of the whole massif returns nothing at all.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A large lift system - six gondolas and four chairlifts, among them the Legend 390 gondola running out over the lake - with free parking at the base. Bikes ride in specially fitted cabins and on equipped chairs; there is a free bike wash, a service point and mountain-bike and downhill-bike rental on site. The current bike pass is sold only at the resort cash desks and published as a downloadable PDF rather than on the page, so the figures here are the last ones this map could read: the 2023 tariff was 1,500 RUB for an unlimited day and 1,200 RUB for a single ascent from July, 1,300 / 1,000 RUB in June, plus 150 RUB for the contactless card on a first purchase. Expect 2026 to be higher and confirm before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 June; closed from 01 October (typical Altai summer window; the resort does not publish exact bike-park dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-19:00<br/><small>Published bike-park hours, Monday to Sunday, subject to weather. Manzherok has been through major lift and trail redevelopment; confirm which runs and which bike-carrying lifts are open.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gorno-Altaysk airport</td><td>Car / taxi</td><td>30-40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Manzherok village</td><td>Car / taxi</td><td>10-15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Barnaul</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the resort's <a href="https://xn--80akcrghjp.xn--p1ai/summer-activities/bike-park">official bike-park page</a> (trail list, lengths, drops and hours), <a href="https://xn--80akcrghjp.xn--p1ai/summer-activities/mazheroker/downhill-school">downhill school</a>, <a href="https://xn--80akcrghjp.xn--p1ai/mountains/cableways">resort cableways</a> and <a href="https://xn--80akcrghjp.xn--p1ai/walking-tickets">summer tickets</a>, with the <a href="https://rider-skill.ru/apres-skies/manzherok/bajk-park-na-kurorte-manzherok-trassy-i-tarify-na-2023-god/">2023 published tariffs</a> for the price. Pin and lift altitudes measured on the OSM gondola and chairlift endpoints. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
