  <Placemark>
    <name>Sodra Berget Bikepark (Sundsvall, Sweden) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sundsvall 78 m - valley station of the drag lift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Green, blue, red and black trails running from the outdoor centre on Sodra Berget, built into the terrain with wooden bridges and jumps rather than bulldozed through it. Sundsvall has put 13 million SEK into the Bike Arena, so the network is still growing.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The lift at Sidsjobacken runs extended summer hours for riders. A Bike Pass covers both the lift and the Bike Arena trail fee. If you do not have a Teamaxess card, one is 50 SEK on site; a full protection set - helmet, body armour, gloves, knee pads and jersey - is 200 SEK a day. Children under 8 ride free with an adult.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The trails themselves are open around the clock in season; the lift runs to its own summer timetable.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sundsvall centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Ostersund</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.sodraberget.se/bikepark">Sodra Berget Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
