  <Placemark>
    <name>Ale Bikepark (Sweden) [180 SEK]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ale 15 m - valley station of the Ankarlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A club hill rather than a resort: downhill has run here since 2006 under the non-profit Alebacken SK, and the park has hosted rounds of the Swedish downhill cup. Alebacken Bikepark looks after the gravity trails and Ale 90 IK the cross-country and trail riding on the same hill.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The ski lift. Day pass 180 SEK adult, 140 SEK up to 18, 60 SEK up to 10. Cash or Swish only. Opening days go up on the club's Facebook page rather than a website, so check before setting off.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer season, run by volunteers.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gothenburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Alvangen station</td><td>Train + bike</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://happyride.se/sveriges-basta-bikeparks/">Happyride guide to Swedish lift-served bike parks</a> and <a href="https://www.freeride.se/sveriges-7-basta-bikeparks/">Freeride magazine</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
