  <Placemark>
    <name>Nordfjord Stisenter (Stryn, Norway) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Stryn 337 m - valley station of the Hovudheisen</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The directory lists only 1 marked blue run, which badly understates the terrain: the Hovudheisen drag climbs 333 m and the Steindalsheisen above it reaches 971 m, so the hill carries well over 600 m of uplift-served vertical in the fjord country of Nordfjord. Uplift is by drag lift, not chair. Expect far more unmarked riding than the listing suggests.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Hovudheisen drag lift from 337 m to about 670 m, with the Steindalsheisen continuing to 971 m. The directory lists no price. Check the operator.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly mid-June to mid-September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><small>Estimated; not yet checked against the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Stryn</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Alesund</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.nordfjord.no/">Visit Nordfjord</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
