  <Placemark>
    <name>Traktor Bike Park (Gjovik, Norway) [shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gjovik 191 m - valley station of the drag lift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Built by hand in the forest from summer 2009 onwards, around an old bulldozer road - hence the name - with north shore woodwork and side lines threaded off the main descent. 300 m of vertical over 2.5 km. It sits between cross-country and downhill: a trail bike with 120-130 mm is enough, though an enduro bike is more fun, and the builders recommend a full-face, knee and elbow pads, and tough tyres because the ground eats thin ones.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - this is shuttle-served riding.</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gjovik centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Oslo</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="http://www.traktorbike.no/park.php">Traktor Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.terrengsykkel.no/stisykling/traktor-bike-park">Terrengsykkel on Traktor Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
