  <Placemark>
    <name>Glenshee Bike Park (Cairngorms, Scotland) [15 GBP]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cairnwell pass 652 m - valley station of the Cairnwell chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The directory lists around 29 trails with no difficulty breakdown; as with other ski areas that figure may include riding beyond the lift-served park. Uplift is from the top of the Cairnwell pass at 652 m - already high ground for Britain - on roughly 240 m of vertical, over bare, wind-scoured Cairngorm hillside with a dozen further tows across the bowl. Confirm the summer bike operation before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Cairnwell chairlift from 652 m to about 893 m, with the Sunnyside and Baddoch chairs and a large network of pomas and t-bars alongside. Around 15 GBP for a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly June to the end of September, weather permitting.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:30<br/><small>Estimated; not yet checked against the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Braemar</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Perth</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://glenshee.org/">Glenshee</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
