  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Kato Bike Park (Mankato, Minnesota) [5 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mankato 240 m - valley station of chair 8</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around 21 marked runs on the Minnesota river bluffs, with at least 8 green, 7 blue and 6 black - a broad spread on only about 70 m of vertical. Eight chairlifts serve the hill, and at 5 USD it is close to the cheapest lift ticket of any park on this map.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chair 8 from 240 m to about 307 m, with seven more chairs across the hill. Around 5 USD for a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The directory gives a 27 April start; roughly late April to the end of October.<br/>Daily opening hours: 16:00-20:00<br/><small>Season start from the directory listing; hours estimated - largely an evening hill.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mankato</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Minneapolis</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://mountkato.com/">Mount Kato</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
