  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park Bovec (Soca valley, Slovenia) [5 EUR per shuttle run]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cezsoca 369 m - the Soca valley's first purpose-built bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two hand-built shuttle runs above the village of Cezsoca, 2 km from Bovec, opened on 31 May 2025. <b>Airline</b> is the flow and jump line at 1.4 km, built with alternative lines and ride-arounds so it works from first laps upwards. <b>Jungle Line</b> is the 1.3 km natural counterpart - gaps, drops, step-ups, roots and rock - and the operator puts it squarely in experienced-rider territory. That is the whole park for now; there is no published third trail.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> A van shuttles riders to the top: 5 EUR a run, with 4-hour and full-day shuttle passes alongside cheaper pedal and e-bike passes. Only the single-run price is published on the site; the pass rates appear in the booking flow.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Season opens 4 April 2026 and runs to the end of October. The shuttle runs Friday to Sunday in April, May, September and October and daily in July and August; June shuttle days are not published, so confirm before travelling. Trails are open 09:00-18:00 in April, May, September and October, and 09:00-19:00 from June to August.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-19:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bovec</td><td>Car / bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Kobarid</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Ljubljana</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bikeparkbovec.com/">Bike Park Bovec</a> and the <a href="https://www.slovenia.info/en/press-centre/news-of-the-tourism-press-agency/33239-adrenaline-awaits-new-bike-park-in-bovec-now-open">Slovenian tourist board opening announcement</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
