  <Placemark>
    <name>Alpen Bikepark Schneeberg - Losenheim (Austria) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Losenheim 881 m - valley station of the Schneeberg four-seat chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 12 km of trail under Lower Austria's highest mountain, and eight named lines to spend it on. Easy Rider Trail and the Schneeberg Line are the gentle ones; Rock'n'Roots, the Lahning-Ries-Line and the Alm-Trail sit in the middle; and Black Snake and Hard Rock are the hard end. The mix is flow, tech and airtime, shaped into natural forest ground rather than bulldozed, and the network is being extended towards 15 km by 2028. At the valley station the Riders Playground adds a pump track, a BAGJUMP airbag and a kids area.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A four-seat chairlift built in 2005, from 840 m up to 1210 m, dropping you at the trailhead. Tickets are sold through the park's own shop rather than printed on the site. Rental, courses and food on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Puchberg am Schneeberg</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Vienna</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://alpen-bikepark.at/">Alpen Bikepark Schneeberg</a> and <a href="https://www.wieneralpen.at/ausflug-freizeit/alpen-bikepark-losenheim">Wiener Alpen tourism</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
