  <Placemark>
    <name>Flowtrail Stromberg (Hunsruck, Germany) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Stromberg 231 m - the bottom of the Flowtrail network</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around 6 marked runs, at least 2 green and 1 blue - one of Germany's best-known flowtrail centres, and the model many others copied. OpenStreetMap names the individual lines: the Rundkurs, the No Jokes Trail, the Wild Hog Trail and Die Sieben Kleeberge, spread over roughly 225 m of Hunsruck hillside.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Everything is pedalled - the network is built as climb-and-descend loops. Free to ride; the trails are maintained by donation and volunteer days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The directory gives a 1 April start; roughly April to mid-November.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Season start from the directory listing; hours estimated. Trails close after heavy rain to protect the surface.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bingen</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Frankfurt</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.flowtrail-stromberg.de/">Flowtrail Stromberg</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
