  <Placemark>
    <name>Campo Imperatore Gravity (Gran Sasso, Italy) [10 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Campo Imperatore 2123 m - the high plateau below the Gran Sasso</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>High, open and serious: the cable car from Fonte Cerreto lifts you onto the Campo Imperatore plateau under the Gran Sasso, and three or four long alpine descents run off it. Vallone della Portella climbs to the Passo del Lupo before winding down the valley; Tre Valloni drops steeply beneath the cable-car line then cuts left back to Fonte Cerreto; Valle Fredda leaves the observatory square and follows the ridge towards Monte Scindarella. This is mountain terrain, not a shaped park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Fonte Cerreto cable car. A return ticket for a rider is about 8 EUR, or 10 EUR with the bike. Check the operating days before you go - they are not daily.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer, while the cable car runs.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>L'Aquila</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Rome</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://itinerari.mtb-mag.com/tours/view/10210">MTB-MAG - Campo Imperatore Gravity</a> and <a href="http://www.gransassobikeday.it/">Gran Sasso Bike Day</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
