  <Placemark>
    <name>Ober Mountain Bike Park (Gatlinburg, Tennessee) [49 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gatlinburg 406 m - valley station of the Ober Mountain aerial tramway</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eleven or more downhill trails above Gatlinburg, from beginner lines to black diamonds. Riders describe it as on the tamer side with little technical ground - the blacks are steep rather than rocky - which makes it a good place to build downhill confidence rather than a destination for hard riding. Helmets are mandatory; rentals, pads and lessons on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The aerial tramway and the mountain's lifts. The bike-park day fee is 49 USD, includes lift access and the park's other attractions; a mountain-bike season pass runs 249-299 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>May to September, with trails closed for rain and bad weather.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gatlinburg centre</td><td>Walk</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Knoxville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://obermountain.com/downhill-mountain-biking/">Ober Mountain downhill mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.obermountain.com/tickets">Ober Mountain tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
