  <Placemark>
    <name>Freeman Ridge Bike Park (Kingfield, Maine) [10 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kingfield 221 m - the Freeman Ridge bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A private, family-run network on Freeman Ridge Road a mile out of Kingfield: about five miles of hand- and machine-built trail across some twenty lines, gravity-fed and laid out for progression, and still growing.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Adult day pass 10 USD, junior 5 USD; season passes 50 and 25 USD. Every rider needs a pass and a signed waiver, and riding is only allowed during posted hours when staff are on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The Maine riding season, during staffed hours only.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kingfield</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Portland, ME</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.freemanridgebike.com/">Freeman Ridge Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.freemanridgebike.com/rates-hours">Freeman Ridge rates and hours</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
