  <Placemark>
    <name>417 Bike Park (Gloucestershire, England) [43 GBP uplift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gloucestershire 183 m - Flyup 417 Bike Park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the largest privately owned bike parks in Britain, opened on Crickley Hill in 2016 and now much more than a set of downhill runs: gravity trails from blue to double black, an indoor Velosolutions pump track, a dirt-jump field with progressive lines, a 4X track and a dual slalom. Coaching, kids' clubs and bike and helmet hire on site, which is why it has a reputation as a place young riders progress fast.<br/><small>Only one line is drawn here: <b>Flowblerone</b> (blue) is the single 417 run OpenStreetMap has mapped. The rest of the park is not in OSM at all, so the map understates it - use the park's own trail map.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The uplift is the draw. Uplift pass 43 GBP; admission without uplift 18.50 GBP, youth 10 GBP, e-bike 21.50 GBP; the indoor pump track is 7 GBP, or 160 GBP an hour to hire outright. Ride and Save bundles cut 20-30 percent off uplifts and 10-20 percent off pump-track sessions if you buy several up front.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round, with late riding until 20:30 on Thursday evenings from June to September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gloucester</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bristol</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://417bikepark.co.uk/">417 Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.mbr.co.uk/mountain-bike-routes/trail-centres/flyup-417-project-gloucester-353187">MBR on the 417 Project</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
