  <Placemark>
    <name>Twisted Oaks Bike Park (Ipswich, England) [11 GBP]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ipswich 10 m - Twisted Oaks Bike Park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Suffolk's newest and largest dedicated bike park, on 42 rolling acres inside Brightwell Country Park. Red and blue trails, jump lines, a dual slalom and skills and jump training areas, with a black trail, a cross-country route, a 4X track and a pump track all announced. A workshop and cafe on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No uplift.</b> Members ride Thursday to Monday; non-members on selected Saturdays and Sundays. Parking is free for members and day riders.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Wednesday to Friday 10:00-16:00, Saturday and Sunday 09:00-16:00. Closed Monday and Tuesday.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Ipswich</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>London</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://booking.page/en/company/page/twistedoaks">Twisted Oaks Bike Park booking</a> and <a href="https://infolink.suffolk.gov.uk/kb5/suffolk/infolink/service.page?id=NlKiw2TL_O8">Suffolk InfoLink</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
