  <Placemark>
    <name>Farmer Johns MTB Park (Stockport, England) [12 GBP]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Stockport 147 m - Farmer Johns MTB Park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A working farm turned bike park just outside Marple Bridge on the edge of the Peak District: several downhill runs graded red through black and severe black, plus a dirt-jump park. The Dirt Factory bike shop on site handles mechanicals, spares and hire, and the Big View Cafe runs weekends and school holidays.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No uplift</b> - push or shuttle yourself. Pay on the day 12 GBP a session for non-members; membership is 50 GBP plus 2 GBP a ride, which pays for itself in about five visits. A bunkhouse sleeps eight at 35 GBP a night and camping is 10 GBP a person.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Every day except Monday, from 09:30 until sunset.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Stockport</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Manchester</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://fjmtb.com/park-info/">Farmer Johns MTB Park</a> and <a href="https://www.facebook.com/FARMERJOHNSMTB/">Farmer Johns MTB Park updates</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
