  <Placemark>
    <name>Ciocco Bike Circle (Barga, Tuscany) [free access]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Il Ciocco 662 m - the bike circle above Barga</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A 600-hectare estate on the Tuscan-Emilian Apennines that hosted the MTB World Championships back in 1991 and has kept building since. The gravity line is a 4.5 km enduro descent from 1300 m down into the heart of the park; there is a 3.8 km XCO circuit with technical sections, around 70 km of signed routes for families and general riding, and a 200 m indoor modular pump track for when the weather turns.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A bike shuttle runs on the estate. <b>Access to the bike park is free</b> - the estate makes its money on accommodation, with chalets sleeping four to six from about 110-120 EUR a night. Workshop, bike wash, tool station, changing rooms and showers on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round; the indoor pump track covers the wet months.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Barga</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Lucca</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Pisa</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.cioccobike.it/en/">Ciocco Bike</a> and <a href="https://www.visittuscany.com/en/attractions/ciocco-bike-circle/">Visit Tuscany</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
