  <Placemark>
    <name>Omeo MTB Park (Victoria, Australia) [free, paid shuttles]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Omeo 623 m - the bike park at the edge of town</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the more remarkable things built in Australian mountain biking lately: 114 km of singletrack across Sam Hill and Mount Mesley, cut by the Common Ground crew, with vertical that stands comparison with Thredbo. Everything from green loops at the base to serious downhill. It is a true ride-in, ride-out town - the trailhead at Livingstone Park, with its pump track and skills park, is 240 m from the Golden Age Hotel and everything else is within 500 m.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> The trails are free. Two commercial operators run shuttles - Gravity Dirt Co and Blue Dirt - and a share of what they take goes back into trail maintenance. Self-shuttling works too, and the green loops at the base need no uplift at all.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Omeo</td><td>Bike</td><td>Direct</td></tr><tr><td>Melbourne</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://rideomeo.com.au/shuttle-service">Omeo MTB Park - shuttles</a>, <a href="https://rideomeo.com.au/faqs">Omeo MTB Park FAQs</a> and <a href="https://www.eastgippsland.vic.gov.au/media-releases/omeo-mtb-park-update-october-2025">East Gippsland Shire on the trail project</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
