  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park Janov (Presov, Slovakia) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Janov 317 m - the bike park below the village</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Four or five hand-built trails southwest of Presov, and the build quality is the point. Funtrail is the beginner line, but it is far from plain - family-friendly sections alongside wooden and clay features, drops, an 18 m wooden bridge and a 36 m wallride. A blue descent sits beside it. Driver 8 runs 1350 m for freeriders who like jumps, with berms, doubles and bridges; Rohatka is 1920 m of large jumps, steep turns, roots and gravel; and Kamenak, about 1480 m, is the hardest - steep, loose and technical. The first trail was cut in early 2016 and the park has grown since.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Free to ride; push or shuttle yourself.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The riding season, weather permitting.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Presov</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Kosice</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://slovenskycestovatel.sk/item/bike-park-janov">Slovensky cestovatel - Bike park Janov</a> and <a href="https://cavargy.sk/bikepark-janov-cavargy-cyklistika-presov/">Cavargy - Bikepark Janov</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
