  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park de Communay (Rhone, France) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Rhone 239 m - Bike Park de Communay</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Three graded pistes - green, blue and red - plus a pumptrack, built on a reclaimed slag heap (le crassier) south of Lyon. Compact and progression-focused rather than long, and the closest gravity riding to the city.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Push or pedal; the pumptrack needs neither.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly March to November. The commune does not publish fixed hours - it is an open public facility.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lyon</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Vienne</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.communay.fr/accueil/actualite/2060-le-crassier-se-metamorphose-place-aux-loisirs-a-deux-roues">Commune de Communay</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/13072500390">OSM node 13072500390</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
