  <Placemark>
    <name>Swiss Bike Park Oberried (Bern, Switzerland) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bern 690 m - Swiss Bike Park Oberried</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A national training facility above the Aare, and much bigger than most car-free parks: 16 distinct areas including four downhill lines (Rock Garden, Anliegerkurven, Serpentinen, Spitzkehren and Stufen), a jumpline, drops, trick jumps, a velodrome, two pump tracks, an uphill trail and a technique loop. Genuinely something for every level, and free.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. An uphill trail and uphill ramps handle the laps.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable spring to late autumn; open Monday to Saturday 09:00-18:00, with selected Sundays and holidays.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bern</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Thun</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Interlaken</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.swissbikepark.ch/">Swiss Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/932615965">OSM way 932615965</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
