  <Placemark>
    <name>La Poma Bike Park (Barcelona, Spain) [day pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Barcelona 67 m - La Poma Bike Park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The most famous pump-track and dirt-jump site in Spain, at Premia de Dalt north of Barcelona. Three pump tracks of different lengths covering every level, a parallel speed-and-style track, a dirt-jump area and a biketrial zone laid out by trials world champion Cesar Canas. Not a descent - a skills and airtime park, and one riders travel for.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Day, weekly, quarterly and annual passes are sold through the park's own shop.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Monday to Thursday 15:00-21:00, Friday to Sunday 09:00-21:00, weather permitting.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Barcelona</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Mataro</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://lapomashop.com/en">La Poma Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.turismemaresme.cat/en/what-to-do/activities/la-poma-bikepark">Maresme tourism</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
