  <Placemark>
    <name>Hatley Pointe Bike Park (North Carolina) [48 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mars Hill 1207 m - the Hatley Pointe base area</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Twelve trails, a mix of flow and technical, on the mountain that was Wolf Ridge Ski Resort until Hatley Pointe reopened it. Phase one is three primary downhill runs - green, blue and black - plus connectors, built by Elevated Trail Design with road gaps, rock spines, wooden drops and a cannon. Roughly 700 ft (215 m) of vertical.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Lift-served by the resort chairlift. Day ticket 48 USD adult, 38 USD child. Tickets must be reserved in advance - there are no walk-up sales.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The park opened for its first season on 1 August 2026, running Thursday to Sunday.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:00<br/><small>Opened 2026; the pin is the base area from OpenStreetMap, as the chairlift itself is not yet mapped.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Asheville</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Charlotte</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://hatleypointe.com/mountain-biking/">Hatley Pointe</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-82.508857,35.954739,1207</coordinates></Point>
