  <Placemark>
    <name>Sugarloaf Bike Park (Maine) [lift ticket, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sugarloaf 539 m - valley station of the Whiffletree SuperQuad</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>New England's newest lift-served bike park, opened in 2025 at Maine's largest ski resort and run by Boyne. The Whiffletree SuperQuad gives about 1,050 ft of vertical per lap - the OSM lift line measures 308 m, or 1,011 ft, which agrees. Machine-built gravity trails run 2.5 to 3 miles at a mellow grade, headlined by the three-mile intermediate flow trail Emerald and the green-circle Syncline; hand-built enduro and downhill lines including Jackpot, Widowmaker Extension, Rookie River, Rock Lobster and Crusher DH are shorter and considerably steeper. The wider Carrabassett Valley network around the resort adds a large amount of cross-country riding under separate management.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Whiffletree SuperQuad carries bikes. Sugarloaf sells single-day lift tickets through its own shop and does not publish a rate on the bike-park page, so we could not verify a 2026 price - check sugarloaf.com before you go. Season passes come with a complimentary Loon ticket, and Ikon passholders get up to two free bike-park tickets.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>2026 season opened 19 June. Weekends only to 30 June, then Thursday to Sunday from July. No closing date is published.<br/>Hours: Thu 14:00-18:00, Fri-Sat 10:00-18:00, Sun 10:00-16:00<br/><small>The operator publishes no season end date, so none is claimed here.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Portland ME</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <small>Only three trail lines are drawn here, and none of them are the park's machine-built runs: OpenStreetMap has not yet mapped Emerald, Syncline, Boulder Dash, Jackpot, Rookie River, Rock Lobster or Crusher DH. What is drawn is the mountain's older graded terrain.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.sugarloaf.com/bike-park">Sugarloaf Bike Park</a>. Pin placed on the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/137778670">Whiffletree SuperQuad</a> base station, verified at 539 m.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
