  <Placemark>
    <name>Parc de la Gorge de Coaticook (Quebec) [~15 CAD, unconfirmed]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Parc de la Gorge de Coaticook 232 m - park reception, east of the gorge</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 23 km of marked, IMBA-graded singletrack on the plateau east of the Coaticook gorge, run by the Societe de developpement de la Gorge de Coaticook, with a skills park and fatbike grooming in winter. This is a technical cross-country network first: the grades here describe roots, rock and tight singletrack rather than gradient, and the trail called Descente loses 2 m over 1.4 km. Total relief in the park is 132 m and the biggest sustained descent on a real trail is 67 m, so treat it as an XC and technical-trail destination with a few short gravity lines, not a downhill hill.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. You pedal, and the climbs are short. A day trail pass is sold at the park reception. <b>Price not confirmed with the operator - call ahead.</b> A regional tourism listing last updated in April 2024 gives 15 CAD adult (16+) and 8 CAD child (4-15); an older cycling write-up gives 10 CAD a day and 30 CAD for the season, and says access is free for campers and for Coaticook RCM residents with proof of address. The park's own rates page would not load for us, and the two secondary figures disagree, so treat 15 CAD as an indication only. Bike rental is available from Velotric in downtown Coaticook.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sherbrooke</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Montreal</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <small>Only three lines are drawn here out of 32 mapped trails. The rest fail the gravity filter this map applies everywhere: 49 of the park's chained traces sit under 4% average gradient. The full 23 km is worth riding - it is just mostly not downhill.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://gorgedecoaticook.qc.ca/en/summer-activities/mountain-bike/">Parc de la Gorge de Coaticook</a> for the network, <a href="https://www.cantonsdelest.com/velo/velo-de-montagne/4/parc-de-la-gorge-de-coaticook">Cantons-de-l'Est</a> for the 23 km total, and <a href="https://www.onyva.quebec/espace-decouverte/activites/fatbike-et-velo-de-montagne-au-parc-de-la-gorge-de-coaticook/">On y va</a> (updated April 2024) for the indicative rate. Pin placed on the OSM-mapped park <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/9118767825">Accueil</a> (reception, node 9118767825).
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-71.797452,45.145035,232</coordinates></Point>
