  <Placemark>
    <name>Gstaad (Bernese Oberland) [58 CHF / Magic Pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gstaad 1040 m - valley station of the Gstaad-Eggli gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A signed singletrail region rather than a built bike park: no jump lines, no dug berms, but around twenty numbered trails hung off the lifts across the Saanenland, plus some 300 km of marked routes. The hard end is six trails graded difficult - Schwylaub 3.9 km, Ruewlis 3.2 km, Rinderberg Ridge 2.6 km, Lerchweid 2.3 km, Ostgrat 2.2 km and Schafwald 1.3 km - and several of those are short, steep drops straight off a ridge station. In the middle sit Wispile-Bruechli at 6.4 km, Horny 3.5 km, Gspan and Rossfaelli, with a set of easy trails such as Louibach and Simmegrund for a first day. Come for natural alpine singletrack and lift-assisted enduro laps; if you want machine-built flow, this is the wrong valley.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A bike day pass is 58 CHF for adults and 29 CHF for children and half-fare holders, and it is on the Magic Pass. Bike carriage itself is free: Eggli and La Videmanette take the bike inside the cabin, Rinderberg hangs it on the outside, and Wispile and Horneggli use a separate transport lift, which can mean waits of up to 20 minutes. The Sanetsch lift is the exception at 9 CHF for the bike.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 18 October (2026 season, Horneggli and Rinderberg daily). Wasserngrat runs Thursday to Sunday only, 25 July to 6 September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Montreux</td><td>Train (GoldenPass)</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Bern</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <small>Only three lines are drawn here, and none of them are from the resort's numbered trail map - OpenStreetMap has not mapped Ruewlis, Ostgrat, Schwylaub, Rinderberg Ridge or the rest. What is drawn is the three separately named trails OSM does carry.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://bergbahnen-gstaad.ch/sommer/erlebnisse/aktivitaeten/bike">Bergbahnen Gstaad</a>. Pin placed on the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/86249803">Gstaad-Eggli gondola</a> valley station (way 86249803), verified at 1040 m. The Pra Ouliémo, Chalberhöni, DH Quoquaire, Dorfflüe Fir Flow, Mülisteine, Lerchweid and Eggli lines were drawn in gpx.studio and supplied for this map, simplified to ~8 m; Hornybar, Kuhstall and Wittere come from OpenStreetMap.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
