  <Placemark>
    <name>Cousimbert (Le Mouret, Fribourg) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Crau Rappo 1300 m - free parking at the top of the road, where you start</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Cousimbert is the wooded ridge between Le Mouret, Treyvaux and La Roche, and it carries a cluster of unsigned, locally-built descents rather than a bike park. Five of them are drawn here, east to west: <b>Sur Martou</b> (red, the longest, 2.7 km and 384 m from the ridge down to 904 m), <b>Le Mézer</b> (red, forking off beside it to follow the Ruisseau du Mézer), <b>Schwand Tsernet</b> (blue), <b>La Joux de Treyvaux</b> (black, 1.7 km off the ridge below the buvette) and <b>Belle Cierne</b> (red, dropping to 886 m on the Treyvaux side). Natural forest singletrack - roots, loam and steep pitches in the black, nothing built, no berms or jumps. La Joux de Treyvaux and Belle Cierne link end to end for a 3 km, 685 m run from the ridge to the valley.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and nothing to pay. One road, the Route du Cousimbert, climbs from Le Mouret and Treyvaux to this parking - twelve free gravel places at 1300 m, with more a few hundred metres either side - which is what makes it easy to session several trails in a day: drive or pedal up once, then re-climb the road between runs. Sur Martou and Schwand Tsernet start a short pedal away; the black La Joux de Treyvaux starts higher and further south, at the Buvette du Gros Cousimbert. That buvette and the huts at Wusta and Crau Rappo are on the ridge for food.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 15 November.<br/><small>Snow-dependent estimate for a 1600 m Prealpine ridge, not an operator date. The forest holds wet a long time after rain.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Fribourg</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bern</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Fribourg</td><td>Bus to La Roche FR, Serbache + climb</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <small>These trails are not signed and not in OpenStreetMap; the lines come from GPX recorded on the ground. Grades are the rider's, not an operator's.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Pin placed on the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1195260184">Crau Rappo parking</a> (way 1195260184), tagged twelve places, gravel, no fee. The secondary pin is the <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/127617218">Buvette du Gros Cousimbert</a> at 1572 m, the top of the longest descent.
    Access and conditions can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.205370,46.710415,1300</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">cousimbert</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert natural enduro dh no-lift</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="open_from">05-01</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="closed_from">11-15</mwm:value>
      </mwm:properties>
