      <mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Cousimbert: Buvette du Gros Cousimbert (1572 m)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Buvette du Gros Cousimbert 1572 m - top of the longest descent</b><br/><br/>
    The high point of the spot and where the black <b>La Joux de Treyvaux</b> starts, 1.7 km and 394 m down to the Treyvaux side; link it into Belle Cierne and you get 3 km and 685 m in one go. Mountain buvette, so food and drink at the top. It is about 2 km south-west of the Crau Rappo parking along the ridge, and roughly 270 m higher, so the black run costs a climb the other three do not. Verified at 1572 m on <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/127617218">OSM way 127617218</a>. See the main Cousimbert pin for trails and access.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.187242,46.697062,1572</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">cousimbert</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>None</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
