  <Placemark>
    <name>Mont Chauve / Mont de l'Ubac (Nice) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mont Chauve d'Aspremont 844 m - the summit, where the descents start</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The most engaged singletrack within reach of Nice, and pure enduro in character: the height is gained on tarmac and wide track, and the riding is all in the descent. Twenty-eight traces are drawn across the two hills. Off Mont Chauve d'Aspremont and its neighbour Mont Chauve de Tourrette, lines fall on every side - Banzai and Non Rumba are the two black ones, Ruche, Mercantour, Planeurs, Flying cinghiale, Cayenne and Zongo the reds, Sing Sing and the GR5 west flank the easier blues - over broken limestone, loose stone and rock steps. Three kilometres east, Mont de l'Ubac and Mont Macaron carry another five: Macaron and its Bordinas variant, Sentier Dede, Leche pas les freins and the long blue Bordinas that runs 2.4 km down to 113 m. Sixteen reds, nine blues, two blacks and one green link in all. Full suspension is the local advice, not a luxury. Rideable year round; best out of the midday heat, and the sunset view over the city is half the reason people ride it in the evening.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and nothing to pay. A road climbs almost to the summit, so you can drive up and session, or do it the usual way and pedal from the Aire Saint-Michel at 318 m - about 4 to 5 km and 350 m of climbing to the top. Bus F from Nice serves the Aire Saint-Michel.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Nice centre</td><td>Bus + pedal</td><td>~1h</td></tr><tr><td>Nice centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: trails drawn with <a href="https://gpx.studio">gpx.studio</a>; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the pin. Pin on the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1557416993">Mont Chauve d'Aspremont</a> summit node (1557416993), measured at 844 m - OSM tags the peak 854 m. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.254380,43.770650,844</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">mont-chauve</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="tags">expert natural enduro dh no-lift</mwm:value>
