    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sigale / Colle de Sigale (Esteron) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sigale 623 m - hilltop village on the Esteron, where the descents finish</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One long, serious drop off the north side of the Cheiron. From the Colle de Sigale at about 1350 m two black sections run in sequence - Col de la Sigale to Gerbiere, then Adrech de Gerbiere - for 5.4 km and 970 m of descent down to the Esteron river at 380 m, below the village. The red alternative, La Colle de Sigale to Le Pous, drops 510 m over 2.8 km on the eastern side of the same ridge. Tight and rocky throughout: switchbacks, rock steps and a few genuinely exposed passages. This is remote riding - no signs, no services on the hill, and the nearest town of any size is 30 km away.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and nothing to pay. The climb to the Colle de Sigale is on road and wide track, roughly 730 m of ascent from the village. Bus 672 links Nice and Sigale, but it is a handful of services a day, so this is effectively a car trip.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Nice</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Grasse</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: trails drawn with <a href="https://gpx.studio">gpx.studio</a>; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the pin. Pin on the OSM <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/4414839966">Sigale</a> village node (4414839966), measured at 623 m; the top of the descents is the <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/12466732778">Colle de Sigale</a> (node 12466732778). Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
