    <name>Val d'Allos - Le Seignus Bike Park (Haut-Verdon) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Le Seignus 1516 m - valley station of the Clos Bertrand chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eight marked runs over 15 km on a single 388 m lift lap, and a well-judged spread for a park this size: two green, one blue, three red and two black. <i>Pif &amp; Paf</i> is the green flow line, surfaced and rollable for a first ever descent, with <i>Green Spirit</i> the more natural of the two; <i>Blue Brother</i> is one long turn-heavy trail in three distinct sections. The reds carry the character - <i>Toboggan</i> is enduro in style, big natural movements on raw ground, while <i>Nine T</i> is the opposite, a built bike-park line of jumps and aerial modules; <i>Red Lines</i> sits between them. <i>Rock Line</i> and <i>Wood Run</i> are the two blacks, the names telling you which surface each one is about. There is also a boardercross with banked turns and berms, a play area for children and beginners, and an easy family descent on the Premin piste. South-facing Haut-Verdon terrain: dry, stony and fast in high summer.<br/><small>No trail lines are drawn here. OpenStreetMap maps this mountain thoroughly but only as a ski area - every graded piste in the bike park's footprint is a winter alpine run, and not one of the eight bike park trails is mapped. Follow the signs and the resort's trail map.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Clos Bertrand six-seat chairlift takes bikes from 1516 m to 1904 m, and is tagged for bicycles in OpenStreetMap. 2026 tariff: 20 EUR a day adult, 14 EUR child and senior; 16/12 EUR half day; 9/8 EUR a single ride; 32/28 EUR for two consecutive days, 85/70 EUR for five non-consecutive days, 170 EUR the season, family packs from 28 to 60 EUR. Under 5 ride free. Small repair parts are sold in the village sports shops, and there is bike parking and signed trail information at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Weekends from 13 June; daily 04 July to 30 August; weekends again 05 to 13 September (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><small>Subject to weather; the lift also carries walkers.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Beyond the park</b><br/>Sixteen marked VTT circuits cover the Haut-Verdon around Allos, three blue, ten red and three black, and the 175 km TransVerdon traverse passes through the valley.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Barcelonnette</td><td>Car (Col d'Allos)</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Digne-les-Bains</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Nice</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr><tr><td>Nice</td><td>Train des Pignes to Thorame-Haute + bus</td><td>~4h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.valdallos.com/bike-park-le-seignus.html">Val d'Allos tourist office</a> for trails, dates and tariff, and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the pin. Pin on the valley station of the OSM-mapped <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/123742603">Clos Bertrand</a> chairlift, measured at 1516 m. Verify ticket and trail status before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.615250,44.241330,1516</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">val-dallos-seignus</mwm:value><mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert bike-park dh enduro chairlift</mwm:value><mwm:value key="open_from">06-13</mwm:value><mwm:value key="closed_from">09-14</mwm:value></mwm:properties><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
