  <Placemark>
    <name>Parc Velo Sommet Saint-Sauveur (Quebec) [62 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Versant Avila 203 m - valley station of the Avila Express chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eleven downhill trails on the Avila side of Sommet Saint-Sauveur, 45 minutes from Montreal and the closest lift-served gravity riding to the city: 2 green, 4 blue, 3 black and 2 double black on 176 m of vertical. The operator splits them into "freeride" - machine-built, wide, smooth and fast - and "technique" - hand-built, narrower, winding, following the natural terrain. Green L'Erabliere and freeride Stolen Gold are the easy pair; Bark Wagon, Bacon Strip, La 50 and Flowy fill the blue grade; Machette, Simple Pleasures and Mario K. are the blacks; La Coupe and Chainsaw Massacre are the expert double blacks. A learning zone with modules sits by the base, alongside rental, a bike wash and the main lodge.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>One high-speed chairlift, the Avila Express, 203 m to 379 m. Online only, nothing sold on site: day ticket 61.99 CAD adult, 50.99 CAD for 13-17, 32.99 CAD for 12 and under; a 4-hour block is 39.99 / 24.99 / 19.99 CAD and a 3-visit pack 119.97 CAD adult. Bike rental 110 CAD adult (140 CAD high performance), 80 CAD junior; protective gear alone 20 CAD. Private lesson 178.20 CAD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer into autumn - an autumn season pass is sold separately. Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:00. Helmet and closed shoes are compulsory on every trail including the learning modules; full-face and body armour strongly recommended.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saint-Sauveur</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Montreal</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.sommets.com/fr/quoi-faire/velo-de-montagne/parc-velo-sommet-saint-sauveur/">Parc velo Sommet Saint-Sauveur</a>, the <a href="https://www.sommets.com/media/lt2jlett/sommet-avila-pistes-bike-park-carte.pdf">official trail map</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the lift and trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
