  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Fromme - North Shore (British Columbia) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>North Vancouver 190 m - Mountain Highway trailhead where the climb starts</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The hill where North Shore riding was invented, and still the reference for what the words mean: steep, rooty, loamy fall-line singletrack threaded with hand-built cedar ladder bridges and rock rolls. Riders climb the Mountain Highway fire road and drop back in on a numbered grid of descents. Expresso is the one most people name first - fast, root-covered, endlessly repeatable; Ladies Only, Grannies, Seventh Secret, Pipeline, Oil Can, Crippler, Bookwus and Digger cover the black and double-black end; Bobsled is the machine-built blue everybody warms up on and Roadside Attraction the gentlest way in. Maintained by the North Shore Mountain Bike Association.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. The Mountain Highway fire road is the climb, roughly 30-45 minutes to the upper trailheads; shuttling is not permitted. Free to ride - the NSMBA runs a Trail Adopter donation programme that funds the maintenance.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round but genuinely wet from October to April; the loam and the wooden features are slick in the rain, so the dry window is roughly June to September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>North Vancouver</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Vancouver downtown</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://nsmba.ca/">North Shore Mountain Bike Association</a>, <a href="https://www.vancouversnorthshore.com/activity/mountain-biking/">Vancouver's North Shore Tourism</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail names and geometry. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
