  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Seymour - North Shore (British Columbia) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>North Vancouver 125 m - Old Buck trailhead where the climb starts</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The friendliest of the three North Shore mountains, and the one that rewards a first visit: a well-graded climb trail and a long list of descents that run from playful blue to full North Shore steep-and-technical. Good Sir Martin is the climb everyone uses; Severed D and Asian Adonis are the steep, ladder-and-rock-roll classics; Neuralyzer is a long modern black; CBC, Corkscrew, Bottletop and Boogieman fill out the middle. Same loam, same cedar woodwork and same wet-season problem as Fromme, with a shade more flow.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Climb Good Sir Martin or the Old Buck trail from the lower car park, roughly 30-50 minutes depending on how high you go. Free; the North Shore Mountain Bike Association maintains the network on donations and volunteer days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable all year, best June to September. The trails hold water and the woodwork is genuinely slippery in the wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>North Vancouver</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Vancouver downtown</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://nsmba.ca/">North Shore Mountain Bike Association</a>, <a href="https://www.mountainbikingbc.ca/vancouver-coast-mountains/north-shore/">Mountain Biking BC</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail names and geometry. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
