  <Placemark>
    <name>Stromlo Forest Park (Canberra, Australia) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Stromlo Forest Park 600 m - event precinct and main trailhead</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Australia's flagship purpose-built mountain bike venue, on the burnt-out pine slopes of Mount Stromlo above Canberra: it hosted a World Cup in 2008 and the UCI World Championships in 2009, and the World Cup downhill track is still there to ride. Over 50 km of trail wraps the hill, from the beginner Deep Creek and Willo Link loops through the flowing Skyline and Luge to the granite slabs of Slick Rock and the long Double Dissolution. Add a four-cross track, a pump track, a criterium circuit and a skills area at the base. Dry, fast, decomposed-granite dirt that rides well almost year-round.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; pedal or shuttle the fire roads to the summit at 780 m for the downhill runs, about 180 m of vertical per lap. Entry and trail use are free - the park is run by the ACT Government.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round, daylight hours. Trails close during total fire bans and after heavy rain; check the park's trail status page.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Canberra city</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Sydney</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.stromloforestpark.act.gov.au/">Stromlo Forest Park</a>, <a href="https://corc.asn.au/trail-maps/">Canberra Off Road Cyclists</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail names and geometry. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
