  <Placemark>
    <name>Smithfield Mountain Bike Park (Cairns, Australia) [free, shuttle extra]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Smithfield 10 m - trailhead beside the Skyrail terminal, 15 km north of Cairns</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Australia's oldest mountain bike park and the highest-profile rainforest trail system anywhere: World Cups in 1994 and 2014, World Championships in 1996 and 2017, Crankworx since. More than 60 km of green, blue and black trail through vine-clad jungle, over creeks and along jagged granite ridges, with around 18 descents from green to double black and four shuttle roads feeding them. The World Champs downhill track, Jacobs Ladder and the A-Line jump lines are the marquee runs. Wet-tropics dirt: grippy, rooty and unforgiving of a mistake.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bike lift. Climb trails from the trailhead, or take a commercial shuttle up the downhill road - Cairns Mountain Bike Tours holds the access. Riding the park itself is free.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. The wet season runs roughly December to April and closes trails for days at a time; the dry season, May to October, is when the racing happens.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Cairns</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Cairns airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://tropicalnorthqueensland.org.au/things-to-do/active-escapes/mountain-biking-cycling/where-to-ride/smithfield-mountain-bike-park-trails/">Tropical North Queensland</a>, <a href="https://bq.org.au/where-to-rides/smithfield-mtb-park/">Bicycle Queensland</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>145.695100,-16.847700,11</coordinates></Point>
