  <Placemark>
    <name>Bootleg Canyon (Nevada, USA) [free, shuttle extra]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Boulder City 770 m - trailhead above town, at the mouth of the canyon</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Roughly 58 km of singletrack hand-cut out of volcanic desert rock above Boulder City, half an hour from Las Vegas, and one of the places that defined North American freeride: for two decades it was the Interbike demo venue and a stock film backdrop, and IMBA rates it an Epic. The lower Caldera, Boy Scout and Lake View loops are ridable cross-country; the upper trails - Armageddon, Reaper, Mother, Elevator Shaft, Kevorkian - are steep, loose, exposed and named accordingly, with grades touching 22%. Views over Lake Mead and the Las Vegas valley the whole way down.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal or take a commercial shuttle up the access road to the antenna towers for the downhill trails. Free to ride; the trails are on City of Boulder City land.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, and best October to April - summer daytime temperatures regularly pass 40 C and riding then is genuinely dangerous. Rock and hardpack, so rain is rarely the problem.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Boulder City</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Las Vegas</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bcnv.org/519/Bootleg-Canyon">City of Boulder City</a>, <a href="https://travelnevada.com/cycling-biking/bootleg-canyon-mountain-bike-park/">Travel Nevada</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail names and geometry. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
