  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Afan Forest Park (Wales) [free, parking charge]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Afan Argoed 165 m - Afan Forest Park visitor centre, above Port Talbot</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 130 km of trail across two valleys, and the home of W2 - one of a handful of IMBA Epics in Europe, a 44 km black route that links Y Wal and White's Level and is a genuine tick in British riding. The red grade is where most of the day goes: Penhydd, Y Wal, White's Level and Blade, all purpose-built singletrack, with the old Skyline route adding remote ridge riding at 600 m. Two centres serve it, Afan Argoed and Glyncorrwg, the latter with a bike-park and skills area alongside.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Every route is a pedal loop; commercial uplift runs occasionally for events only. Riding is free, parking is charged. Cafes, bike shop, hire, showers and camping on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, all-weather surfaced trails. Forestry operations close individual routes at times, so check before setting off.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Port Talbot</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiff</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://afanforestpark.com/mountain-biking/">Afan Forest Park</a>, <a href="https://naturalresources.wales/days-out/places-to-visit/south-west-wales/afan-forest-park-glyncorrwg-mountain-bike-centre/?lang=en">Natural Resources Wales</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
