  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Cwmcarn Forest (Wales) [uplift extra]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cwmcarn 120 m - forest drive visitor centre, north of Newport</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two wild, natural, contouring red cross-country routes above the Bristol Channel - the legendary Twrch Trail and the newer Cafall - plus the Cwmcarn downhill tracks, which have hosted national-level racing for two decades, and the black-graded Pedalhounds line. The site was gutted by larch disease felling and later forest fires and has been rebuilt in stages; the downhill track is open again, with a diversion still in place on the top of the Twrch descent.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The cross-country loops are pedalled from the car park. The downhill tracks are served by a bookable commercial uplift (Cwmdown); the Pedalhounds trail can also be reached by climbing the Cafall trail. Parking is charged.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. Check the forest's own trail-status page before travelling - sections have been closed repeatedly for felling and fire damage.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Newport</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiff</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.cwmcarnforest.co.uk/en/activities/mountain-biking-at-cwmcarn/">Cwmcarn Forest</a>, <a href="https://www.mbwales.com/agents/cwmcarn/">MB Wales</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
