  <Placemark>
    <name>Coed Llandegla (Wales) [free, parking charge]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Coed Llandegla 275 m - Oneplanet Adventure centre, west of Wrexham</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact, well-run trail centre in a conifer plantation on the Denbighshire moors, and the default after-work ride for the north-west of England as much as for Wales. Four waymarked loops stack on each other: green at about 5 km, blue at 12 km, red at 18 km and black at 21 km, plus off-piste Natural Selection lines, a dual slalom track, a skills area and a jump line. The riding is fast, bermed and forgiving rather than technical - a good first trail centre and a good place to ride hard when it is wet everywhere else.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; all loops are pedalled from the centre. Riding is free, parking is charged. Cafe, bike shop, hire (hardtail to full-suspension e-bike) and showers on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, all-weather surfaced trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Wrexham</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Manchester</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mbwales.com/agents/coed-llandegla/">MB Wales</a>, <a href="https://www.redbull.com/gb-en/coed-llandegla-mtb-guide">Red Bull trail guide</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
