  <Placemark>
    <name>Forest of Dean - Cannop (England) [free, uplift extra]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cannop 125 m - Forest of Dean Cycle Centre, near Coleford</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the busiest riding sites in England, and two things at once. The waymarked side has the Verderers blue - an 11 km all-weather flow loop voted the best blue trail in England - and the red Freeminers cross-country route. The gravity side has around fourteen short downhill tracks packed onto one hillside, blue through double black, full of drops, tables, berms, loam and roots, served by a bookable uplift. Sandstone and coal-measure dirt in old industrial woodland.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Push up, or book the Fly Up Downhill uplift for the gravity tracks. Riding is free, parking is charged. Cafe, bike shop, hire, showers, bike wash and coaching on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. The downhill tracks are natural surface and get properly greasy in winter; the Verderers loop is all-weather.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Coleford</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bristol</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.fodmtb.com/trails">FoD MTB</a>, <a href="https://www.mbuk.com/articles/what-makes-the-forest-of-dean-one-of-the-uks-most-popular-trail-centres">Mountain Biking UK</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
