  <Placemark>
    <name>Hamsterley Forest (England) [free, bike park extra]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Hamsterley 175 m - forest visitor centre, County Durham</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>2,000 hectares of County Durham forest with about 65 km of waymarked cross-country trail plus a separate gravity site. The red Edge Trail is the headline cross-country ride at 21 km, with steep climbs, water crossings and long stretches of flowing, occasionally technical singletrack; there is a skills loop and easier family routes from the visitor centre. Two miles away, Descend Bike Park - the hill Danny Hart grew up on - runs downhill and four-cross tracks on its own uplift.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The forest trails are pedal loops; forest parking is charged. The downhill tracks at Descend Bike Park are a separate paid site with its own uplift and opening days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Forest trails year-round. The bike park runs to its own published calendar, mostly weekends.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bishop Auckland</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Newcastle</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.forestryengland.uk/hamsterley-forest/cycling-and-mountain-biking-trails-hamsterley-forest">Forestry England</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
