  <Placemark>
    <name>Rostrevor - Kilbroney (Northern Ireland) [free, uplift extra]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kilbroney Park 40 m - trailhead hub above Carlingford Lough</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The best-known trail centre in Ireland, climbing from Kilbroney Park into the Mourne Mountains towards Slieve Martin. A 27 km red loop and a 19 km black loop do the cross-country work, over slabby granite with long views down Carlingford Lough; alongside them are Ireland's first two official downhill trails and a set of harder black and extreme lines. Rocky, exposed and weather-beaten - closer in feel to Scottish riding than to a plantation trail centre.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The loops are pedalled from the trailhead. Bike Mourne runs a bookable uplift from the Kilbroney Park car park to the higher trailheads, plus bike hire and a cafe. Riding and parking are free.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. Exposed high sections get genuinely wild in winter weather.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Newry</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Belfast</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr><tr><td>Dublin</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://mountainbikeni.com/trail-centres/rostrevor/">Mountain Bike NI</a>, <a href="https://www.bikemourne.com/rostrevor-mountain-bike-trails/">Bike Mourne</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
