  <Placemark>
    <name>Punta Ala Trail Center (Tuscany, Italy) [shuttle extra]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Punta Ala 10 m - trail centre base on the Maremma coast</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The reference enduro destination on the Tuscan coast: dozens of trails and marked itineraries spread over three connected areas - Bandite di Scarlino, Massa Marittima and the Sentieri Castiglionesi around Tirli - running from family tours to expert-only descents. Dry, rocky, Mediterranean singletrack through cork oak and macchia, most of it finishing within sight of the sea. Shuttle service, guiding, rental and a pump track at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. A shuttle service runs through the season for the longer descents; otherwise the climbs are short. Trail access is free, shuttles and guiding are paid.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly March to November, with the season opening around Easter. This is a winter and shoulder-season destination - high summer on the coast is hot.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Follonica</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Pisa airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Florence</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://visitpuntaala.bike/en/our-trails/">Punta Ala Trail Center</a>, <a href="https://www.visittuscany.com/en/attractions/punta-ala-trail-center/">Visit Tuscany</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
