  <Placemark>
    <name>Kaiteriteri Mountain Bike Park (Nelson, New Zealand) [free, donation]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kaiteriteri 65 m - park entrance off Martin Farm Road</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>250 hectares of regenerating native forest at the door of Abel Tasman National Park, and the best-known ride in the Nelson region: about 40 trails and over 70 km, graded 2 to 5. Easy Rider and Glade Runner are the smooth, wide way in; Karmakaze adds technical sections, Velocity is the steep fast one, The Rockface has the ruts and slabs and Bad Jelly is the hand-built enduro line with the rock drops. Several trails finish within sight of the beach.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Climb trails from the entrance, with commercial shuttles and guided tours available. Free to ride; donations fund the trust that maintains the park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. Best over the southern summer, December to April; the clay holds water after heavy rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Motueka</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Nelson</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://bikekaiteriteri.co.nz/">Kaiteriteri Mountain Bike Park</a>, <a href="https://nelsonmtb.club/kaiteriteri-trails/">Nelson MTB Club</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
