  <Placemark>
    <name>Vallee Bras-du-Nord (Quebec) [trail pass, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Saint-Raymond 165 m - Vallee Bras-du-Nord main welcome centre</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The largest singletrack network in the Quebec City region: about 100 km of hand-built trail across several sectors of the Bras-du-Nord valley, run by a non-profit co-operative that also does social reintegration work through trail building. The Saint-Raymond sector holds roughly 30 km of narrow, technical riding over three small hills right by the town; the Shannahan sector further up the valley has the longer, wilder lines. Laurentian granite, roots and rock slabs, with river gorges and waterfalls along the way.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no shuttle - everything is pedalled. A day trail pass or an annual membership is required; the membership runs 1 May to 30 April. Rental, huts, camping and a shuttle for the hiking trails are available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly May to October for mountain biking, then fat bike through the winter.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saint-Raymond</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Quebec City</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://valleebrasdunord.com/en/outdoor-activities/mountain-bike/">Vallee Bras-du-Nord</a>, <a href="https://valleebrasdunord.com/en/pricing/">its pricing page</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
