  <Placemark>
    <name>Empire 47 (Lac-Delage, Quebec) [24.60 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Empire 47 170 m - reception and trailhead at the foot of the slopes</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A non-profit trail centre twenty minutes north of Quebec City, on the hillside above Lac Delage: 44 signed trails over about 80 km, graded on the operator's own six-step scale - 2 debutant, 6 facile, 16 intermediaire, 5 avance, 8 expert and 4 extreme on the 2024 summer map. Riding is cross-country and enduro rather than downhill: the family sector at the base barely climbs, the first summit is 150 m of gain and opens the enduro lines, and the top of the hill - Mont de la Cote du Cure, 428 m - is about 270 m above the reception. The steep end is genuinely steep: Nosferatu, Descente du Coude and Haute Valkyrie all hold 15-19% over their full length. There are also two jump lines, an airbag, a drop zone and a large paved, floodlit pumptrack by the welcome building.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no shuttle - every descent is earned, and the network is built with dedicated climbing trails (Montee de la Soif, Montee de Lait, Montee de l'Estra) rather than fire roads. Day access 24.60 CAD for 16 and over, 12 CAD ages 7-15, 61.20 CAD family; season pass 280 CAD adult, 105 CAD junior, 665 CAD family. Taxes are extra and a day ticket bought online must be used the same day. Helmets are compulsory. Rental, coaching, a workshop, a bike wash and patrol are on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-May to the end of October for mountain biking, 08:00-21:00 on weekdays and 08:00-19:00 at weekends. The site then runs about 50 km of groomed fatbike trail through the winter.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lac-Delage</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Quebec City</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.empire47.com/en/">Empire 47</a>, its <a href="https://www.empire47.com/en/fees-and-rental/">fees page</a> and <a href="https://www.empire47.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Empire-47-Summer-Map-2024-Velo-min.pdf">2024 summer bike map</a>, <a href="https://www.quebecvelodemontagne.com/en/destinations/empire-47">Quebec velo de montagne</a>, <a href="https://www.quebec-cite.com/en/what-to-do-quebec-city/best-mountain-biking">Quebec City tourism</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
