  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Blue Mountain Bike Park (Ontario) [59 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Blue Mountain 250 m - valley station of the Comet chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The main lift-served gravity riding in Ontario, on the Niagara Escarpment above Georgian Bay two hours from Toronto. Only about 150 m of vertical off the Comet chairlift, but the trails are properly built and graded green through black, from wide beginner flow to steep, rocky expert descents on the escarpment face. Twenty-three further cross-country and downcountry trails run from the village, and the resort village itself has everything a weekend needs.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Comet quad chairlift carries bikes; a day ticket covers the lift and all downhill trails. Adult 59 CAD online, 62 CAD at the window; youth 15 and under 48 CAD online, 51 CAD at the window.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>June to October. Thursday and Friday 12:00-18:00 and weekends 10:00-18:00 through the summer; Fridays 12:00-17:00 and weekends 10:00-17:00 from September, plus selected Mondays.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Collingwood</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Toronto</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.skibluemt.com/mountain-biking/tickets-and-rentals/">Blue Mountain mountain biking tickets</a>, <a href="https://www.bluemountain.ca/things-to-do/biking">Blue Mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the lift geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
