  <Placemark>
    <name>Coldwater Mountain (Alabama, USA) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Anniston 270 m - Coldwater Mountain trailhead</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Roughly 90 km of singletrack on 1,600 hectares of Forever Wild land halfway between Birmingham and Atlanta, laid out by IMBA Trail Solutions from 2012 and still growing - the reason Anniston is on the map for southeastern riding at all. Bomb Dog is the trail people name first, a long machine-built descent of switchberms; there are green stacked loops at the bottom, technical rocky climbing above, and a jump line. Dries fast on Appalachian sandstone.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no shuttle; the loops climb and descend from the trailheads. Free.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, and at its best October to April - Alabama summers are hot and humid.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Anniston</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Birmingham</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Atlanta</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.alabamaforeverwild.com/">Alabama Forever Wild</a>, <a href="https://www.singletracks.com/mtb-trails/new-trail-opening-brings-coldwater-mountain-in-anniston-alabama-to-about-50-miles-of-singletrack/">Singletracks</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
