  <Placemark>
    <name>Val d'Isere Bike Park (Savoie, France) [15 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Val d'Isere 1830 m - valley station of the Olympique gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>High-altitude gravity riding on the Bellevarde and Solaise faces, linked to Tignes across the Borsat chairlift, with more than 220 km of marked routes between the two. The graded park runs from the long blue flow of Popeye and Flowy Jumper through Fee Magique and Blue Lagoon, up to the technical Into the Wild and Fast Wood and the black Rock'n Ride, Bellev'hard and Very Bike Trip. Alpine terrain above 2,000 m for the top halves, then long descents through pasture and forest into the village.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Olympique gondola and Solaise gondola carry bikes from the village, with the Borsat chairlift making the link to Tignes and a free shuttle in the valley. A bike-park day pass is around 15 EUR; passes are sold at the tourist office, the sports centres and the Olympique departure.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer only, roughly early July to end of August - the 2026 season ran 4 July to 30 August. The Olympique runs 09:45-16:40, the Borsat 10:15-16:25.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bourg-Saint-Maurice</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Geneva airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere-in-summer/mountain-bike-and-atv/bike-park/">Val d'Isere bike park</a>, <a href="https://www.valdisere.ski/en/bikepark">Val d'Isere lifts</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the lift and trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
