  <Placemark>
    <name>Bad Kleinkirchheim (Carinthia, Austria) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bad Kleinkirchheim 1065 m - valley station of the Kaiserburgbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Home of the Flow Country Trail, the longest flow trail of its kind in Europe: 15 km of gravel-surfaced berms and rollers dropping about 910 m from the Kaiserburg station at 2,100 m to the valley, at an average 8% and with easier bypasses around every harder section - a trail deliberately built so that beginners can ride the whole thing. Around it the Nockberge network adds seven signed singletrails and fifteen tours, including the Maibrunntrail and the Rossalmhuttentrail, plus long backcountry loops like the Priedrof round and the FIS Franz Klammer tour.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Two summer lifts carry bikes: the Kaiserburgbahn out of Bad Kleinkirchheim and the Brunnachbahn from St. Oswald. Ticket prices are published each season by the Bergbahnen - check before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer into autumn, following the summer lift calendar - broadly June to October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Villach</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Klagenfurt</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Salzburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.badkleinkirchheim.com/en/bike/flow-country-trail/">Bad Kleinkirchheimer Bergbahnen</a>, <a href="https://www.badkleinkirchheim.com/en/bike/biking-trails-tours/">its trails and tours page</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the lift and trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
