  <Placemark>
    <name>Kamloops Bike Ranch (British Columbia) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kamloops 455 m - the Bike Ranch, between Valleyview and Juniper Ridge</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Canada's largest municipal bike park, 26 hectares inside the city, and the ground where a large slice of freeride history was filmed - Kranked and the Froriders came off these dry, dusty hoodoo slopes. It grew from a few illegal steep lines behind the arena into twelve downhill trails from beginner to pro, packed with berms, jumps and drops, a floodlit jump corral where world-class riders turn up unannounced, a skills area at the top and a paved pump track complex added in 2024. Kamloops silt: fast, loose over hard, and utterly unlike the coast.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - a short access climb from the car park serves the whole hill. Free, run by the City of Kamloops with the Kamloops Mountain Bike Trail Association.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly April to October, and the driest riding in British Columbia. The jump lines close when wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kamloops centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Vancouver</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.kamloops.ca/recreation-culture/parks-sports-fields/kamloops-bike-ranch-all-wheels-pump-track-facility">City of Kamloops</a>, <a href="https://www.kmbta.com/bikeranch">KMBTA</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
