  <Placemark>
    <name>Gooseberry Mesa (Utah, USA) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gooseberry Mesa 1550 m - Windmill trailhead, above Hurricane</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The technical slickrock benchmark of southern Utah, and the ride people put beside Moab rather than below it. About 30 km of interconnecting loops on top of a mesa, linking painted slickrock domes with sandy singletrack: the North Rim, South Rim, Practice Loop, Hidden Canyon and the White, Yellow and Bowls and Ledges routes, all waymarked with paint dots on the rock. Constant technical problem-solving rather than speed, with Zion on the skyline the whole time.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift, no shuttle, barely any climbing - the trails wander the mesa top. Free, on BLM land. The access road is rough dirt and impassable when wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Autumn to spring, roughly September to May. High summer is dangerously hot; the slickrock itself is unaffected by rain but the access road is not.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Hurricane</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>St George</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Las Vegas</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.visitutah.com/things-to-do/mountain-biking/mountain-biking-trails/gooseberry-mesa">Visit Utah</a>, <a href="https://www.utahmountainbiking.com/trails/goose.htm">Utah Mountain Biking</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
