  <Placemark>
    <name>Phil's Trail Complex - Bend (Oregon, USA) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bend 1185 m - Phil's Trailhead, four miles west of town</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The network that made Bend a mountain bike town: roughly 65 km of interlinked singletrack in the ponderosa forest immediately west of the city, named after Phil Meglasson, who cut the first lines here in the 1980s. Phil's itself is the fast, smooth, endlessly flowing classic; Ben's, Kent's, Marvin's Gardens, Voodoo, Grand Slam and Whoops - the town's jump trail - branch off it, and the complex connects onward to Wanoga and the Cascade Lakes trails. Dry volcanic pumice soil that drains almost instantly.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; gentle climbing on a network designed to be pedalled in loops. Free, on Deschutes National Forest land - a Northwest Forest Pass is needed for the car park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly April to November; snow closes the higher trails in winter, though the lowest loops often ride year-round. Rare mud.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bend</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Portland</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/r06/deschutes/recreation/phils-trailhead">Deschutes National Forest</a>, <a href="https://visitcentraloregon.com/things-to-do/attractions/phils-trail-complex/">Visit Central Oregon</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-121.385540,44.043410,1183</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">phils-trail-bend</mwm:value>
