  <Placemark>
    <name>Tokai - Table Mountain (Cape Town, South Africa) [activity permit]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Tokai 55 m - The Range car park, on the Constantia side</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Cape Town's home trails, on the eastern slopes of the Table Mountain chain inside the national park. A long fire-road climb through pine plantation and restored fynbos reaches the contour paths, and the descents come back down through the trees with the False Bay coastline below - Vasbyt, Barrydale, Blackadder and the rest, ranging from flowing to genuinely rocky. Silvermine over the ridge and the Constantia greenbelts below extend the day. The plantations are being progressively felled and rehabilitated, so individual lines move.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; everything is climbed. SANParks requires a Level 3 My Activity Permit to cycle in Table Mountain National Park - annual, or day permits sold at the Tokai braai-area kiosk for a few tens of rand.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. Winter, roughly June to August, is the Cape's wet season; summer is dry, windy and hot.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Cape Town centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Cape Town airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.sanparks.org/parks/table-mountain/what-to-do/activities/mountain-biking">SANParks Table Mountain</a>, <a href="https://www.sanparks.org/parks/table-mountain/cards-permits">permits</a>, <a href="https://tokaimtb.com/">TokaiMTB</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Permits, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
