  <Placemark>
    <name>Atherton Forest Mountain Bike Park (Queensland, Australia) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Atherton 770 m - Baldy Yabi trailhead, Herberton Range State Forest</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Atherton Tablelands network, an hour inland and 700 m above Cairns, and the cool-climate counterweight to Smithfield: seventeen purpose-built singletrack trails through open forest of gums, bloodwoods, she-oaks, grasstrees and cycads, plus old forestry plots of teak and tallowwood. Trail 12, Stairway to Heaven, is a 10.5 km switchback climb to the high point; the descents off it include Ricochet, the biggest at 252 m of drop. Mostly green and blue with black alternative lines, and a skills park at the Atherton trailhead in town.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no commercial shuttle - the network is built to be climbed. Free, on Queensland state forest land, with entries at Vernon Street in Atherton and at Rifle Range Road.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, and much drier and cooler than the coast. The wet season, roughly December to April, still closes trails after heavy rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Atherton</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Cairns</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://parks.qld.gov.au/parks/herberton-range/about/mountain-bike">Queensland Parks</a>, <a href="https://tropicalnorthqueensland.org.au/listing/product/atherton-forest-mountain-bike-park/">Tropical North Queensland</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
