  <Placemark>
    <name>Kirroughtree - 7stanes (Scotland) [free, parking charge]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kirroughtree 25 m - visitor centre in Galloway Forest Park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The most technically interesting of the 7stanes centres, in the ancient forest of Galloway: granite slabs, natural rock gardens and tight singletrack rather than manicured berms. The red Twister loop is the one most people ride; the black Black Craigs adds the Bargaly Wood section, a long stretch of absorbing rock work that is closer to natural trail than trail-centre fare. Green and blue loops and a skills area cover the easier end.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; all loops are pedalled from the visitor centre. Riding is free, parking is charged. Cafe, bike hire and washdown on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, all-weather surfaced trails - the granite sections stay rideable when the forest floor does not.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Newton Stewart</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Glasgow</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://forestryandland.gov.scot/visit/kirroughtree">Forestry and Land Scotland</a>, <a href="https://scotlandstartshere.com/point-of-interest/7stanes-kirroughtree/">Scotland Starts Here</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
