  <Placemark>
    <name>Laggan Wolftrax (Scotland) [free, parking charge]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Laggan 330 m - Wolftrax trailhead in Strathmashie Forest</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 30 km of purpose-built trail in Caledonian pine forest above the River Spey, in the Cairngorms National Park. The green and blue loops are gentle and family-friendly; the red is a proper trail-centre red; the black is one of the most technical purpose-built singletracks in Scotland, a granite-slab and boulder line that is closer to a rock climb on wheels than to a flow trail. A skills area and a large jump line sit by the car park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; all loops climb from the trailhead. Riding is free, parking is charged by Forestry and Land Scotland. Cafe and bike hire on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, though this is the Highlands - winter brings snow and short days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Newtonmore</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Inverness</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://forestryandland.gov.scot/visit/laggan-wolftrax">Forestry and Land Scotland</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
