  <Placemark>
    <name>Highland Wildcat - Golspie (Scotland) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Golspie 25 m - Rhives car park at the foot of Ben Bhraggie</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Home of the longest singletrack descent in the UK: from the Duke of Sutherland monument on the summit of Ben Bhraggie, more than 7 km of continuous trail runs all the way down to sea level at Golspie, ending metres from the beach. The upper section is open, rocky and exposed above the treeline; the lower half threads fast through birch and pine. Black and red graded lines dominate, with gentler blue and green loops lower down, and the North Sea in view for most of the descent.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Climb the waymarked ascent or arrange a private shuttle up the hill road; the community trust that built and maintains the trails asks for donations. Free.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. Exposed and wind-blasted up top; best from spring to autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Golspie</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Inverness</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h05</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.highlandwildcat.com/">Highland Wildcat</a>, <a href="https://www.visitscotland.com/info/see-do/highland-wildcat-trails-golspie-p317471">VisitScotland</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
