  <Placemark>
    <name>Gisburn Forest (England) [free, parking charge]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gisburn Forest 155 m - forest hub trailhead, Forest of Bowland</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The main trail centre of northern Lancashire, in the Forest of Bowland above Stocks Reservoir. A red loop with black sections - the Eight, with the Hully Gully and Whelpstone Crag descents - does the heavy lifting; a blue loop and a progressive skills area cover the rest, and a set of separate downhill lines including the orange-graded Hope Line drop off the steeper flank. Gritstone and peat, so wetter underfoot than a Welsh trail centre, but the built sections hold up.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; loops are pedalled from the hub. Riding is free, parking is charged by Forestry England. Cafe and bike wash on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Clitheroe</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Manchester</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.forestryengland.uk/gisburn-forest-and-stocks/cycling-and-mountain-biking-trails-gisburn">Forestry England</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
