  <Placemark>
    <name>Swinley Forest (Berkshire, England) [free, parking charge]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Swinley Forest 140 m - Crowthorne and Bracknell woods, near The Look Out</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The default ride for west London and the Thames Valley: 24 km of waymarked, purpose-built, all-weather singletrack on free-draining Bagshot sand, plus a large network of forest tracks. A blue and a red loop do the signed riding, both fast, rolling and tightly wooded rather than steep - there is barely 60 m of relief in the whole forest - and a skills area and jump lines sit alongside. Its value is that it drains in hours, so it rides in January much as it does in July.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; flat-to-rolling loops from the car parks. Riding is free, parking is charged. Swinley Bike Hub at The Look Out has hire, coffee and a workshop.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, and genuinely all-weather - this is the wet-season answer for southern England.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bracknell</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>London</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://swinleybikehub.com/mountain-bike-trails/">Swinley Bike Hub</a>, <a href="https://www.forestryengland.uk/swinley-forest">Forestry England</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
