  <Placemark>
    <name>Grizedale Forest (Lake District, England) [free, parking charge]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Grizedale 210 m - Moor Top car park, between Coniston and Hawkshead</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Lake District's best-known waymarked riding, between Coniston Water and Windermere. The red-graded North Face Trail is the headline: 16 km of singletrack, boardwalk and forest road with hard climbs paid back by long descents and views over the lakes, and it takes most riders over two hours. Easier family routes and the Parkamoor loop extend the network, and the forest is dotted with the sculpture trail it is equally known for.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; the loops climb. Riding is free, parking is charged by Forestry England. Visitor centre, cafe and hire nearby.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. This is the wettest corner of England and the natural sections show it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Hawkshead</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Kendal</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.forestryengland.uk/grizedale">Forestry England</a>, <a href="https://www.visitlakedistrict.com/things-to-do/grizedale-mountain-biking-trails-p1218441">Visit Lake District</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
