  <Placemark>
    <name>Whinlatter Forest (Lake District, England) [free, parking charge]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Whinlatter 320 m - forest visitor centre above Braithwaite</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>England's only true mountain forest, on the pass above Keswick, and home to the Altura Trail - the longest purpose-built mountain bike trail in the Lake District at 19 km, split into a north and south loop and graded red throughout. Sustained climbs, long flowing descents through spruce, and views out over Bassenthwaite Lake and Skiddaw. A blue Quercus loop covers the easier end.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; both loops climb from the visitor centre. Riding is free, parking is charged by Forestry England. Cafe, hire and bike wash on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, though the pass is high enough to hold snow in winter.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Keswick</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Penrith</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.forestryengland.uk/whinlatter">Forestry England</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
