  <Placemark>
    <name>Narvikfjellet (Norway) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Narvik 245 m - valley station of the Narvikfjellet gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Lift-served riding inside the Arctic Circle, straight above the town and the Ofotfjord. The gondola serves two bike trails from the upper station at 620 m, and the wider Narvik area holds far more: the Ankenesfjellet downhill run drops 5.3 km of roots, bridges and jumps close to town, and the Reinesfjellet trail in Skjomen is a 21.6 km line over bare granite slabs, bowls and drops with the Frostisen glacier opposite. Midnight-sun riding through June and July.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Narvikfjellet gondola carries bikes; the mountain road can also be pedalled. Ticket prices are published each summer by the operator.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Short Arctic summer, roughly late June to early September, following the gondola calendar.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Narvik centre</td><td>Walk</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Evenes airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.narvikfjellet.no/en/mountain_bike">Narvikfjellet</a>, <a href="https://www.visitnarvik.com/mountain-biking">Visit Narvik</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the lift geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
