  <Placemark>
    <name>Gerlitzen Alpe (Carinthia, Austria) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Annenheim 520 m - valley station of the Kanzelbahn, on the Ossiacher See</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the five Flow Trails Karnten mountains, rising straight off the Ossiacher See. The Kanzelbahn lifts bikes from the lakeshore to 1,440 m; from there the PROlitzen trail runs 3.8 km of black-graded singletrail down the flank, and the lake.bike kids park at the top station stacks five short Bino trails - one green, two blue and two red - built specifically for children from about three years old, which makes this an unusually good family mountain. Long alpine pasture tours continue over the summit at 1,900 m.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Kanzelbahn gondola carries bikes from Annenheim; the Gipfelbahn continues to the summit, and a toll road from Treffen reaches the top station by car. Ticket prices are published each summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer into autumn, following the summer lift calendar - broadly June to October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Villach</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Klagenfurt</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.kaernten.at/flowtrails/">Flow Trails Karnten</a>, <a href="https://www.visitvillach.at/de/leader-projekt-mountainbike-trail-gerlitzen-alpe.html">Visit Villach</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the lift geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
