  <Placemark>
    <name>Nassfeld (Carinthia, Austria) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Troepolach 615 m - valley station of the Millennium-Express</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Trail World Nassfeld sits on the Austrian-Italian border ridge above the Gailtal, and the trails cross it: eleven singletrails plus a flow trail run in both countries. The Mex-Line-I is the easy headline, 4 km of flowing forest and meadow from Gmanberg at 1,044 m down to Troepolach at 614 m; the Lift and Bike Giro takes the Millennium-Express up to the Madritsche and comes back down 11.7 km. One of the five Flow Trails Karnten mountains.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The three-section Millennium-Express carries bikes from Troepolach to 1,900 m, with further gondolas and chairlifts across the plateau. Ticket prices are published each summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer, following the lift calendar - the 2026 bike season ran 13 June to 27 September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Hermagor</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Villach</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Udine</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.nassfeld.at/en/Summer-World/Bike-World/Trails">Nassfeld trails</a>, <a href="https://www.kaernten.at/flowtrails/">Flow Trails Karnten</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> for the lift geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
