  <Placemark>
    <name>TrailGround Brilon (Sauerland, Germany) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Brilon 455 m - TrailGround trailhead at Am Haengeberg</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A lift-free trail centre on the edge of Brilon in the Sauerland: three signed singletrail loops of 7 to 17 km - Haengeberg, Bilstein and Plattenberg - totalling about 28 km, of which roughly 60% is singletrack. The character is deliberately moderate: gentle climbs, smooth descents, berms, banking and small kickers, built so that ordinary riders get a full day of flow rather than a handful of hard descents. Views out over the Briloner Hochflaeche.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no shuttle - the loops climb and descend from the edge of town. Free.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, weather permitting; the Sauerland gets snow in winter.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Brilon</td><td>Bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Dortmund</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.trailgroundbrilon.de/">TrailGround Brilon</a>, <a href="https://www.wintersport-arena.de/sommer/biken/trailground-brilon">Wintersport-Arena Sauerland</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
