  <Placemark>
    <name>Canmore Nordic Centre (Alberta, Canada) [park pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Canmore Nordic Centre 1425 m - day lodge and trailhead above Canmore</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Built for the cross-country skiing of the 1988 Winter Olympics and now one of the best trail networks in the Canadian Rockies: over 100 km ranging from wide gravel to committed singletrack, wrapped around the Bow Valley with Ha Ling Peak and the Three Sisters overhead. There is a dirt-jump area and a technical trail zone with bridges, drops, skinnies and a wall ride, and the network connects out to the Highline and the Canmore valley trails. Mostly intermediate to advanced.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; everything is pedalled. An Alberta Parks pass or day parking fee applies. Trail Sports at the day lodge has rental, repair, lessons and guiding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly May to October, snow permitting - the centre goes back to skiing in winter.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Canmore</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Calgary</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Banff</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.albertaparks.ca/parks/kananaskis/canmore-nordic-centre-pp/activities/summer-activities/">Alberta Parks</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-115.386180,51.090200,1425</coordinates></Point>
