  <Placemark>
    <name>Sentiers du Moulin (Quebec) [17 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lac-Beauport 347 m - trailhead and chalet at 99 chemin du Moulin</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A non-profit outdoor centre 25 minutes from Quebec City with 47 km of singletrack: 12 easy, 10 intermediate and 25 difficult trails, which tells you where the weight sits. The character is enduro - relatively easy climbs paying into long technical descents through Laurentian hardwood, with mountain views from the upper trails. Cross-country skiing, snowshoeing and fat biking share the network in winter.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; all climbing is pedalled. Day access 16.53 CAD adult, 11.31 CAD for 13-17, free under 12, sold online only.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly May to October for mountain biking, then fat bike over the winter.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lac-Beauport</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Quebec City</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.sentiersdumoulin.com/en/home/">Sentiers du Moulin</a>, <a href="https://sentiersdumoulin.com/en/tarif">its pricing page</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/8058444">OpenStreetMap relation 8058444</a>, which is what fences the network's trails. Pin marks the OSM site entrance at 99 chemin du Moulin, measured at 347 m. Prices, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
