  <Placemark>
    <name>Retallack (British Columbia) [lodge package]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Retallack 1075 m - lodge at the old townsite, between Kaslo and New Denver</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Cat-assisted mountain biking deep in the Selkirk Mountains, on the same machines that run the cat-skiing operation in winter - one of very few places anywhere that does it. Riders average six to ten runs and 3,600-4,600 m of descent a day on private, guided, hand-built loam in old-growth cedar and hemlock; the longest single run drops about 1,800 m, among the longest lift-assisted descents in the world. Intermediate to expert only, sold as multi-day lodge packages rather than day tickets.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Snowcat uplift, guided. Packages include lodging, meals and guiding - there is no day-ticket option and no public access to the trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer only, roughly July to September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>New Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Nelson</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Kelowna</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.retallack.com/mountain-biking/">Retallack</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, packages and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
