  <Placemark>
    <name>Valmont Bike Park (Colorado, USA) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Boulder 1600 m - Valmont Bike Park, east of downtown</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>17 hectares of purpose-built cycling terrain inside the city of Boulder, and the model that a generation of North American municipal bike parks copied. Around 43 short trails and features across zones for every discipline: slopestyle and dirt jumps, dual slalom, pump tracks, a cyclocross course, technical rock gardens and progression lines, all colour-graded green to red with XS-to-XL technical ratings. Flat by Colorado standards - the elevation comes from what was built, not the hill.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; the park is compact and everything is re-ridden in minutes. Free, open dawn to dusk, run by the City of Boulder.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round as conditions allow - the park closes when the surface is too wet to ride without damage.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Boulder centre</td><td>Bike</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://bouldercolorado.gov/locations/valmont-bike-park">City of Boulder</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-105.234250,40.031700,1601</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
