  <Placemark>
    <name>Bailey Mountain Bike Park (North Carolina, USA) [paid entry]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mars Hill 680 m - bike park beside Mars Hill University</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The first bike park in the United States owned and operated by a university - Mars Hill built it around its collegiate cycling programme, half an hour north of Asheville. Downhill and enduro lines drop the flank of Bailey Mountain through Appalachian hardwood, mixing machine-built jump trails with steep, rooty natural descents, and the park hosts collegiate and regional gravity racing. Compact, but with real vertical for the region.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Shuttle uplift on operating days, otherwise pedal access. Paid entry; the park runs to a published calendar rather than daily.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly spring to autumn on published days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mars Hill</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Asheville</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mhu.edu/">Mars Hill University</a>, park operator listings and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, opening days and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-82.559420,35.820090,678</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">bailey-mountain</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="tags">intermediate expert bike-park dh enduro shuttle</mwm:value>
