  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Craigieburn Trails (Canterbury, New Zealand) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Craigieburn 810 m - Mistletoe Flat car park, off the Arthur's Pass highway</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Backcountry Southern Alps riding an hour and a half from Christchurch, and a very different proposition from the country's flow-trail parks: dual-use tramping and biking tracks through beech forest and above the bushline in the Castle Hill basin, linking the Craigieburn ski area at 1,300 m down some 600 m to Castle Hill village. Craigieburn Edge is the signature - grade 5, along exposed ridgelines before dropping into the beech - and the Dracophyllum and Luge tracks fill out the network. Intermediate to advanced, exposed, and a long way from help.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no shuttle; the ski-field road and the tracks are the climb. Free, on Department of Conservation land.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly December to April. Snow closes the high sections in winter and the weather at 1,300 m turns fast in any season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Castle Hill village</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Christchurch</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.craigieburntrails.org.nz/">Craigieburn Trails</a>, <a href="https://www.newzealand.com/us/feature/craigieburn-mountain-biking-tracks/">Tourism New Zealand</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>171.731000,-43.151180,808</coordinates></Point>
