  <Placemark>
    <name>St Helens and Bay of Fires (Tasmania, Australia) [free, shuttle extra]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>St Helens 5 m - trailhead in town, on Georges Bay</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The coastal half of Tasmania's trail-building boom, and the natural pairing with Blue Derby an hour inland. Two distinct offerings: a stacked-loop network of about 65 km on the dry granite hills immediately south of St Helens, graded green through double black; and the Bay of Fires Trail, a 42 km point-to-point that starts in sub-alpine terrain on top of the Blue Tier, drops through myrtle forest and tree ferns, and finishes on the sand at Swimcart Beach. Coastal granite, white sand and orange lichen the whole way down.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The town loops are pedalled. The Bay of Fires trail is one-way and needs a shuttle to the Blue Tier start - several operators run it from St Helens. Trail use is free.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, with a drier east-coast climate than the rest of Tasmania. Summer and autumn are best.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>St Helens</td><td>Bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Launceston</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr><tr><td>Derby</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.discovertasmania.com.au/things-to-do/outdoor-and-adventure/sthelensmountainbiketrails/">Discover Tasmania</a>, <a href="https://destinationbayoffires.com/st-helens-mtb-trails/">Destination Bay of Fires</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>148.248810,-41.324970,4</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
