        <mwm:value key="tags">beginner expert natural dh enduro shuttle no-lift rain-resilient</mwm:value>
      </mwm:properties>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon>
      <mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mogo Trails (New South Wales, Australia) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mogo 135 m - Mitchells trailhead in Mogo State Forest</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The largest new trail network on the New South Wales south coast: 72 purpose-built trails over about 125 km in Mogo State Forest, ten minutes from Batemans Bay and three hours from Canberra. The grading runs the whole way from green family loops through blue flow to full double black and dedicated jump trails, with the 28 km Burnaaga adventure trail added on top. Spotted-gum forest on sandy, fast-draining soil, rebuilt on ground that burned in the 2019-20 fires.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no commercial shuttle; the network is designed as stacked pedal loops from several trailheads. Free.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. Trails close during total fire bans and after heavy rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Batemans Bay</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Canberra</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr><tr><td>Sydney</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://mogotrails.com.au/the-trails/">Mogo Trails</a>, <a href="https://www.visitnsw.com/destinations/south-coast/batemans-bay-and-eurobodalla/mogo/attractions/mogo-trails-mogo-mountain-biking-trails">Visit NSW</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>150.158070,-35.784110,137</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
