    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>You Yangs Regional Park (Victoria, Australia) [free, park entry]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>You Yangs 150 m - regional park entrance, between Melbourne and Geelong</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Melbourne's nearest real mountain biking, on a granite outcrop rising abruptly out of flat farmland west of the city. Over 50 km across two areas: the Kurrajong plantation holds about 20 km of three flowing loops through eucalypt plantation, while the Stockyards area to the north has the steeper, more technical riding, three downhill tracks and the granite slabs the park is known for. Well over 100,000 rider visits a year, and one of the busiest riding areas in Victoria.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; short, steep climbs. A Parks Victoria vehicle entry fee applies.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. Trails close on days of total fire ban and after heavy rain; summer is hot and exposed.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Geelong</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Melbourne</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.parks.vic.gov.au/places-to-see/parks/you-yangs-regional-park/things-to-do/mountain-bike-riding-in-you-yangs-regional-park">Parks Victoria</a>, <a href="https://www.youyangsmtbinc.com.au/site/trails.html">You Yangs MTB</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
