  <Placemark>
    <name>Fox Creek Bike Park (South Australia) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cudlee Creek 320 m - Bennetts Road car park, in the Adelaide Hills</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Adelaide's main riding area and one of the most modern community bike parks in Australia: more than 50 km of singletrack over 800 hectares of Fox Creek forest, with about 560 m of vertical to work with. The park was destroyed in the 2019-20 Black Summer fires and rebuilt from scratch, and it now includes two purpose-built adaptive mountain bike trails for two-, three- and four-wheeled cycles - still rare anywhere in the world. Green through black, all under an hour from Adelaide airport.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no shuttle; the network is built as pedal loops from several car parks. Free, open dawn to dusk year-round.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round. Closed on days of total fire ban and during forest operations - check before setting off.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Adelaide</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Adelaide airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://foxcreekbikepark.com.au/">Fox Creek Bike Park</a>, <a href="https://southaustralia.com/products/adelaide-hills/attraction/fox-creek-bike-park">South Australia</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
