  <Placemark>
    <name>Valemount Bike Park (British Columbia) [free, membership encouraged]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Valemount 1125 m - Mountain Bike Trail System trailhead, in the Robson Valley</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 80 km of trail across the bases of two mountains flanking Valemount, halfway between Jasper and the Cariboo, with about 700 m of vertical. VARDA's own guide names 56 trails in the bike park, from buttery machine-built flow (Tinfoil Hat, High Roller) to technical old-school fall-line descents (Andreas' Downhill, Firebreak), and the town has quietly turned from a highway waystation into a destination for riders across western Canada. Far enough from anywhere that the trails are rarely busy.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; a shuttle road and climb trails serve the descents. Free to ride, though the VARDA trail society asks for a season membership to fund maintenance.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly June to October, snow permitting.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Valemount</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Jasper</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Kamloops</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://visitvalemount.ca/riding-the-valemount-mountain-bike-park/">Tourism Valemount</a>, <a href="https://www.mountainbikingbc.ca/thompson-okanagan/valemount/">Mountain Biking BC</a>, <a href="https://ridevalemount.com/mountain-biking/">VARDA's trail guide</a> (which classifies each name as descent, climb or connector) and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
