  <Placemark>
    <name>Kolo Bike Park (North Carolina, USA) [19 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Asheville 680 m - Adventure Center of Asheville, south of downtown</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact commercial park inside Asheville itself, and the easy way into a region better known for the hard riding of Pisgah and DuPont: about 8 km of purpose-built singletrack on rolling terrain, plus pump tracks and a skills park, with a progression built in for beginners and children. A full bike shop and rental fleet share the site with the Adventure Center's zip lines and ropes course.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; the hill is small and the loops are short. Day pass 19 USD, with a 10 USD rate on Sundays. Rental available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, weather permitting.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Asheville downtown</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Charlotte</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://ashevilletreetopsadventurepark.com/kolo-bike-park/">Kolo Bike Park</a>, <a href="https://www.exploreasheville.com/asheville/listing/recreation-nature/kolo-bike-park">Explore Asheville</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
