  <Placemark>
    <name>Smugglers&#x27; Notch Bike Park (Vermont, USA) [15 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Smugglers' Notch 335 m - Morse Highlands base, where the conveyor lift runs</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact three-acre gravity park at a Vermont family resort rather than a full mountain operation: a flat-ground skills area, a pump track and a two-acre downhill skills park with about 105 m of vertical, served by a Wonder Carpet conveyor. Two flow trails, a rock garden and a jump line drop off it. Around the resort, roughly 8 km of singletrack and 13 km of doubletrack fill out the day, and the wider Vermont network is on the doorstep.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A conveyor carpet lift serves the downhill skills park, running late morning and afternoon. Day pass around 15 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer into early autumn, following the resort calendar.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Jeffersonville</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Burlington</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.smuggs.com/facilities/smugglers-notch-bike-park/">Smugglers’ Notch Resort</a>, <a href="https://vmba.org/plan_your_ride/smugglers-notch-resort/">VMBA</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
