  <Placemark>
    <name>The Summit Bechtel Reserve (West Virginia, USA) [free, check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Glen Jean 550 m - Jared Harvey mountain bike trails and bike shop</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the largest purpose-built mountain bike facilities in the United States, on the Boy Scouts' national reserve above the New River Gorge - by total mileage it ranks around third in the country. The Jared Harvey trails cover flow lines, a dual-slalom course, a skills park, a dirt-jump learning zone and several pump tracks, and since 2018 they have been open to the public outside Scouting events. Appalachian sandstone, and the New River Gorge climbing and rafting on the doorstep.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; a mountain bike road serves the upper trails. Public access is free but subject to the reserve's event calendar - check before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Spring to autumn, around the reserve's programme.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Beckley</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Charleston WV</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.summitbsa.org/venues/jared-harvey-mountain-bike-trails/">Summit Bechtel Reserve</a>, <a href="https://wvexplorer.com/2018/12/07/world-class-trails-at-scout-reserve-now-open-to-mountain-bikers/">West Virginia Explorer</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
