  <Placemark>
    <name>Pomerelle Mountain Resort (Idaho, USA) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Pomerelle 2350 m - base lodge in the Albion Mountains</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A small, high, dry Idaho hill in the Sawtooth National Forest, and part of the state's long lift-served biking history. Six old-school downhill trails cover about 16 km with roughly 300 m of vertical off the triple chair, with big views over the Magic Valley from the top. This is not a modern flow park - the trails are raw and the lift runs on very few days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The triple chairlift takes bikes, but lift-served days are limited - in recent seasons only a race weekend for the Pomerelle Pounder, one of Idaho's longest-running mountain bike races. Otherwise pedal up. Check the operator before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Short summer season, and only on published lift days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Albion</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Burley</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Twin Falls</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://visitidaho.org/things-to-do/mountain-biking/pomerelle-mountain-resort-2/">Visit Idaho</a>, <a href="https://mtbparks.com/Idaho/224-Pomerelle-Mountain-Resort/View-details.html">MTBparks</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
