  <Placemark>
    <name>Matarranya Dirt Park (Spain) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Matarranya, Aragon, Spain 708 m - local bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A built dirt and jump park on the Aragonese side of the Matarranya, in the hills between Teruel and the Ebro. OpenStreetMap records it as a bike park; the surrounding Matarranya is better known for its long dry-stone singletrack.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; a small built park, ridden in short laps. Access is normally free, but the operator publishes little - check locally before making a trip of it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Not published. Built parks of this kind normally ride from spring to autumn and close when the ground is too wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Valderrobres</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Zaragoza</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <small>Placed from the OpenStreetMap object below rather than from an operator's own map, so the trail detail here is deliberately thin.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1496141003">OSM way 1496141003</a>.</i>]]></description>
