    <name>Juraflow (Germany) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bavaria, Germany 536 m - local bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A flow trail on the Franconian Jura near Eichstaett, built and maintained by the DAV Sektion Eichstaett. Tagged in OpenStreetMap for mountain biking and BMX; club-built trails like this are how most of Bavaria outside the Alps gets legal gravity.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; a small built park, ridden in short laps. Access is normally free, but the operator publishes little - check locally before making a trip of it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Not published. Built parks of this kind normally ride from spring to autumn and close when the ground is too wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Eichstaett</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Ingolstadt</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
