  <Placemark>
    <name>Fraser Bike Park (USA) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Colorado, USA 2617 m - local bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A town bike park in Fraser, in the Winter Park valley at 2,600 m, and a useful warm-up or wet-day alternative to the Trestle park up the road. Built jumps, berms and progression lines.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; a small built park, ridden in short laps. Access is normally free, but the operator publishes little - check locally before making a trip of it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Not published. Built parks of this kind normally ride from spring to autumn and close when the ground is too wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Winter Park</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
