  <Placemark>
    <name>Cannock Chase (Staffordshire, UK) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cannock Chase - the Midlands' original trail centre</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two waymarked trails built and maintained by the Chase Trails volunteer group. 'Follow the Dog' is a 6.7 mile red loop of fast flowing singletrack with boardwalks, rock gardens and drop-offs; 'The Monkey Trail' extends it with bigger climbs, more technical descents and optional black-graded lines. Over 35,000 volunteer hours went into building them.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - pedal-up trail centre. Free to ride, all year. Parking charge at Birches Valley.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Birmingham</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Stafford</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://chasetrails.co.uk/">Chase Trails</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
