  <Placemark>
    <name>Dalby Forest (North Yorkshire, UK) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Dalby Forest - North York Moors trail centre</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A Forestry England trail centre on the southern slopes of the North York Moors. The red route is a long experts-only ride combining fast flowing singletrack, technical features, challenging climbs and tricky descents; green and blue routes and a skills area serve everyone else.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - pedal-up trail centre. Forest Drive toll applies to vehicles.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>York</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Scarborough</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.forestryengland.uk/dalby-forest">Forestry England</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
