  <Placemark>
    <name>Brechfa Forest (Carmarthenshire, Wales) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Brechfa - natural-feeling Welsh forest trails</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Three waymarked trails across two trailheads. Byrgwm car park serves a green with a blue extension and the black 'Raven'; the red 'Gorlech' starts from Abergorlech. The riding feels more natural and less manufactured than most Welsh trail centres.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - pedal-up. Free to ride and free parking.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Carmarthen</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Swansea</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://naturalresources.wales/days-out/places-to-visit/south-west-wales/brechfa-forest/">Natural Resources Wales</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
