  <Placemark>
    <name>Aston Hill Bike Park (Buckinghamshire, UK) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Aston Hill - the south's most historic bike park, reopened</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Five graded downhill runs, a 4X track and a two-part XC loop on a steep slope in the Chilterns, forty minutes from central London. Challenging when dry and a serious proposition when wet. Closed in 2021 by ash dieback, it reopened in 2025 under Bike Park Chilterns CIC with re-imagined trails on a ten-year Forestry England lease.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - push or pedal up. Membership or day ticket required.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>London</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr><tr><td>Wendover</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://astonhill.co.uk/">Aston Hill Bike Park</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
