  <Placemark>
    <name>7stanes Ae (Dumfries and Galloway, Scotland) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ae Forest - 7stanes downhill and the Ae Line</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the seven 7stanes centres, with green, blue and red graded trails plus a skills area and a genuine extreme downhill section used for serious racing. The 'Ae Line' descent is the draw for gravity riders.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift for the waymarked trails; uplift days are run by third parties on the downhill. Free to ride.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Dumfries</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Glasgow</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://forestryandland.gov.scot/visit/activities/mountain-biking/7stanes">Forestry and Land Scotland</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
