  <Placemark>
    <name>7stanes Mabie (Dumfries and Galloway, Scotland) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mabie - twisting woodland singletrack and a skills area</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A 7stanes centre with a skills area and trails that snake through mature woodland. The red 'Phoenix' trail is the main loop; there is also a small downhill and freeride area.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - pedal-up. Free to ride, parking charge.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Dumfries</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Carlisle</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://forestryandland.gov.scot/visit/activities/mountain-biking/7stanes">Forestry and Land Scotland</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
