  <Placemark>
    <name>7stanes Newcastleton (Scottish Borders, Scotland) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Newcastleton - the best-kept secret of the 7stanes</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Trails suitable for all levels with a fraction of the crowds of Glentress. Riders consistently describe it as the quietest and most underrated of the seven centres.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - pedal-up. Free to ride.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
