  <Placemark>
    <name>Stainburn Forest (North Yorkshire, UK) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Stainburn - short, brutal and technical</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A small Yorkshire trail centre with a reputation out of proportion to its size. The black 'Warren Boulder Trail' and the technical climbs are among the hardest waymarked riding in England; a red and a skills loop round it out.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - pedal-up. Free to ride.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Leeds</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Harrogate</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.forestryengland.uk/">Forestry England</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
