  <Placemark>
    <name>Lee Quarry (Lancashire, UK) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lee Quarry - Pennine gritstone and slate</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A reclaimed quarry above Bacup turned into a rocky trail network with a technical black loop, a skills area and jump lines, all on hard-wearing stone that rides well in the wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - pedal-up. Free to ride.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
