  <Placemark>
    <name>Moray Monster Trails (Moray, Scotland) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Moray Monster Trails - 30 km across three sites</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Thirty kilometres of trails split across three separate and independent sites. Winding Walks has the extreme freeride terrain and the red-graded Fochabers Ring; Ordiequish holds the easier blue routes. Long described as mountain biking's best kept secret.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - pedal-up. Free to ride.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Elgin</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Inverness</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://forestryandland.gov.scot/visit/moray-monster-trails">Forestry and Land Scotland</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
