  <Placemark>
    <name>Makara Peak Mountain Bike Park (Wellington, New Zealand) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Makara Peak - 50 km of volunteer-built singletrack above Wellington</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 50 km of singletrack across 250 hectares of dense native bush, 7 km from central Wellington, with more than 40 trail options graded easy through difficult. Highlights include a 72 m suspension bridge and panoramic views over Wellington Harbour, Cook Strait and, on a clear day, the South Island. Established in 1998 by volunteers on what was gorse-covered farmland.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - pedal-up. Free to ride, open year-round. Four main entry points, the principal one on South Karori Road.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; wettest months are winter.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Wellington CBD</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Karori</td><td>Bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://makarapeak.bike/">Makara Peak Supporters</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
