  <Placemark>
    <name>Signal Hill (Dunedin, New Zealand) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Signal Hill - New Zealand's best downhill track</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>More than 29 km of trails minutes from central Dunedin. Signal Hill carries the mantle of having New Zealand's best downhill track: a demanding beast with rock gardens, jump lines, ruts and steep sections to test the best. The Big Easy is a 6.1 km climb built so gently that almost any rider can top out at the lookout, and The Plateau hub links descent options at every grade.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift - pedal-up, though the Big Easy makes the climb painless. Free to ride. Main car park off Logan Park Drive.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; wettest months are winter.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Dunedin CBD</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Dunedin CBD</td><td>Bike</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.dunedin.govt.nz/">Dunedin City Council</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
