  <Placemark>
    <name>Coast Gravity Park (Sechelt, BC, Canada) [shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Coast Gravity Park - built by riders, for riders</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A privately owned 160-acre gravity park on the Sunshine Coast with 17 trails from beginner to pro, founded in 2013 by local riders and trail builders. Fast flowy lines sit alongside serious jump trails, and it was the first bike park in the region to offer year-round uplift. Host of Park After Dark, the Backwoods Jam and BC Cup rounds.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Shuttle uplift to the top of the trails. Full-day, half-day, multi-day, family and season passes; Norco rentals and coaching on site. Check current prices before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; trails may close in heavy rain or storm damage.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access forest trails; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sechelt</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Vancouver</td><td>Car + ferry</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.coastgravitypark.ca/">Coast Gravity Park</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
