  <Placemark>
    <name>Seven Springs Bike Park (Pennsylvania, USA) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Seven Springs - 18 lift-served trails in the Laurel Highlands</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A downhill park opened in 2008 in the Laurel Highlands, about 60 miles southeast of Pittsburgh. Eighteen downhill trails on the Front Face are served by the Polar Bear Express high-speed chairlift over 452 ft of vertical; the North Face, served by the Gunnar high-speed chairlift, adds more than three miles of trail and 750 ft of drop. Trails are graded like ski runs, with berms, rock gardens, drops, ladder bridges, tabletops and 20+ foot jumps.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Two high-speed chairlifts carry bikes. Day and season passes; check current prices and operating days before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from May; closed from October.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Pittsburgh</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Somerset</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.7springs.com/">Seven Springs Mountain Resort</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
