  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Hood Skibowl Bike Park (Oregon, USA) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Skibowl West 1121 m - base area parking, at the foot of the lifts</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Chairlift-accessed downhill on the southern slopes of Mount Hood at Government Camp, with 1,500 ft of vertical filled with trails for downhill riders of all abilities. The Adventure Park holds a freeride bike park and a skills park alongside the lift-assisted trail network, served by the Scenic Sky Chair.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Scenic Sky Chair carries bikes. Day passes; typical season mid-June through October. Check current prices and operating days.<br/><br/>
    The pin is the <b>Skibowl West</b> parking lot on the north side of Mount Hood Highway (US-26), directly below the Lower Bowl Chair Lift base station at 1,113 m and the two rope tows. Skibowl East, on the far side of the highway, is the separate Adventure Park base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from June; closed from November.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Portland</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Government Camp</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.skibowl.com/">Mount Hood Skibowl</a>, pin from <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/150578162">OpenStreetMap way 150578162</a> ("Skibowl West Parking").
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
