  <Placemark>
    <name>Cote Bleue - Chaine de l'Estaque (Bouches-du-Rhone, France) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cote Bleue - limestone garrigue between Marseille and Marignane</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Chaine de l'Estaque running west from Marseille to Martigues, dropping straight into the Mediterranean along the Cote Bleue. Rocky white-limestone singletrack through low garrigue with calanque views the whole way, linking Carro, Sausset-les-Pins, Carry-le-Rouet and Niolon. Technical and loose rather than steep - grip on polished limestone is the limiting factor, not gradient.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up. The pin marks the seaside trailhead at Carro; the riding climbs inland onto the ridge. Free access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; best in spring and autumn. <b>Massifs in Bouches-du-Rhone and the Var are closed by prefectoral order on high fire-risk days between June and September</b> - check the daily access map before setting off.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access public land; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Marseille</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Marignane</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C%C3%B4te_Bleue">Cote Bleue</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
