  <Placemark>
    <name>Mont Ventoux (Vaucluse, France) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mont Ventoux 1426 m - a 25 km enduro descent off the Giant of Provence</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The south face of Mont Ventoux carries a 25 km enduro descent taking around three hours, dropping from the bare limestone summit ridge through the beech forest to the vineyards below. The Espace VTT-FFC Ventoux marks 13 routes across the massif, two of them enduro-graded, and there are technical descents around the Chalet Reynard area. The pin is at Chalet Reynard, the road-accessible start point at 1,426 m.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - shuttle to Chalet Reynard or the summit by road, or pedal the famous climb. Free access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; best in spring and autumn. <b>Massifs in Bouches-du-Rhone and the Var are closed by prefectoral order on high fire-risk days between June and September</b> - check the daily access map before setting off.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access public land; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bedoin</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Avignon</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.parcduventoux.fr/nos-actions/lecotourisme/espace-vtt-ffc/">Parc naturel regional du Mont-Ventoux</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
