  <Placemark>
    <name>Foret de Janas - Cap Sicie (Var, France) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Notre-Dame du Mai 321 m - the Cap Sicie massif above La Seyne</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The pine and oak forest of Janas covering the Cap Sicie massif between La Seyne-sur-Mer and Six-Fours-les-Plages, with a light enduro loop of fun singletrack and long sea views. Trails such as les Baruelles, the route des Oratoires and the Francillon circuit link forest tracks to singletrack; the pin sits at the Notre-Dame du Mai chapel on the summit ridge, where the descents to the sea start.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal or shuttle up the piste to Notre-Dame du Mai. Free access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; best in spring and autumn. <b>Massifs in Bouches-du-Rhone and the Var are closed by prefectoral order on high fire-risk days between June and September</b> - check the daily access map before setting off.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access public land; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>La Seyne-sur-Mer</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Toulon</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://laseyne.info/index.php/la-seyne/foret-de-janas">Foret de Janas</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
