  <Placemark>
    <name>Parc naturel regional de la Sainte-Baume (Var, France) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sainte-Baume 697 m - garrigue and forest singletrack under the ridge</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A regional natural park built around the long Sainte-Baume ridge, with rides of three hours and more linking garrigue and forest singletrack under the north face and its ancient beech forest. The pin is at Plan-d'Aups-Sainte-Baume, the plateau village that is the usual starting point.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up. Free access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; best in spring and autumn. <b>Massifs in Bouches-du-Rhone and the Var are closed by prefectoral order on high fire-risk days between June and September</b> - check the daily access map before setting off.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access public land; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Aubagne</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Marseille</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.pnr-saintebaume.fr/">Parc naturel regional de la Sainte-Baume</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
