  <Placemark>
    <name>Massif du Garlaban (Bouches-du-Rhone, France) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Le Garlaban 673 m - Pagnol's white cliffs above Aubagne</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The white limestone massif above Aubagne, the landscape of Marcel Pagnol's books. The 'balcons de Lascours' traverse winds along the mountainside with views over Garlaban, the Sainte-Baume, Gemenos, Aubagne and Cap Canaille; the Espigaou Riders route covers 21 km across the sector. Rocky, exposed and technical, with very little shade.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up. Free access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; best in spring and autumn. <b>Massifs in Bouches-du-Rhone and the Var are closed by prefectoral order on high fire-risk days between June and September</b> - check the daily access map before setting off.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access public land; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Aubagne</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Marseille</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.utagawavtt.com/randonnee-vtt-gps/Le-Garlaban-best-of-14680">Le Garlaban</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
