  <Placemark>
    <name>Espace VTT du Parc de Figuerolles (Martigues, France) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Parc de Figuerolles - a free municipal VTT space above the Etang de Berre</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A 130-hectare municipal park on the edge of the Etang de Berre with a dedicated VTT space open seven days a week, free of charge, split into a beginner zone and one for more adventurous riders. Around a dozen singletrack lines, five or six of them built up with tables, gaps, drops and banked turns, plus a pumptrack. The main descent drops 130 m from the Lebre plateau to Figuerolles beach and is built as an enduro trail.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal or push up. Free access, seven days a week.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; best in spring and autumn. <b>Massifs in Bouches-du-Rhone and the Var are closed by prefectoral order on high fire-risk days between June and September</b> - check the daily access map before setting off.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access public land; no ticket office.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Martigues</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Marseille</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.ville-martigues.fr/loisirs/parc-de-figuerolles/vtt">Ville de Martigues</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
