  <Placemark>
    <name>Wilder Ranch State Park (Santa Cruz, California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Wilder Ranch - coastal terrace and redwood singletrack west of Santa Cruz</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A state park immediately west of Santa Cruz combining flat coastal-terrace tracks above the sea cliffs with a large upland network of singletrack and fire road climbing into the redwoods and chaparral. Long-standing Santa Cruz classics such as Enchanted Loop, Wilder Ridge and Zane Grey are here, and it connects into the wider Gray Whale Ranch and UCSB terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up. State park day-use parking fee.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; trails are best in spring and can be closed or off-limits when wet in winter.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Check the park's own hours and any wet-weather closure before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Santa Cruz</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>San Jose</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=549">California State Parks</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
