  <Placemark>
    <name>DeLaveaga Park (Santa Cruz, California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>DeLaveaga - Santa Cruz's steep in-town gravity park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A city park on the east side of Santa Cruz with a dense, steep network cut into the eucalyptus and oak. Short, sharp and famously technical, with the Top of the World lines and a set of well-known jump and freeride trails packed into a small hillside. The default after-work ride for the Santa Cruz industry.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal or shuttle up. Free access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; trails are best in spring and can be closed or off-limits when wet in winter.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Check the park's own hours and any wet-weather closure before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Santa Cruz</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Santa Cruz</td><td>Bike</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.cityofsantacruz.com/government/city-departments/parks-recreation">City of Santa Cruz</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
