  <Placemark>
    <name>Waterdog Lake and Sugarloaf (Belmont, California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Waterdog Lake - the Peninsula's technical backyard network</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact open-space network above Belmont on the San Francisco Peninsula, climbing from the lake through oak and chaparral onto Sugarloaf Mountain. Rooty, rocky and steeper than its small footprint suggests, it is the main technical riding between San Francisco and the South Bay and the go-to after-work loop for Silicon Valley.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up. Free access; street parking at the Lake Road trailhead.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; trails are best in spring and can be closed or off-limits when wet in winter.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Check the park's own hours and any wet-weather closure before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>San Mateo</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Palo Alto</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.belmont.gov/departments/parks-recreation/parks-trails">City of Belmont</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
