  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Diablo State Park (California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mount Diablo 610 m - the East Bay's big mountain</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The dominant peak of the East Bay, with a large network of fire roads and some singletrack spread over its flanks. Long sustained climbs and descents on loose, rocky surface, and on a clear day one of the widest views in California from the summit road. The pin marks the park; several trailheads ring the mountain from Walnut Creek, Danville and Clayton.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up. State park day-use fee at the staffed entrances.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; trails are best in spring and can be closed or off-limits when wet in winter.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Check the park's own hours and any wet-weather closure before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Walnut Creek</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>San Francisco</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=517">California State Parks</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
