  <Placemark>
    <name>Briones Regional Park (California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Briones - open grassland ridges in the East Bay hills</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A large East Bay Regional Park District holding of rolling grassland and oak between Lafayette, Martinez and Orinda. Riding is mostly wide fire road over steep grassy ridges with long open descents; exposed and hot in summer, and heavy going after rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up. Free access; parking fee at the staffed entrances.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; trails are best in spring and can be closed or off-limits when wet in winter.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Check the park's own hours and any wet-weather closure before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lafayette</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Berkeley</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.ebparks.org/parks/briones">East Bay Regional Park District</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
