  <Placemark>
    <name>Skyline Wilderness Park (Napa, California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Skyline Wilderness Park - first-class technical singletrack in Napa</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The biggest riding right in Napa, and one of the few parks in the North Bay with genuinely first-class technical singletrack. The Manzanita, Thatcher's Rim Rock, Napa-Solano Ridge and Skyline trails string together narrow, rocky lines with drops, steps and steep loose sections; most of the park needs intermediate to advanced skills. All trails are shared with hikers and horses.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up. Park entry fee.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; trails are best in spring and can be closed or off-limits when wet in winter.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Check the park's own hours and any wet-weather closure before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Napa</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>San Francisco</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.skylinepark.org/activities/biking/">Skyline Wilderness Park</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
