  <Placemark>
    <name>Sonoma Coast State Park - Willow Creek (California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Willow Creek - 18 miles of fire road from Occidental to the sea</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Willow Creek unit of Sonoma Coast State Park, where fire roads run roughly 18 miles from outside Occidental all the way down to the coast. Views over the Willow Creek watershed on one side and the Russian River on the other, with numerous junctions allowing loops or a point-to-point out to the ocean. Wide-track riding rather than technical singletrack.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up, or run it one-way with a shuttle. Free access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; trails are best in spring and can be closed or off-limits when wet in winter.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Check the park's own hours and any wet-weather closure before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Jenner</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Santa Rosa</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=451">California State Parks</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
