  <Placemark>
    <name>Simas Peak - Toro Park (Monterey County, California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Simas Peak 682 m - double black above the Monterey Bay</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The high point of the Toro Regional Park network south of Salinas, reached beyond Ollason Peak and Black Mountain. Rated double black diamond with an extreme physical grade: parts of the trail approach 30 per cent, and dry hardpack under a thin layer of loose gravel gives very little grip, so both the climb and the descent can turn into hike-a-bike. The reward is a view over Monterey Bay on one side and the Salinas Valley on the other. Few people ride up here - plan accordingly.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal and push up from the Toro Park entrance. County park day-use fee.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; trails are best in spring and can be closed or off-limits when wet in winter.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Check the park's own hours and any wet-weather closure before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Salinas</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Monterey</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.co.monterey.ca.us/government/departments-a-h/administrative-office/parks/toro-park">Monterey County Parks</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
