  <Placemark>
    <name>Limerock Peak (Sylmar, California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Limerock Peak 904 m - the biggest climb and descent in Sylmar</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The route starts on Little Tujunga Road and heads up the south east ridge to the open summit of Limerock, gaining 1,476 ft - the most vertical of any mountain bike trail in the Sylmar area - before dropping the same way. Steep and rocky throughout, with panoramic views from the top over the San Fernando Valley. Rated the hardest ride in the area and typically taking a little over two hours. The terrain is coastal sage scrub with no shade at all.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up from Little Tujunga Road. Free access. The pin marks the summit, where the descent starts.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; brutally hot and shadeless in summer, and the surrounding Angeles National Forest land can close on high fire-risk days.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access public land; carry more water than you think you need.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sylmar</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Los Angeles</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/r05/angeles">Angeles National Forest</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
