  <Placemark>
    <name>Towsley Canyon - Santa Clarita Woodlands (California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Towsley Canyon 423 m - trailhead for the 5.1 mile singletrack loop</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A 5.1 mile singletrack loop in Santa Clarita Woodlands Park with 1,107 ft of descent, best ridden counter-clockwise unless you enjoy suffering: it climbs 600 ft quickly up a set of pyramid-style switchbacks, then another 400 ft to the summit. The payoff is at the end - a fast, flowing section of wide singletrack with small jumps and berms. The neighbouring East Canyon and Los Pinetos trails extend the ride from the same park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - pedal up from Ed Davis Park at Towsley Canyon. Free access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; brutally hot and shadeless in summer, and the surrounding Angeles National Forest land can close on high fire-risk days.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access public land; carry more water than you think you need.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Santa Clarita</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Los Angeles</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://mrca.ca.gov/parks/park-listing/ed-davis-park-in-towsley-canyon/">Mountains Recreation and Conservation Authority</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
