  <Placemark>
    <name>Palisades Tahoe - Olympic Valley (Lake Tahoe, California, USA) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Olympic Valley 1897 m - pedal-access riding, not a lift-served bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The 1960 Olympic valley is a hub for a large Tahoe trail network rather than a downhill park. The Western States trail climbs from Highway 89 between Olympic Valley and Alpine Meadows up the steep face known as The Wall, with newer singletrack built to make the climb more bike-friendly; from the top you can descend banked turns back to the start or drop toward Olympic Valley. The Jackass network on the outskirts of Truckee is easily reached from here, climbing around 6 miles and 2,000 vertical feet of fire road to a purpose-built downhill with sweeping turns. Valley-floor bike paths link along the Truckee River toward the lake.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>Bikes are not allowed on the Aerial Tram</b>, and there is no bike access past Shirley Lake - this is not a lift-served park. Uphill access for bikes is via the Thunder Mountain trail. Free to ride; bike rental in the village.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from June once the snow clears; closed from October.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>High Sierra at ~1,900 m - snow lingers on the upper trails well into June.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Truckee</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Reno</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.palisadestahoe.com/events-and-activities/biking-lake-tahoe">Palisades Tahoe</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
