  <Placemark>
    <name>Uludag Sarialan (Bursa, Turkey) [cable car carries bikes]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sarialan 1634 m - top station of the Bursa Uludag cable car</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>There is no built bike park here: the riding is the natural descent off the Uludag massif south of Bursa, reached by cable car. The best-documented line starts at Sarialan with a rocky, technical upper section, drops into a stream-bed flow section and finishes on flat road. The full Sarialan-to-Bursa descent used by the HASDOWNHILL downhill-enduro race falls about 1,240 m from the top station to the city, over steep slopes, rock sections and tight natural turns; 125 riders started the most recent edition. A shorter technical downhill line of around 5 km is also ridden on the mountain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Bursa Teleferik runs in sections from Teferruc at 390 m via Kadiyayla at 1235 m to Sarialan at 1634 m, and on to Kurbagakaya at 1792 m; the trip takes roughly 25 minutes. Bikes are carried and are charged separately: a rider report quoted 35 TL for the passenger fare plus 60 TL for the bike, with bike carriage allowed in a midday window. Fares and the bike window both change, so confirm with the operator before turning up with a bike. A summer chairlift also runs from Sarialan towards Cobankaya.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 November (estimated snow-free indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: cable-car hours<br/><small>Bike-carriage times and prices are from rider reports, not an operator page, and were not reconfirmed. No trail lines are drawn: OpenStreetMap has no mountain-bike-tagged geometry anywhere in the Uludag massif, and the public GPS-trace archive holds only road and driving logs here. The descents are unsigned natural lines inside Uludag National Park - check access rules and trail legality locally before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bursa centre</td><td>Car or tram to Teferruc</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Istanbul</td><td>Ferry and car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: Bursa Teleferik station and lift geometry from OpenStreetMap; pin on the <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/471794341">Sarialan top station</a> (way 471794341), measured at 1634 m. Trail and race detail from Turkish press coverage of the Uludag downhill-enduro event and from rider reports on bike carriage. Verify current operations locally.</i>]]></description>
