  <Placemark>
    <name>Kazdagi / Mount Ida (Balikesir, Turkey) [no lift, shuttle or pedal]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sarikiz tepesi yolu 1407 m - top of the mapped descent</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Kazdagi National Park, the ancient Mount Ida, rises straight out of the Gulf of Edremit, and the forest-track network off its ridge is graded for mountain biking in OpenStreetMap. Two lines are drawn here: the upper <b>Sarikiz tepesi yolu</b>, 5.1 km of grade 2-3 track losing 261 m off the 1,407 m ridge, and a long grade-4 descent of 10.7 km that drops 691 m from 1,104 m to 413 m on the Edremit side. The surface is tagged as rock garden, ground and gravel, which matches the reputation: rocky, loose and unrelenting rather than flowy. Published route guides put the riding here at intermediate to difficult.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no shuttle service. Riders either pedal the forest roads from the Edremit side or arrange a vehicle to the ridge. Free, but the national park charges vehicle entry at the gate.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (estimated snow-free indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>These are forest tracks carrying mountain-bike difficulty tags in OpenStreetMap, not a signed bike-trail network - nothing here is waymarked or maintained for gravity riding. The ridge holds snow in winter while the lower half stays rideable. Kazdagi is a national park with protected endemic flora; check current access rules and any seasonal fire closures at the gate before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Edremit</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Izmir</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr><tr><td>Canakkale</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: trail geometry and difficulty grades from OpenStreetMap; pin on the top of <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/494856350">way 494856350</a> ("Mount Ida - Sarikiz tepesi yolu"), measured at 1407 m. Route difficulty corroborated by published Kazdagi cycling-tour guides. Verify access locally.</i>]]></description>
