  <Placemark>
    <name>Station Mountain Bike Park (Texas) [50 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Station Mountain 305 m - shuttle base on Crider Road, Marble Falls, Texas</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A shuttle-served jump park in the Hill Country, opened in November 2023 and built by local rider Rhett Jones. About 6 miles of trail across roughly 20-23 short runs from green to double black on 316 ft (96 m) of vertical, and the highest density of jump trails in Texas: rollers, tabletops and gap jumps including the 45 ft gap that ends El Cinco, the largest public-access jumps in the state. It is not only jumps - Marble Falls drops through a chunky creek bed and Your Mom takes on roots and rock drops, while High, Medium and Low Tide are the beginner progression. Other named lines include 75 Hits, 'Murica, The Holder, Berm Park, Banquet, Step One, Your Dad, Nickle &amp; Dine, Beer Trail and Albanian Boogie.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Uplift is a wooden trailer towed by a tractor, running continuously while the park is open. Day pass 50 USD including unlimited shuttle laps; season pass 400 USD; the regional Loam Pass is also accepted. Pedalling the service road is allowed at any time and is not discounted. Bike shop, rentals, taco and snack shop, toilets and tent camping on site.<br/><br/>
    <p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Weekends are walk-in; on weekdays you must text ahead to arrange a shuttle. The park closes for rain and bad weather - check before driving out.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round, weather permitting.<br/>Daily opening hours: shuttles 09:00-16:00, pedalling any time<br/>
    <small>Published operating hours; the park runs Saturday and Sunday, weekdays by arrangement.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Marble Falls</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Austin</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr><tr><td>Dallas</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <small>OpenStreetMap has no mapping of this park. The pin is the published park coordinate for 1101 Crider Road, which falls on the Crider Road spur (<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/15139631">way 15139631</a>) and measures 305 m - consistent with the operator's 1011 ft base and 1327 ft summit. Approach from the east; the western gate is closed.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.stationmountain.com/">Station Mountain Bike Park</a>, <a href="https://www.twowheeledwanderer.com/posts/station-mountain-bike-park/">Two Wheeled Wanderer trail guide</a> and <a href="https://www.mtbatx.com/austintrails/bikeparks/stationmountain">MTBATX</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-98.366390,30.653010,305</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
