  <Placemark>
    <name>Rocky Hill Ranch (Texas) [10 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Rocky Hill Ranch 131 m - trailhead in the loblolly pines, 578 FM 153, Smithville, Texas</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the oldest mountain-bike ranches in Texas and the closest real singletrack to Austin, with 18-25 miles of trail threaded through 222 acres of wooded hills east of the Colorado River. The riding ranges from straightforward jeep track to ledges, short punchy climbs, twisting pine singletrack and built technical features. It is not steep - nothing here drops more than about 25 m - so the character comes from the tightness of the lines and the relentless little climbs rather than from vertical. Around 35 named trails are mapped, among them Grey's Highway, WendysWild West, West Fenceline, Tristy, Off the Lip, Tunnel o' the Pines, Omar's Howl, Longhorn Loop, Frontal Lobotomy and Miracle Mile.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift: pedal-only. Day use 10 USD per person, paid at the self-service station near the parking area; camping around 20 USD a night, with primitive sites, RV hook-ups, showers and restrooms. An annual waiver is required. Repeat riders earn a 20% discount through the ranch's RHR Dollerz scheme.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round - the ranch advertises 365 days a year.<br/>Daily opening hours: open 24 hours<br/>
    <small>Published operating hours; call ahead for trail conditions after rain, the pine soil holds water.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Smithville</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Austin</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Houston</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <small>OpenStreetMap has no building or entrance mapped for the ranch. The pin is the north end of the trail network, at the head of WendysWild West (<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/497191774">way 497191774</a>), measured at 131 m.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.rockyhillranch.com/">Rocky Hill Ranch</a> and <a href="https://explorebastropcounty.com/listings/rocky-hill-ranch/">Explore Bastrop County</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
