  <Placemark>
    <name>Bluff Creek Ranch (Texas) [10 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bluff Creek Ranch 115 m - working cattle ranch and trailhead, 537 Owl Creek Road, Warda, Texas</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The first mountain-bike ranch in Texas, and still one of the best-loved: 8.9 miles of well-shaded, rolling singletrack winding through hardwoods and pines on a working cattle ranch 60 miles east of Austin. The trails are fast and flowing rather than steep, and the tree cover makes it rideable in heat that shuts the rest of the state down. A long-standing race venue.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift: pedal-only. Day pass 10 USD per rider, 5 USD for children aged 6 to 12. Camping on site, booked by email. Online waivers are good for the calendar year.<br/><br/>
    <p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Cash or check only - no credit cards. No e-bikes with throttles; pedal-assist only.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round.<br/>Daily opening hours: gate 07:00-22:00; trails open 24 hours for campers<br/>
    <small>Published operating hours.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>La Grange</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Austin</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 20</td></tr><tr><td>Houston</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <small>Pin on the ranch building mapped in OpenStreetMap with the operator's own website (<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1943720179">node 1943720179</a>), beside the campsite node, measured at 115 m. The trail network itself is not mapped in OpenStreetMap.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://bcrwarda.com/">Bluff Creek Ranch</a> and <a href="https://roundtop.com/culture/bluff-creek-ranch-mountain-biking-trail-camping-hiking/">Round Top - Bluff Creek Ranch</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
