  <Placemark>
    <name>Mulberry Mountain Gravity Park (Arkansas) [50 USD shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mulberry Mountain 482 m - shuttle base at the lodge and general store, Ozark, Arkansas</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A shuttle-served gravity park that opened over the weekend of 6-8 March 2026 on the 400-acre Mulberry Mountain Lodging &amp; Events property, surrounded by the Ozark National Forest along the Pig Trail National Scenic Byway. Three trails so far, all cut by Gradient Trails LLC and totalling about 2 miles on 600 ft (183 m) of vertical: <b>Si Gogglin</b> (intermediate, 4200 ft, 542 ft of drop, 13% average), <b>Mulberry Mauler</b> (advanced, 2900 ft, 530 ft, 18.3%) and <b>Sasquatch Screamer</b> (advanced, 3100 ft, 530 ft, 17.4%). Beginner trails are advertised as coming, and the operator has said the vertical could reach 1400 ft if a National Forest expansion is approved.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A full-size crew-cab Polaris Ranger UTV takes five riders and bikes up the shuttle road in about four minutes. Shuttle day pass 50 USD plus tax, booked online. The trails are free to pedal up if you would rather earn them. Check in at the general store for a wristband and waiver before riding. Cabins, RV and camping on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round, with shuttles running Friday, Saturday and Sunday.<br/>Daily opening hours: shuttle days only; confirm times when booking<br/>
    <small>Operating days are published; exact hours are not, so confirm at booking.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Ozark</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bentonville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr><tr><td>Little Rock</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <small>Pin on the resort polygon mapped in OpenStreetMap (<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1390758537">way 1390758537</a>, leisure=resort, 4117 Mulberry Mountain Loop), measured at 482 m. The three gravity trails are not yet mapped in OpenStreetMap.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mulberrygravity.com/">Mulberry Mountain Gravity Park</a>, <a href="https://arkansasoutside.com/mulberry-mountain-gravity-park-opening-2026/">Arkansas Outside</a> and <a href="https://www.singletracks.com/mtb-trails/mulberry-mountain-gravity-park-opens-in-the-ozarks-with-600-vertical-feet-of-downhill-trails/">Singletracks</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
