  <Placemark>
    <name>Alpine Valley Resort (Wisconsin) [5 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Alpine Valley 251 m - base area and self-pay trail station, Elkhorn, Wisconsin</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A ski hill an hour and a half from Chicago that turns its slopes over to one long singletrack in summer: 8.1 miles with about 1035 ft of climbing and the same again of descent, laid out as two loops with a couple of short downhill shortcuts to cut the climbing. It opens with a leg-burning climb through the trees up the side of the hill, then delivers punchy climbs and fast descents around the top, with bridges, drops, rock gardens, wooden features and berms. Built for intermediate and advanced riders.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift for bikes: the resort's chairlifts are winter-only, so you pedal. Trail pass 5 USD a day or 25 USD a year, paid at the self-pay station left of the buildings at the parking area - the singletrack starts beside it. A signed waiver is required annually and helmets are mandatory. E-bikes allowed, none with throttles.<br/><br/>
    <p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Stay on the marked trail and never cross onto the golf course - the resort warns that trespassing could close the trail for everyone.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Typically ridable from April to the end of October; the resort's summer operation runs roughly late May to early November.<br/>
    <small>The resort publishes no dedicated bike-trail hours or season dates - this is a typical window, not an operator figure. Check the trail's Facebook page for current status.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lake Geneva</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Milwaukee</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Chicago</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <small>Pin on the valley station of the Lodge Chair (<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/256884218">way 256884218</a>), measured at 251 m against 318 m at its top. The bike trail itself is not mapped in OpenStreetMap.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.alpinevalleyresort.com/mountain-biking/">Alpine Valley Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.alltrails.com/trail/us/wisconsin/alpine-valley-mountain-bike-trail">AllTrails</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
