  <Placemark>
    <name>The Mountain Top at Grand Geneva (Wisconsin) [10 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>The Mountain Top 256 m - Adventure Center at the ski-hill base, Lake Geneva, Wisconsin</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Grand Geneva resort's ski hill becomes a trail centre in summer, with 8.5 miles of singletrack ranging from easy to expert. The signature line, Mountain Top, is a 5-mile blue loop with about 480 ft of climbing and the same of descent; the rest is tucked into the woods at the back of the property and gets technical - plenty of short climbs and tight, twisty sections. Nothing here is long, but the layout packs a lot of direction changes into a small hill an hour and a half from Chicago.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No uplift for bikes: the Grand Notch, Grand Valley and Grand Slope chairlifts run in winter only, so you pedal. Day pass 10 USD, annual pass 25 USD, both from the Adventure Center. Bike rental 60 USD for two hours; helmet rental 10 USD and helmets are required.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer season, running to 13 September in the published 2026 calendar.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00 daily<br/>
    <small>Published operating hours from the Adventure Center; the opening date is not published, so 1 May is a typical start.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lake Geneva</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Milwaukee</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Chicago</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <small>Pin on The Mountain Top chalet mapped in OpenStreetMap (<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/493595077">way 493595077</a>), measured at 256 m, inside the resort's winter_sports area (<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/601919996">way 601919996</a>). The bike trails are not mapped in OpenStreetMap.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.grandgeneva.com/adventure-center">Grand Geneva Adventure Center</a> and <a href="https://www.visitlakegeneva.com/things-to-do/outdoors/hiking-biking/">Visit Lake Geneva</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
