  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park Limousin (Haute-Vienne, France) [35 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Les Vignes 470 m - shuttle base at La Ferme des Vignes, La Jonchere-Saint-Maurice</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>19 marked downhill runs on 150 hectares of the Monts d'Ambazac, 20 minutes north of Limoges: 4 green, 4 blue, 7 red and 4 black. The operator names Trou Normand, Voie Blanche and Green Piste (green); Totem, Francky Trail, Lisiere and Chat Chouffy (blue); B Line, A Line, Mont Chery, Steph, Ragondin and the two enduro lines Oulala and Kaolin (red); World Cup, Raide Rock, Chainsaw and Viking Line (black). The operator advertises 300 m of vertical across the site; the ridge above the base measures about 660 m against 470 m at the farm, so a single lap is nearer 200 m. Green runs are described as wide and rolling, blue as varied with small jumps, red as tight and rooted with bigger jumps, black as steep with drops. Low granite hills, so this is a forest park rather than an alpine one.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Uplift is by shuttle rather than a lift: an 8-seat van runs every 15 minutes, 09:30-12:30 and 13:30-17:00. A full day with shuttle is 35 EUR, a half day 25 EUR, and a group day 30 EUR per rider from 5 people. The 12 EUR enduro pass gives access without the shuttle, for riders pedalling their own laps. Enduro and downhill bikes rent for 50 EUR a half day and 65 EUR a day, park access not included.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open all year, every weekend.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00<br/><small>Season, hours and prices from the operator's own pages; weekday sessions and courses are by arrangement, so book before travelling.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Limoges</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Gueret</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.bikepark-limousin.com/en-GB/">Bike Park Limousin</a>. Coordinates from the operator's address at La Ferme des Vignes; altitudes measured on the elevation model. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>1.459680,45.999850,470</coordinates></Point>
