  <Placemark>
    <name>Le Mont-Dore (Sancy, Puy-de-Dome) [30 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Le Mont-Dore 1059 m - valley station of the Capucin funicular</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The historic gravity hill of the Massif Central, and a different animal from neighbouring Super-Besse: the descents here are marked forest and volcanic-ridge routes rather than a shaped park. Four circuits drop from the Salon du Capucin at 1233 m, reached by the funicular: Le Capucin (green, 3 km), the Descente du Rigolet (blue, 9.2 km), Les Rigolets (red, 16.3 km) and La Sancy Ouest (black, 35 km), all part of the 51-route Espace Sancy VTT-FFC. The Sancy cable car climbs from 1335 m to 1760 m below the summit, and bikes are allowed on it for one line only - the GR4E down the ski-run corridor, over 500 m of rocky descent, signed for experienced riders and best ridden early in the day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Capucin funicular, France's oldest, carries bikes: 30 EUR a day and 20 EUR a half day for a rider with a bike. The Sancy cable car is a separate ticket 3 km up the valley. Super-Besse, 12 km away over the massif, holds the shaped bike park and is a separate spot on this map.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Funicular daily 4 July to 30 August 2026, then Tuesday to Sunday 1 to 27 September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:40 (September: 10:00-12:10 and 14:00-17:40)<br/><small>Dates, hours and the VTT tariff from the operator's own listing; the cable-car bike rules are the Sancy tourist office's.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Clermont-Ferrand</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Le Mont-Dore station</td><td>Train + walk</td><td>~10 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.sancy.com/voir-faire/activites-pleine-nature/vtt/le-vtt-de-descente/">Sancy tourist office</a>. Lift endpoints and altitudes from OpenStreetMap and the elevation model. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
