  <Placemark>
    <name>Le Mont-Dore: Sancy cable car (valley)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sancy cable car valley station 1335 m, at the ski area 3 km up the valley from the town. Bikes are carried for the GR4E descent only.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>2.814250,45.541630,1335</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">mont-dore</mwm:value></mwm:properties></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Le Mont-Dore: Sancy cable car (top)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Top of the Sancy cable car at 1760 m, below the 1885 m summit. The GR4E drops from here down the ski-run corridor - over 500 m of rocky descent, for experienced riders.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>2.813160,45.532530,1760</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app"><mwm:properties><mwm:value key="spot">mont-dore</mwm:value></mwm:properties></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Chalmazel Bike Park (Monts du Forez, Loire) [21 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Chalmazel 1114 m - valley station of the Jasseries chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The only lift-served gravity park in the Monts du Forez, on the Loire side of Pierre-sur-Haute: 6 gravity runs - 1 green, 1 blue, 3 red and 1 black - for about 27 km of downhill and enduro in total, the longest line running 17.5 km. The green is a 700 m banked run off the Campanules drag lift, deliberately gentle for a first day on a downhill bike; the flagship red is fast and jumpy with technical sections. Wooded, north-facing and often damp - a rooty park rather than a dusty one.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Jasseries chairlift climbs from 1114 m to 1456 m and carries bikes; the Campanules drag lift serves the beginner run. A bike-park day is around 21 EUR, and a gravity bike with protection rents for about 25 EUR. <b>Lift operation in summer varies from year to year</b> - the station asks riders to phone 04 77 96 08 69 and check which lift is turning before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer season from the Ascension weekend to mid-September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:30<br/><small>Season from the station; hours estimated. Prices and trail counts from the KelBikePark listing - confirm with the station.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saint-Etienne</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Lyon</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.chalmazel-ete.fr/">Station de Chalmazel</a> and <a href="https://www.kelbikepark.fr/fr/bikeparks/chalmazel">KelBikePark</a>. Lift endpoints and altitudes from OpenStreetMap and the elevation model. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>3.826900,45.676870,1114</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://comaps.app">
      <mwm:properties>
        <mwm:value key="spot">chalmazel</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="tags">beginner intermediate expert bike-park dh enduro chairlift t-bar</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="open_from">05-14</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="closed_from">09-15</mwm:value>
        <mwm:value key="price_day">21 EUR</mwm:value>
