  <Placemark>
    <name>Monts d'Arree (Finistere, Bretagne) [no-lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Roc'h Trevezel 344 m - the roadside car park under the ridge, on the D785</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Brittany's mountains, and the best-known natural riding in the west of France: a bare quartzite ridge of heather and gorse running above the Armorique regional park, with the region's high point (Roc'h Ruz, 385 m) on it. The riding is short, rocky and technical rather than long - climb the ridge by road or by wide track, then link the singletrack down through the tors and the beech woods, 100 to 200 m of drop at a time. OpenStreetMap holds a real network here, graded up to mtb:scale 3 around Saint-Rivoal, Brennilis and Bodenna, plus marked route=mtb loops. In September the massif hosts the Roc'h des Monts d'Arree, one of the biggest mass-start rides in France at around 6000 riders.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no shuttle - pedal it. Free access on public land and marked trails; the ridge itself is a protected heath, so stay on the paths.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round. Atlantic weather: the peat and the heather hold water, and the massif is genuinely wet in winter - the rock is greasy and the low sections churn.<br/>Daily opening hours: dawn to dusk<br/><small>Free-access public land; no ticket office. Trail evidence from OpenStreetMap; the ridge is a Natura 2000 heath, so ride what is signed.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Morlaix</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Brest</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.tourismebretagne.com/selon-mes-envies/topitos/ou-pratiquer-le-vtt-en-bretagne/">Tourisme Bretagne</a>. Pin is the Roc'h Trevezel car park (OpenStreetMap way 252462892); altitude from the elevation model. Access and trail status can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-3.910060,48.403830,344</coordinates></Point>
